 <span style="color:#88c0d0"> </span>     54  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 4.3</span>  Cut build time under five minutes              <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>                    <span style="color:#b48ead">+ci</span>
 <span style="color:#88c0d0"> </span>     53  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 4.2</span>  Move nightly backups to object storage         <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>                    <span style="color:#b48ead">+ops</span>
 <span style="color:#88c0d0"> </span>     55  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 4.0</span>  Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint        <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>                      <span style="color:#b48ead">+docs</span>
 <span style="color:#88c0d0"> </span>     57  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">L</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▃</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 2.0</span>  Replace the carousel on the home page          <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>                  <span style="color:#b48ead">+ui</span>
 <span style="color:#88c0d0"> </span>     59  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">L</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▃</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 2.0</span>  Archive last year&#39;s analytics dashboards       <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>
 <span style="color:#88c0d0"> </span>     61  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">-</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 0.4</span>  Sketch ideas for the Q4 offsite                <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">home</span>
 <span style="color:#88c0d0"> </span>     60  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">-</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 0.1</span>  Investigate flaky checkout test                <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>                   <span style="color:#b48ead">+bug +ci</span>






















 <span style="color:#88c0d0">j/k</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6"> move   </span><span style="color:#88c0d0">/</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6"> search   </span><span style="color:#88c0d0">enter</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6"> open   </span><span style="color:#88c0d0">s</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6"> start   </span><span style="color:#88c0d0">g/G</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6"> ends   </span><span style="color:#88c0d0">q</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6"> leave   </span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-config"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-config">config</h3><p>Maps to — (registry + core.capabilities).</p><p>Read and change tasqx settings.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx config &lt;list|get &lt;key&gt;|describe &lt;key&gt;|set &lt;key&gt; &lt;value&gt;|unset &lt;key&gt;|path|store|edit&gt;</code></pre><h4 id="h-cli-config--list">tasqx config list</h4><p>Show every setting with its value, source and default</p><h4 id="h-cli-config--get">tasqx config get</h4><p>Print one setting&#39;s resolved value</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-config--get-key" data-param="&lt;key&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;key&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Setting key, e.g. <code>theme.name</code></dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-config--describe">tasqx config describe</h4><p>Print one setting&#39;s description, units and default (#236.2)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-config--describe-key" data-param="&lt;key&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;key&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Setting key, e.g. <code>daemon.idle_timeout</code></dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-config--set">tasqx config set</h4><p>Set a setting in <code>config.toml</code></p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-config--set-key" data-param="&lt;key&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;key&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Setting key, e.g. <code>theme.name</code></dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-config--set-value" data-param="&lt;value&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;value&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New value</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-config--unset">tasqx config unset</h4><p>Remove a setting so it falls back to its default</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-config--unset-key" data-param="&lt;key&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;key&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Setting key</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-config--path">tasqx config path</h4><p>Print the path of <code>config.toml</code> (it may not exist yet)</p><h4 id="h-cli-config--store">tasqx config store</h4><p>Print which store this command would actually write to</p><h4 id="h-cli-config--edit">tasqx config edit</h4><p>Edit settings on an interactive screen, previewing themes live</p><ul class="notes"><li><code>describe</code> prints a setting&#39;s meaning, unit and default — for <code>daemon.idle_timeout</code> the number <code>get</code>/<code>list</code> show is minutes, and the unit is otherwise only visible in the daemon&#39;s own startup banner.</li><li><code>store</code> answers which store you are actually writing to — and says so when a running daemon owns it, because the remote path never consults $TASQX_DB, so a correct $TASQX_DB is silently inert whenever a daemon is listening.</li><li><code>list</code> shows both homes. Most settings live in <code>config.toml</code>; <code>default_project</code> lives in the store and is set with <code>tasqx use</code> (D21).</li><li>Resolution order is <code>--flag</code>, then <code>$TASQX_*</code>, then <code>config.toml</code>, then the built-in default (D9). The SOURCE column names the layer that won.</li><li><code>edit</code> opens an interactive screen: up/down to move, enter to toggle a switch or open a theme picker, esc to leave. Moving through the theme list repaints the screen in that theme before anything is written.</li><li><code>edit</code> needs a real terminal. Piped or redirected it refuses and exits 2 rather than writing escape codes into your pipe — scripts should use <code>set</code>/<code>unset</code> (D26).</li><li><code>tokens.enabled</code> allows the daemon to attribute AI token usage from local tool transcripts; <code>otlp.enabled</code> (+ <code>otlp.port</code>) runs a local OTLP/HTTP receiver instead — see <code>tasqx manual reports</code> and <code>tasqx manual daemon</code>. Both require a running daemon; self-reported counts (<code>token.add</code>) work with both off.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-use"><code>use</code></a> · <a href="#cli-theme"><code>theme</code></a> · <a href="#cli-manual"><code>manual</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx config get theme.name</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx config describe daemon.idle_timeout</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx config path</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx config store</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx config set theme.name gruvbox</code></pre></div><p class="muted">writes config.toml, preserving your comments</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx config edit</code></pre></div><p class="muted">full-screen editor; arrow through themes and watch them apply</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx config list</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#8a8a8a">SETTING              VALUE                                 SOURCE</span>
theme.name           nord                                  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
dashboard.enabled    true                                  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
dashboard.panels     tasks,projects,burndown,pulse,effort  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">config.toml</span>
dashboard.refresh    auto                                  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
dashboard.window     week                                  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
notify.enabled       false                                 <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
tokens.enabled       false                                 <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
otlp.enabled         false                                 <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
otlp.port            4318                                  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
daemon.idle_timeout  0                                     <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
completion.hint      true                                  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
default_project      website                               <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">store</span>
detail.time_format   both                                  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">default</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-docs"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-docs">docs</h3><p>Maps to — (no store).</p><p>Open the exhaustive browser guide (self-contained HTML).</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx docs [--out PATH | --no-open | --stdout] [--screen NAME]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-docs-out" data-param="--out"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--out</code><span class="badge">&lt;path&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Write the guide to this path instead of a temp file. Implies --no-open: naming an output file is asking for the file, not for a browser</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-docs-no-open" data-param="--no-open"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--no-open</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Write the file but never launch a browser. Prints the path instead</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-docs-stdout" data-param="--stdout"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--stdout</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Write the HTML to stdout instead of a file (pipe it anywhere)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-docs-screen" data-param="--screen"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--screen</code><span class="badge">&lt;name&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Write ONE captured screen as a standalone page — the terminal styling of the guide, nothing else — to --out, or to stdout. An unknown name exits 2 listing the screens there are</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>The exhaustive browser guide (self-contained HTML). For a quick in-terminal guide, <code>tasqx manual</code>.</li><li><code>--screen NAME</code> writes ONE captured screen instead of the guide: a standalone page carrying the guide&#39;s terminal styling and nothing else, to <code>--out</code> or to stdout. It is the rasterisation path behind the README&#39;s pictures (<code>scripts/snap.sh</code>), and an unknown name exits 2 listing every screen there is.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-manual"><code>manual</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx docs</code></pre></div><p class="muted">open the browser guide</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx docs --stdout</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx docs --screen list</code></pre></div><p class="muted">one captured screen, standalone</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: its output is this page — either the whole HTML document or the temporary path it was written to. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-about"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-about">about</h3><p>Maps to — (no store).</p><p>Who made tasqx, where to find it, and what build this is.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx about</code></pre><p>Takes no arguments of its own; the global flags still apply.</p><ul class="notes"><li>Six lines: the author, two links, the build this binary was made from, the store it would open, and <code>times UTC</code> — every clock tasqx reads and prints is UTC, including one typed without an offset (D132). The build is the string <code>tasqx --version</code> prints — the crate version plus the commit — and reads <code>unknown</code> on a build from a source tarball, which has no git to ask.</li><li>It opens no store and no network. The store line is the path a command WOULD open, resolved without creating anything, so asking where things live never authors a data directory.</li><li>A credits screen is not data, so there is no API method and <code>--json</code> is declined with a note (D31&#39;s carve-out list, D127).</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-manual"><code>manual</code></a> · <a href="#cli-docs"><code>docs</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx about</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it prints this machine&#39;s store path and the commit this binary was built from. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-manual"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-manual">manual</h3><p>Also <code>man</code>. Maps to — (no store).</p><p>Browse the complete guide in your terminal.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx manual [&lt;command|topic&gt;]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-manual-topic" data-param="&lt;topic&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;topic&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">A command (e.g. <code>init</code>), an alias, or a topic slug (e.g. <code>filters</code>)</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>No store, no network. <code>tasqx docs</code> is the fuller browser guide.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-docs"><code>docs</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx manual init</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx manual filters</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx manual</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0;font-weight:700">TASQX MANUAL</span>

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">TOPICS</span>
  getting-started  Getting started
  projects         Projects
  capturing        Capturing tasks
  dates            Dates &amp; recurrence
  filters          Filter grammar
  screens          Screens &amp; browsing
  reminders        Reminders
  reports          Reports &amp; charts
  daemon           Daemon &amp; watch
  automation       Automation (MCP &amp; API)
  json-api         JSON API
  completion       Shell completion

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">COMMANDS</span>
  init         Create a project — just a name, no folder.
  add          Capture a task — title plus inline sugar.
  modify       Change a task — set fields or --clear them.
  list         List tasks matching a filter.
  agenda       What is coming up, when — `list` ordered by time.
  next         The one highest-urgency unblocked task.
  dashboard    Open the overview screen, or ask for its panels as data.
  pick         Browse tasks on a full-screen list: read one, search them, start one.
  show         Show one task in full detail.
  why          Explain a task&#39;s urgency score.
  start        Mark a task active.
  stop         Pause an active task.
  adjust       Correct a task&#39;s tracked time.
  done         Complete a task.
  cancel       Cancel a task.
  reopen       Reopen a completed or cancelled task.
  undo         Take back the last thing this store recorded.
  annotate     Attach a timestamped note to a task.
  unannotate   Permanently scrub one annotation&#39;s text, by id.
  tag          Attach tags to a task.
  untag        Remove tags from a task.
  dep          Make one task depend on another.
  undep        Remove a dependency edge.
  use          Set the default project for bare adds.
  archive      Retire a project — out of rotation, tasks untouched.
  projects     List projects (default marked with `*`).
  check        Acceptance criteria on a task: add, mark, drop.
  brief        Everything needed before starting a task, in one read.
  report       Summary counts, or outcomes, optionally grouped, as text or HTML.
  chart        Render throughput, heatmap, or burndown charts.
  theme        List or preview terminal themes.
  config       Read and change tasqx settings.
  memory       Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).
  tokens       Record token spend after the fact, or repair stored attribution (D50, D167).
  export       Dump tasks as canonical JSON.
  import       Load tasks from a JSON file or stdin.
  api          One JSON envelope in on stdin → one out on stdout.
  daemon       Long-lived single-writer server.
  watch        Live-updating task view.
  mcp          Serve MCP over stdio with an operator-selected scope.
  docs         Open the exhaustive browser guide (self-contained HTML).
  about        Who made tasqx, where to find it, and what build this is.
  manual       Browse the complete guide in your terminal.
  completions  Turn on Tab completion for your shell.
  setup        Install the Claude Code integration: the MCP server and the bundled skills.

▸ Jump to a topic or command:  tasqx manual &lt;name&gt;
▸ Full browser guide:          tasqx docs

</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-projects">Projects</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-init"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-init">init</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-project.create"><code>project.create</code></a>.</p><p>Create a project — just a name, no folder.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx init &lt;name&gt; [--desc &lt;text&gt;]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-init-name" data-param="&lt;name&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;name&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Project name, e.g. work.tasqx</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-init-desc" data-param="--desc"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--desc</code><span class="badge">&lt;desc&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional description</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>A project is just a name in the store — no folder is created.</li><li>init claims the default project only if the store has none yet.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-use"><code>use</code></a> · <a href="#cli-add"><code>add</code></a> · <a href="#cli-projects"><code>projects</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx init keuken-verbouwen</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx init work --desc &quot;Day job&quot;</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx init home &amp;&amp; tasqx use home</code></pre></div><p class="muted">claim then set default</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx init research</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="font-weight:700">research</span>
<span style="font-weight:700">created</span>   default stays <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">tasqx use &quot;research&quot;</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-use"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-use">use</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-project.use"><code>project.use</code></a>.</p><p>Set the default project for bare adds.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx use &lt;name&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-use-project" data-param="&lt;project&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;project&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">An existing, non-archived project name</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>The project must already exist and not be archived. <code>tasqx projects</code> marks the default with <code>*</code>.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-init"><code>init</code></a> · <a href="#cli-projects"><code>projects</code></a> · <a href="#cli-add"><code>add</code></a> · <a href="#cli-archive"><code>archive</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx use keuken-verbouwen</code></pre></div><p class="muted">move where a bare add lands</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx use api</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="font-weight:700">api</span>
<span style="font-weight:700">now the default</span>   was <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">a bare tasqx add lands here</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-archive"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-archive">archive</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-project.archive"><code>project.archive</code></a>.</p><p>Retire a project — out of rotation, tasks untouched.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx archive &lt;name&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-archive-project" data-param="&lt;project&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;project&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">An existing project name</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Archiving is a shelf, not a delete: the tasks keep their history and their project, and <code>tasqx projects --all</code> still lists the project.</li><li>An archived project is out of rotation for WRITES — <code>use</code> refuses it (exit 5), and so does an <code>add</code>/<code>modify</code> that names it, and so does a second <code>archive</code> of it (<code>project is already archived</code>, exit 5). No write may name an archived project, this one included; <code>store.import</code> restoring the flag from a document is the one write that still can. Reads are unaffected: <code>list</code>, <code>report</code> and <code>agenda</code> still show it and its tasks — archiving is a rotation change, not a hide.</li><li>There is no <code>unarchive</code> verb and no <code>project.unarchive</code> method: among the project methods, archiving is one-way. <code>store.import</code> does write a project&#39;s <code>archived</code> flag from the document, so restoring a saved export un-archives one — a data restore, not an undo.</li><li>Archiving the project that IS the default clears the default: a bare <code>tasqx add</code> then has no project until <code>tasqx use &lt;project&gt;</code>. The line says which of the two happened.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-projects"><code>projects</code></a> · <a href="#cli-use"><code>use</code></a> · <a href="#cli-init"><code>init</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx archive keuken-verbouwen</code></pre></div><p class="muted">retire it; archiving your default project clears the default</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx archive home</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="font-weight:700">home</span>
<span style="font-weight:700">archived</span>   <span style="color:#ebcb8b">2 open tasks left in it</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">default unchanged</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">tasqx list project:home</span>
</pre></div><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx archive home</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>error [conflict]: project is already archived: home (`tasqx projects --all` lists it; archiving it again would change nothing)</code></pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-projects"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-projects">projects</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a>.</p><p>List projects (default marked with `*`).</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx projects [--all]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-projects-all" data-param="--all"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--all</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Include archived projects</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li><code>--all</code> is the only way to see an archived project: without it the table shows the live ones, which is what <code>add</code> and <code>use</code> will accept.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-init"><code>init</code></a> · <a href="#cli-use"><code>use</code></a> · <a href="#cli-archive"><code>archive</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx projects --all</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx projects</code></pre><pre class="term">  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">PROJECT  DESCRIPTION</span>
  <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>      Public REST API and its SDKs
  <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">home</span>
  <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>    CI, deploys and on-call
  <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>   iOS and Android apps
<span style="color:#88c0d0">*</span> <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>  Marketing site and docs portal
</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-capturing">Capturing tasks</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-add">add</h3><p>Also <code>a</code>, <code>new</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.add"><code>task.add</code></a>.</p><p>Capture a task — title plus inline sugar.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx add &lt;title…&gt; [--project p] [--due d] [--scheduled s] [--wait w] [-p H|M|L] [-t tag]… [--repeat r] [--remind r] [-e est] [--budget-tokens n]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-add-title" data-param="&lt;title…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;title…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task title (may carry inline sugar)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-project" data-param="--project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--project</code><span class="badge">&lt;project&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">File the task under an existing project (see <code>tasqx projects</code>)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-p-priority" data-param="-p, --priority"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">-p, --priority</code><span class="badge">H|M|L</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Priority: H, M, or L (or high/medium/low)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-due" data-param="--due"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--due</code><span class="badge">&lt;due&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Due date — natural language ok (e.g. friday, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, eom, -1d)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-scheduled" data-param="--scheduled"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--scheduled</code><span class="badge">&lt;scheduled&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Scheduled date — natural language ok</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-wait" data-param="--wait"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--wait</code><span class="badge">&lt;wait&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Wait-until date — natural language ok (task stays in backlog)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-repeat" data-param="--repeat"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--repeat</code><span class="badge">&lt;repeat&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Recurrence rule, e.g. &quot;every 3 days&quot; or &quot;weekly on mon,wed,fri&quot;</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-remind" data-param="--remind"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--remind</code><span class="badge">&lt;remind&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Reminder: a due-anchored offset (-1h, -30m, -2d) or an absolute date (&quot;friday 9am&quot;). Without this, the task never notifies (§9)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-e-estimate" data-param="-e, --estimate"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">-e, --estimate</code><span class="badge">&lt;estimate&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Effort estimate — human duration (4h, 90m, 1h30m, 2d) or ISO PT4H</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-budget-tokens" data-param="--budget-tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--budget-tokens</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Token budget — a size gauge over FRESH tokens (input + output + cache creation; cache reads are not counted). It stops nothing: tasqx is a store an agent calls between turns and cannot preempt one. An overrun is a signal that the task was probably too big to hand over whole</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-add-t-tag" data-param="-t, --tag"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">-t, --tag</code><span class="badge">&lt;tag…&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Repeatable tag flag</dd></div></dl><p>Anywhere a command takes a <code>&lt;ref&gt;</code>, it accepts either the short id you see in the table (<code>1</code>) or the full UUID. Short ids are for your fingers; UUIDs are stable forever and are what <a href="#data">export</a> carries.</p><p>Flags win over inline sugar when both name the same field. The sugar column is bound to the parser's own key table, so a spelling here is a spelling that parses:</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-24-h0">Flag</th><th id="tbl-24-h1">Sugar</th><th id="tbl-24-h2">Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--project &lt;p&gt;</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>project:</code>, <code>proj:</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2">Free-form dotted name.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--priority &lt;p&gt;</code> / <code>-p</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>!high</code>, <code>!h</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2"><code>H</code>, <code>M</code>, <code>L</code> (or high/medium/low).</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--tag &lt;t&gt;</code> / <code>-t</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>+tag</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2">Repeatable.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--due &lt;d&gt;</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>due:</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2"><a href="#scheduling">Natural language</a>.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--scheduled &lt;d&gt;</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>scheduled:</code>, <code>sched:</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2">When you plan to start.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--wait &lt;d&gt;</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>wait:</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2">Hide in the backlog until then.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--repeat &lt;r&gt;</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>repeat:</code>, <code>every:</code>, <code>recur:</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2"><a href="#scheduling">Recurrence rule</a>.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--remind &lt;r&gt;</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>remind:</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2"><a href="#reminders">Offset or absolute</a>.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Flag" headers="tbl-24-h0"><code>--estimate &lt;e&gt;</code> / <code>-e</code></td><td data-label="Sugar" headers="tbl-24-h1"><code>est:</code>, <code>estimate:</code></td><td data-label="Notes" headers="tbl-24-h2"><code>4h</code>, <code>90m</code>, <code>1h30m</code>, <code>2d</code>, or ISO <code>PT4H</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul class="notes"><li>Inline sugar: <code>+tag</code>, <code>project:p</code> (or <code>proj:</code>), <code>!high</code>, <code>due:…</code>, <code>scheduled:…</code> (or <code>sched:</code>), <code>wait:…</code>, <code>repeat:…</code> (or <code>every:</code>/<code>recur:</code>), <code>remind:…</code>, <code>est:4h</code> (or <code>estimate:</code>).</li><li>A bare add lands in the default project (<code>tasqx use</code> to change it).</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-modify"><code>modify</code></a> · <a href="#cli-use"><code>use</code></a> · <a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a> · <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx add Buy milk</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx add Ship it due:friday +api !high --project work</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx add Water plants repeat:&quot;every 3 days&quot;</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx add Call bank due:&quot;friday 9am&quot; --remind -30m</code></pre></div><p class="muted">reminder 30m before due</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx add &quot;Draft the Q4 roadmap&quot; project:website !H due:friday +planning</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#62</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Draft the Q4 roadmap</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">added</span>   <span style="color:#bf616a">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">16.6</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span> Fri   <span style="color:#b48ead">+planning</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-modify"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-modify">modify</h3><p>Also <code>mod</code>, <code>m</code>, <code>edit</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.modify"><code>task.modify</code></a>.</p><p>Change a task — set fields or --clear them.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx modify &lt;ref&gt; [words/sugar…] [--project p] [--due d] [--scheduled s] [--wait w] [-p H|M|L] [-t tag]… [--repeat r] [--remind r] [-e est] [--tracked t] [--budget-tokens n] [--clear &lt;field&gt;]… [--expected-rev N]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-modify-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-rest" data-param="&lt;rest…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;rest…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New title words and/or inline sugar (due:friday, +tag, project:p, !high, est:4h, repeat:&quot;every week&quot;, remind:-1h). Bare words become the new title; omit them to leave the title alone</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-project" data-param="--project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--project</code><span class="badge">&lt;project&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Move the task to an existing project (see <code>tasqx projects</code>)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-p-priority" data-param="-p, --priority"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">-p, --priority</code><span class="badge">H|M|L</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Priority: H, M, or L (or high/medium/low)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-due" data-param="--due"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--due</code><span class="badge">&lt;due&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Due date — natural language ok (friday, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, eom, -1d)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-scheduled" data-param="--scheduled"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--scheduled</code><span class="badge">&lt;scheduled&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Scheduled date — natural language ok</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-wait" data-param="--wait"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--wait</code><span class="badge">&lt;wait&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Wait-until date — natural language ok</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-repeat" data-param="--repeat"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--repeat</code><span class="badge">&lt;repeat&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Recurrence rule, e.g. &quot;every 3 days&quot; or &quot;weekly on mon,wed,fri&quot;. Clear it with <code>--clear recurrence</code></dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-remind" data-param="--remind"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--remind</code><span class="badge">&lt;remind&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Reminder: a due-anchored offset (-1h, -30m) or an absolute date</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-e-estimate" data-param="-e, --estimate"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">-e, --estimate</code><span class="badge">&lt;estimate&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Effort estimate — human duration (4h, 90m, 1h30m, 2d) or ISO PT4H</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-tracked" data-param="--tracked"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--tracked</code><span class="badge">&lt;tracked&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Correct the tracked-time total — human duration (4h, 90m, 1h30m, 2d) or ISO PT4H. Overwrites the stored total outright rather than adding to it; clear it back to zero with <code>--clear tracked</code></dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-budget-tokens" data-param="--budget-tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--budget-tokens</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Token budget — a size gauge over FRESH tokens (input + output + cache creation; cache reads are not counted). It stops nothing: tasqx is a store an agent calls between turns and cannot preempt one. An overrun is a signal that the task was probably too big to hand over whole</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-t-tag" data-param="-t, --tag"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">-t, --tag</code><span class="badge">&lt;tag…&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Add a tag (repeatable). Routed to tag.add</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-clear" data-param="--clear"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--clear</code><span class="badge">&lt;field…&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Clear a field back to unset (repeatable). The only removal syntax for a steering field; a tag comes off with <code>tasqx untag &lt;ref&gt; &lt;tag&gt;</code></dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-modify-expected-rev" data-param="--expected-rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--expected-rev</code><span class="badge">&lt;rev&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optimistic concurrency: fail with <code>conflict</code> (exit 5) unless the task is still at this rev, so a concurrent edit is reported instead of clobbered. <code>tasqx show &lt;ref&gt; --json</code> reports the current <code>_rev</code>, and every successful modify prints the new one</dd></div></dl><p><code>--clear</code> is repeatable over a closed set:</p><pre class="plain"><code>project   priority   due   scheduled   wait   remind   recurrence   estimate   tracked   budget_tokens</code></pre><p><code>title</code> and <code>status</code> are absent on purpose: a task without a title is not a task, and lifecycle moves through <code>start</code>/<code>done</code>/<code>cancel</code> so their invariants hold. Naming a field in both a set and a <code>--clear</code> is a <code>bad_request</code>, not a precedence puzzle.</p><ul class="notes"><li>Setting is <code>due:friday</code>/<code>--due friday</code>; removal is only ever <code>--clear &lt;field&gt;</code> — there is no magic empty value.</li><li><code>--clear</code> covers the steering fields only. <code>modify 42 +api</code> adds a tag; taking one off is <code>tasqx untag 42 api</code>.</li><li><code>--expected-rev</code> fails with conflict (exit 5) if the task moved on.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-add"><code>add</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a> · <a href="#cli-untag"><code>untag</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx modify 42 due:friday !high est:4h</code></pre></div><p class="muted">set fields</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx modify 42 --clear due --clear remind</code></pre></div><p class="muted">clear fields</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx modify 42 repeat:&quot;every monday&quot;</code></pre></div><p class="muted">set a recurrence</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx modify 55 due:friday !high</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#55</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">modified</span>   <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">16.7</span>   <span style="font-weight:700">due Fri</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>   <span style="color:#b48ead">+docs</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 4h   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">rev 2</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-show"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-show">show</h3><p>Also <code>get</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>.</p><p>Show one task in full detail.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx show &lt;ref&gt; [--card [--ascii]]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-show-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-show-card" data-param="--card"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--card</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Print the task as a 72-column box-drawn card, for pasting into a document</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-show-ascii" data-param="--ascii"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--ascii</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">With --card: draw the borders with + - | instead of box-drawing characters</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Full detail: tags, annotations, dependencies, blocked state, <code>_rev</code>.</li><li><code>--card</code> prints a fixed 72-column box-drawn card meant to be pasted into a document (a chat, a PR); <code>--ascii</code> draws its borders with <code>+ - |</code>. The default screen is unchanged (D146).</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-modify"><code>modify</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a> · <a href="#cli-annotate"><code>annotate</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx show 1</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx show 1 --card</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx show 51</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#51</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">⊘ blocked</span><span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700"> by #50 · Rate-limit the /search endpoint</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">status</span>      pending           <span style="color:#8a8a8a">urgency</span>     <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">12.2</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">project</span>     api               <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span>         <span style="font-weight:700">Mon (in 5 days)</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">estimate</span>    5h                <span style="color:#8a8a8a">tags</span>        +docs
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">created</span>     16 Aug (31 days ago)
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">modified</span>    16 Aug (31 days ago)
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">rev</span>         1
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> [x] Every renamed symbol has a row in the table
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> [x] One worked example per SDK (js, py, go)
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">[ ]</span> The rate-limit ceiling is stated with its real number
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">[ ]</span> Reviewed by whoever ships 3.0
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">·</span> Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release, not after it. A migration note that lands a week
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>   late is a support ticket that already happened.
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">·</span> Blocked until the rate limit lands: the guide has to state the real ceiling, and quoting a
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>   number that then changes is worse than waiting.
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">·</span> Scope: the 2.x → 3.0 rename table, the auth change, and a worked example per SDK. Not the
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>   reference — that generates itself.
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-start"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-start">start</h3><p>Also <code>s</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.start"><code>task.start</code></a>.</p><p>Mark a task active.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx start &lt;ref&gt; [--keep] [--client TOOL] [--session-id ID] [--transcript-path PATH]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-start-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-start-keep" data-param="--keep"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--keep</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Keep other active tasks running (opt out of single-active)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-start-client" data-param="--client"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--client</code><span class="badge">&lt;tool&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Calling tool as &quot;&lt;name&gt; &lt;version&gt;&quot;, e.g. &quot;claude-code 2.1&quot;. Selects the transcript parser; without it no transcript is ever read</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-start-session-id" data-param="--session-id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--session-id</code><span class="badge">&lt;id&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Agent session id, verified against the transcript to earn high confidence. Requires --client</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-start-transcript-path" data-param="--transcript-path"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--transcript-path</code><span class="badge">&lt;path&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Absolute path to the session transcript the tokens will be found in. Requires --client</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>The correlation flags are for AI agents: they tell the attribution engine which session and transcript to measure this interval from. Without them a task is never attributed and reports zero tokens.</li><li>--session-id and --transcript-path require --client, which is what selects the transcript parser. Given without it, attribution would store a permanent zero instead of a measurement.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-stop"><code>stop</code></a> · <a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a> · <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx start 1</code></pre></div><p class="muted">single-active by default</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx start 1 --keep</code></pre></div><p class="muted">keep others running</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx start 1 --client &#39;claude-code 2.1&#39; --session-id $SID</code></pre></div><p class="muted">record who is working, for token attribution</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx start 49</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#a3be8c">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#49</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Fix token refresh race on Android</span>
<span style="color:#a3be8c">▶</span> <span style="font-weight:700">started</span>   <span style="color:#bf616a">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">17.0</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span> tomorrow 17:00   <span style="color:#b48ead">+bug</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 4h
  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#48</span>  <span style="color:#a3be8c">stopped</span> · <span style="color:#8a8a8a">Ship the v2 pricing page</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-stop"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-stop">stop</h3><p>Also <code>st</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.stop"><code>task.stop</code></a>.</p><p>Pause an active task.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx stop &lt;ref&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-stop-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div></dl><p>See also <a href="#cli-start"><code>start</code></a> · <a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a> · <a href="#cli-adjust"><code>adjust</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx stop 1</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx stop 48</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#48</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Ship the v2 pricing page</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#a3be8c;font-weight:700">stopped</span>   <span style="color:#bf616a">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">17.8</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span> today 17:00   <span style="color:#b48ead">+launch</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 6h
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-adjust"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-adjust">adjust</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-task.adjust_tracked"><code>task.adjust_tracked</code></a>.</p><p>Correct a task&#39;s tracked time.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx adjust &lt;ref&gt; &lt;delta&gt; --reason TEXT</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-adjust-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-adjust-delta" data-param="&lt;delta&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;delta&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Signed duration: -2h25m takes time off, +30m (or 30m) adds it</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-adjust-reason" data-param="--reason"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--reason</code><span class="badge">&lt;reason&gt;</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Why the time is being corrected (required; kept in the event log)</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Works on any task, done included, so calibration in <code>report --outcomes</code> can be corrected after the fact. A correction that would take the banked total below zero is refused.</li><li>Each correction is its own event with its reason, and <code>tasqx undo</code> takes the newest one back. <code>show</code> prints the net of every correction beside the total: <code>tracked 2h30m (adjusted -2h25m)</code>.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-stop"><code>stop</code></a> · <a href="#cli-undo"><code>undo</code></a> · <a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx adjust 1 -2h25m --reason &#39;idle gap&#39;</code></pre></div><p class="muted">take off time the clock ran while nobody worked</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx adjust 1 +30m --reason &#39;forgot to start&#39;</code></pre></div><p class="muted">add time that never reached the clock</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx adjust 42 -2h25m --reason &quot;idle gap&quot;</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#42</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Paginate the audit log</span>
<span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">adjusted -2h25</span>   <span style="font-weight:700">tracked 6h25 of 4h</span>   <span style="color:#bf616a">H</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">6.2</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-done"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-done">done</h3><p>Also <code>d</code>, <code>x</code>, <code>complete</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a>.</p><p>Complete a task.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx done &lt;ref&gt; [--force] [--client TOOL] [--session-id ID] [--transcript-path PATH] [--tool TOOL] [--model MODEL] [--input-tokens N] [--output-tokens N] [--cache-read-tokens N] [--cache-creation-tokens N] [--total-tokens N]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-done-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-force" data-param="--force"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--force</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Complete the task even though some of its dependencies are still open (recorded; <code>report --outcomes</code> counts it under FORCED)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-client" data-param="--client"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--client</code><span class="badge">&lt;tool&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Calling tool as &quot;&lt;name&gt; &lt;version&gt;&quot;, e.g. &quot;claude-code 2.1&quot;. Selects the transcript parser; without it no transcript is ever read</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-session-id" data-param="--session-id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--session-id</code><span class="badge">&lt;id&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Agent session id, verified against the transcript to earn high confidence. Requires --client</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-transcript-path" data-param="--transcript-path"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--transcript-path</code><span class="badge">&lt;path&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Absolute path to the session transcript the tokens will be found in. Requires --client</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-tool" data-param="--tool"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--tool</code><span class="badge">&lt;tool&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The AI tool doing the work, free-form (e.g. &quot;claude-code&quot;). Recorded on the completion event on its own; when token counts are present it also names the measurement, defaulting to --client if omitted</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-model" data-param="--model"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--model</code><span class="badge">&lt;model&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model doing the work, e.g. &quot;claude-opus-5&quot;. Recorded on the completion event on its own, and carried on the measurement when token counts are present</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-input-tokens" data-param="--input-tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--input-tokens</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported input tokens this task cost (0 or more)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-output-tokens" data-param="--output-tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--output-tokens</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported output tokens this task cost (0 or more)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-cache-read-tokens" data-param="--cache-read-tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--cache-read-tokens</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported cache-read tokens this task cost (0 or more)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-cache-creation-tokens" data-param="--cache-creation-tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--cache-creation-tokens</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported cache-creation tokens this task cost (0 or more)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-done-total-tokens" data-param="--total-tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--total-tokens</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit token count, for a harness that reports only a total — instead of the four counts above, never beside them (D167)</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>A task whose dependencies are still open is refused, naming them. --force completes it anyway; the override lands on the done event and <code>tasqx report --outcomes</code> counts it under FORCED (D150). Cancelling a blocked task needs no flag.</li><li>The correlation flags carry the same meaning as on <code>start</code>, and are recorded per occurrence: a task can start and finish many times, and attribution pairs the two events of one interval.</li><li>--tool/--model and the four *-tokens flags are the self-report channel (D50/D65): any present token count records a measurement, attributed to --tool (or --client if --tool is omitted). --tool/--model alone, with no count, still land on the completion event. Skip all of them and the response carries a tokens_hint explaining what was not recorded — printed under the Done line.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-cancel"><code>cancel</code></a> · <a href="#cli-reopen"><code>reopen</code></a> · <a href="#cli-start"><code>start</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx done 1</code></pre></div><p class="muted">completes; spawns the next recurrence if any</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx done 1 --force</code></pre></div><p class="muted">complete it although a dependency is still open; the override is recorded</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx done 1 --client &#39;claude-code 2.1&#39; --session-id $SID</code></pre></div><p class="muted">close the interval an agent opened with the same ids</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx done 1 --tool claude-code --model claude-opus-5 --input-tokens 4200 --output-tokens 900</code></pre></div><p class="muted">self-report the turn&#39;s spend — the primary measurement channel (D50)</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx done 47</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#47</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Renew the TLS certificate for api.example.dev</span>
<span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">done today</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span> 2d ago   <span style="color:#b48ead">+ops</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 1h
note: no token counts were self-reported — tasqx done --help names the flags
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-cancel"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-cancel">cancel</h3><p>Also <code>delete</code>, <code>del</code>, <code>rm</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.cancel"><code>task.cancel</code></a>.</p><p>Cancel a task.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx cancel &lt;ref&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-cancel-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>There is no destructive delete. <code>delete</code>/<code>rm</code> are aliases for cancel: the task keeps its history, stays in the event log, and <code>tasqx reopen &lt;ref&gt;</code> undoes it.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a> · <a href="#cli-reopen"><code>reopen</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx cancel 1</code></pre></div><p class="muted">a cancelled dependency releases its dependents (D11)</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx delete 1</code></pre></div><p class="muted">same thing — tasqx has no hard delete; reverse it with <code>reopen</code></p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx cancel 59</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#59</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Archive last year&#39;s analytics dashboards</span>
<span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">cancelled</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 1h
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-reopen"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-reopen">reopen</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-task.reopen"><code>task.reopen</code></a>.</p><p>Reopen a completed or cancelled task.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx reopen &lt;ref&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-reopen-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div></dl><p>See also <a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a> · <a href="#cli-cancel"><code>cancel</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx reopen 1</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx reopen 46</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#46</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Tune the autoscaler</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">reopened</span>   <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">4.2</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 2h
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-undo"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-undo">undo</h3><p>Also <code>u</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-event.revert"><code>event.revert</code></a>.</p><p>Take back the last thing this store recorded.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx undo</code></pre><p>Takes no arguments of its own; the global flags still apply.</p><ul class="notes"><li>It takes no ref, and that is the design: only the NEWEST event can be reversed exactly, because nothing has happened since to have read or overwritten what the inverse puts back.</li><li>Six operations are undoable — <code>stop</code>, <code>untag</code>, <code>undep</code>, <code>annotate</code>, <code>annotate --edit</code> and <code>adjust</code>. Every other one exits 5 naming itself and the verb that does take it back (<code>done</code> -&gt; <code>tasqx reopen</code>, <code>modify</code> -&gt; <code>tasqx show</code> then a second <code>modify</code>).</li><li>Undo APPENDS: the event it reverses stays in the log and a new <code>undo</code> event lands behind it, so <code>tasqx chart</code> and the audit trail read <code>X happened, then it was undone</code>.</li><li>There is no redo, so <code>tasqx undo</code> twice in a row exits 5: the second one would find the first undo as the newest event and the pair would toggle forever.</li><li>It reverses the newest RECORDED event, which is not always the last command you typed. A command that changed nothing records nothing — <code>tasqx undep 1 2</code> where no such edge exists, or <code>tasqx start</code> on a task already running — so <code>undo</code> reaches past it to the previous change. That is why the answer names what it undid: read it before assuming it hit what you were aiming at.</li><li>A single event outside the undoable five permanently blocks undo for everything BEFORE it, not just for itself: the newest event on an active store is almost always <code>add</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>modify</code>, and once one of those lands, an annotation from ten seconds earlier can never be reached (#228.2). This is a same-breath affordance — undo the thing you just did — not an undo stack.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-untag"><code>untag</code></a> · <a href="#cli-undep"><code>undep</code></a> · <a href="#cli-reopen"><code>reopen</code></a> · <a href="#cli-chart"><code>chart</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx undo</code></pre></div><p class="muted">reverses the newest event, and says which one</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx untag 42 api &amp;&amp; tasqx undo</code></pre></div><p class="muted">the tag comes back off the shelf</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it reverses the newest event, so a capture would have to record two commands and the manifest records one. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-annotate"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-annotate">annotate</h3><p>Also <code>note</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-annotation.add"><code>annotation.add</code></a> + <a href="#api-annotation.update"><code>annotation.update</code></a>.</p><p>Attach a timestamped note to a task.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx annotate &lt;ref&gt; [--edit &lt;annotation-id&gt;] &lt;text…&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-annotate-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-annotate-text" data-param="&lt;text…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;text…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The annotation text</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-annotate-edit" data-param="--edit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--edit</code><span class="badge">&lt;annotation_id&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Replace the body of this annotation instead of adding one; its id, timestamp and position are kept</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Wrote something you shouldn&#39;t have? <code>tasqx unannotate &lt;ref&gt; &lt;annotation-id&gt;</code> scrubs it — there is no other way back.</li><li>Wrote something wrong? <code>--edit &lt;annotation-id&gt;</code> replaces that note&#39;s text in place (D165): its id, timestamp and position stay, so a corrected first note is still the card&#39;s Description, and <code>tasqx undo</code> puts the old text back.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-modify"><code>modify</code></a> · <a href="#cli-unannotate"><code>unannotate</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx annotate 1 Called the plumber, waiting on a quote</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx annotate 50 &quot;Ship it behind a flag; the ceiling is 60 requests a minute per key.&quot;</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#50</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Rate-limit the /search endpoint</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">annotated</span>   Ship it behind a flag; the ceiling is 60 requests a minute per key.
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-unannotate"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-unannotate">unannotate</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a>.</p><p>Permanently scrub one annotation&#39;s text, by id.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx unannotate &lt;ref&gt; &lt;annotation-id&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-unannotate-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-unannotate-annotation-id" data-param="&lt;annotation_id&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;annotation_id&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The annotation&#39;s id, as <code>tasqx show &lt;ref&gt;</code> reports it</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>A HARD delete (D113): the text is overwritten in the store, not merely hidden — use it to take back a secret, a customer name, or a wrong root cause pasted into a note by mistake. This also redacts the original <code>annotate</code> event&#39;s own body, so <code>tasqx chart</code> (<code>event.list</code>) and <code>tasqx export</code> stop showing it too — not only <code>tasqx show</code>.</li><li>The annotation&#39;s id is not printed by <code>tasqx show</code> — read it from <code>tasqx show &lt;ref&gt; --json</code> (the <code>annotations[].id</code> field) or a prior <code>tasqx annotate</code> response.</li><li><code>tasqx undo</code> does NOT cover this: the body is already gone from the log by the time the removal event exists, so there is nothing left to restore.</li><li>An unknown id, or one already removed, exits 4 (not_found) rather than answering ok for nothing.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-annotate"><code>annotate</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-undo"><code>undo</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx unannotate 1 018f2f7e-...</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it takes the id of one annotation, which is a UUID out of the store it is run against. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-tag"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-tag">tag</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-tag.add"><code>tag.add</code></a>.</p><p>Attach tags to a task.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx tag &lt;ref&gt; &lt;tag…&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-tag-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tag-tag" data-param="&lt;tag…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;tag…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tag names, with or without the leading <code>+</code></dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>A tag is written the same way here as in <code>add</code>/<code>modify</code> sugar: <code>+api</code> and <code>api</code> name one tag, and duplicates collapse.</li><li>Re-adding a tag the task already has is not an error — the answer is the resulting tag set, so nothing has to be guessed.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-untag"><code>untag</code></a> · <a href="#cli-modify"><code>modify</code></a> · <a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tag 1 api release</code></pre></div><p class="muted">two tags, one call</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tag 1 +api</code></pre></div><p class="muted">the leading + is optional — same tag either way</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx tag 55 openapi sdk</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#55</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">tagged</span>   <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">+docs</span> <span style="color:#b48ead;font-weight:700">+openapi</span> <span style="color:#b48ead;font-weight:700">+sdk</span>   <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">4.0</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 4h
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-untag"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-untag">untag</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-tag.remove"><code>tag.remove</code></a>.</p><p>Remove tags from a task.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx untag &lt;ref&gt; &lt;tag…&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-untag-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-untag-tag" data-param="&lt;tag…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;tag…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tag names, with or without the leading <code>+</code></dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Removing a tag the task does not have exits 4 and removes nothing, naming the tags it does have. A typo may not answer ok.</li><li>There is no <code>--clear tags</code>: a tag comes off by name, which is why this verb exists.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-tag"><code>tag</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx untag 1 api</code></pre></div><p class="muted">removes it, and prints what remains</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx untag 1 api release</code></pre></div><p class="muted">all or nothing: one unknown tag removes neither</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx untag 55 docs</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#55</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">untagged</span>   <span style="color:#b48ead;font-weight:700">+docs</span>   <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">4.0</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 4h
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-dep"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-dep">dep</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-dependency.add"><code>dependency.add</code></a>.</p><p>Make one task depend on another.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx dep &lt;ref&gt; &lt;depends_on&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-dep-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The dependent task (short_id or UUID)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-dep-depends-on" data-param="&lt;depends_on&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;depends_on&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task it depends on (short_id or UUID)</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li><code>&lt;ref&gt;</code> becomes blocked until <code>&lt;depends_on&gt;</code> is done or cancelled; a <code>&lt;ref&gt;</code> that is itself already closed is never blocked.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-undep"><code>undep</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx dep 2 1</code></pre></div><p class="muted">task 2 waits on task 1</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx dep 52 49</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#bf616a">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#52</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Dark mode for the settings screen</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a">⊘</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">blocked by #49</span> · <span style="color:#8a8a8a">Fix token refresh race on Android</span>   <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄▃</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">8.6</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span> 25 Sep   <span style="color:#b48ead">+ui</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-undep"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-undep">undep</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-dependency.remove"><code>dependency.remove</code></a>.</p><p>Remove a dependency edge.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx undep &lt;ref&gt; &lt;depends_on&gt;</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-undep-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The dependent task (short_id or UUID)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-undep-depends-on" data-param="&lt;depends_on&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;depends_on&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task it depended on (short_id or UUID)</dd></div></dl><p>See also <a href="#cli-dep"><code>dep</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx undep 2 1</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx undep 51 50</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#51</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="font-weight:700">no longer waits on #50</span>   <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a">12.2</span>   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span> Mon   <span style="color:#b48ead">+docs</span>   <span style="color:#8a8a8a">est</span> 5h
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-check"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-check">check</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-check.add"><code>check.add</code></a> + <a href="#api-check.set"><code>check.set</code></a> + <a href="#api-check.remove"><code>check.remove</code></a>.</p><p>Acceptance criteria on a task: add, mark, drop.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx check &lt;add &lt;ref&gt; &lt;criterion…&gt;|set &lt;ref&gt; &lt;check_id|position&gt; &lt;state&gt; [--evidence e]|remove &lt;ref&gt; &lt;check_id|position&gt;&gt;</code></pre><h4 id="h-cli-check--add">tasqx check add</h4><p>Add an acceptance criterion to a task</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-check--add-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-check--add-body" data-param="&lt;body…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;body…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion, in your own words</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-check--set">tasqx check set</h4><p>Mark a criterion passed or failed, with the evidence for it</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-check--set-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-check--set-check-id" data-param="&lt;check_id&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;check_id&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The check&#39;s id, from <code>tasqx show</code> — or its 1-based position there</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-check--set-state" data-param="&lt;state&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;state&gt;</code><span class="badge">open|passed|failed</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">open | passed | failed</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-check--set-evidence" data-param="--evidence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--evidence</code><span class="badge">&lt;evidence&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your proof: a test name, an excerpt of output, a commit sha</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-check--remove">tasqx check remove</h4><p>Also <code>rm</code>.</p><p>Drop a criterion that was the wrong thing to ask</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-check--remove-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-check--remove-check-id" data-param="&lt;check_id&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;check_id&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The check&#39;s id — or its 1-based position in <code>tasqx show</code></dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>tasqx NEVER RUNS a check. The criterion is a claim and the evidence is a citation; both are stored verbatim and neither is interpreted. A hook you installed is what runs commands, calling <code>check set</code> like any other client.</li><li>Completing with a criterion still open is not refused — nothing is blocked — but <code>tasqx report --outcomes</code> counts it as an unproven completion.</li><li><code>failed</code> is a normal outcome. Use <code>rm</code> only when the criterion was the wrong thing to ask; removing one the work failed hides the finding.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx check add 1 the notes name every breaking change</code></pre></div><p class="muted">add a criterion</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx check set 1 019f-abc passed --evidence &quot;suite green&quot;</code></pre></div><p class="muted">mark it</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx check rm 1 019f-abc</code></pre></div><p class="muted">drop a criterion</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx check set 1 2 failed</code></pre></div><p class="muted">the second criterion, by position</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx check add 50 &quot;p99 stays under 200ms at the new ceiling&quot;</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#50</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Rate-limit the /search endpoint</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">status</span>      pending           <span style="color:#8a8a8a">urgency</span>     <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">15.9</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">project</span>     api               <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span>         <span style="font-weight:700">Sat (in 3 days)</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">estimate</span>    3h                <span style="color:#8a8a8a">tags</span>        +perf
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">blocks</span>      #51               <span style="color:#8a8a8a">created</span>     31 Aug (16 days ago)
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">modified</span>    today 09:00 UTC (just now)
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">rev</span>         2
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">▌</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">[ ]</span> p99 stays under 200ms at the new ceiling
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-brief"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-brief">brief</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a>.</p><p>Everything needed before starting a task, in one read.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx brief &lt;ref&gt; [--memory-limit N] [--card [--ascii]]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-brief-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-brief-memory-limit" data-param="--memory-limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--memory-limit</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many memory hits to show</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-brief-card" data-param="--card"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--card</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Print the task as a 72-column box-drawn card, for pasting into a document</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-brief-ascii" data-param="--ascii"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--ascii</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">With --card: draw the borders with + - | instead of box-drawing characters</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>The task, what each of its prerequisites concluded, what it blocks, and memory found under a query tasqx derives from the task&#39;s own title, tags and project — so nobody has to guess search terms.</li><li>Half the memory page (rounded up) is reserved for knowledge docs, so a ruling is never buried under a sibling task&#39;s own notes; annotations fill whatever slots docs leave (D147).</li><li>Memory is scoped to the task&#39;s project and does not widen when that finds nothing: <code>tasqx memory search</code> is the wider read.</li><li><code>--card</code> prints a fixed 72-column box-drawn card meant to be pasted into a document (a chat, a PR); <code>--ascii</code> draws its borders with <code>+ - |</code>. The default screen is unchanged (D146).</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a> · <a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx brief 1</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx brief 1 --memory-limit 3</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx brief 1 --card</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx brief 51</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">#51</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">⊘ blocked</span><span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700"> by #50 · Rate-limit the /search endpoint</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">status</span>      pending           <span style="color:#8a8a8a">urgency</span>     <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">12.2</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">project</span>     api               <span style="color:#8a8a8a">due</span>         <span style="font-weight:700">Mon (in 5 days)</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">estimate</span>    5h                <span style="color:#8a8a8a">tags</span>        +docs
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">created</span>     16 Aug (31 days ago)
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">modified</span>    16 Aug (31 days ago)
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">rev</span>         1
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> [x] Every renamed symbol has a row in the table
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> [x] One worked example per SDK (js, py, go)
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">[ ]</span> The rate-limit ceiling is stated with its real number
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">[ ]</span> Reviewed by whoever ships 3.0
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">·</span> Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release, not after it. A migration note that lands a week
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>   late is a support ticket that already happened.
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">·</span> Blocked until the rate limit lands: the guide has to state the real ceiling, and quoting a
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>   number that then changes is worse than waiting.
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">·</span> Scope: the 2.x → 3.0 rename table, the auth change, and a worked example per SDK. Not the
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▌</span>   reference — that generates itself.

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">DEPENDS ON</span>
  <span style="color:#88c0d0">#50</span>  Rate-limit the /search endpoint  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">pending</span>

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">FROM MEMORY</span>
  release-process  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">docs/release.md</span>  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">[api]</span>
    <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">description How an SDK release is cut, tagged and announced Cut the…</span>
</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-dates">Dates &amp; recurrence</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-agenda"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-agenda">agenda</h3><p>Also <code>ag</code>, <code>cal</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a>.</p><p>What is coming up, when — `list` ordered by time.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx agenda [filter…] [--days N]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-agenda-filter" data-param="&lt;filter…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;filter…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL, e.g. &quot;project:work +api&quot; (default: the working set)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-agenda-days" data-param="--days"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--days</code><span class="badge">&lt;days&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many days ahead to look (1-3650; default 14). Overdue tasks are shown regardless</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>A task is placed on the EARLIER of its <code>due</code> and <code>scheduled</code> — the first day it asks anything of you — and the WHEN column says which of the two that was.</li><li>Overdue tasks are always shown, whatever <code>--days</code> says: a horizon is a question about the future.</li><li>This view holds a row back for exactly two reasons, and both are COUNTED under the table rather than dropped in silence: no date at all, and past the horizon. Each count names the way to see them — the horizon line quotes the exact <code>--days</code> that reaches the furthest one, or, when the row is further out than the widest window <code>--days</code> accepts, says so and points at <code>tasqx list</code>.</li><li>Done and cancelled tasks are left out unless your filter names a status, the same rule <code>report</code> applies to cancelled tasks (D24). <code>tasqx agenda status:done</code> shows them.</li><li>Days are UTC days, because a date typed without a time is stored as midnight UTC; grouping by local time would file <code>--due 2026-08-05</code> under the 4th west of Greenwich.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a> · <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a> · <a href="#cli-add"><code>add</code></a> · <a href="#cli-modify"><code>modify</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx agenda --days 3</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx agenda project:work</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx agenda</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">through 30 Sep (+14d)</span>   <span style="font-weight:700">8 tasks</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">·</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">1 overdue</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">·</span> <span style="color:#a3be8c">#48 running</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">·</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">1 blocked</span>

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">    ID          URG  TASK                                           PROJECT  WHEN        TAGS</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">Overdue</span>
    47  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">18.1</span>  Renew the TLS certificate for api.example.dev  <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>    <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">due 2d ago</span>  <span style="color:#b48ead">+ops</span>

<span style="color:#88c0d0">Today · Wed 16 Sep</span>
<span style="color:#a3be8c">▶</span>   48  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">17.8</span>  Ship the v2 pricing page                       <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>  due 17:00   <span style="color:#b48ead">+launch</span>

<span style="color:#88c0d0">Tomorrow · Thu 17 Sep</span>
    49  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">17.0</span>  Fix token refresh race on Android              <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>   due 17:00   <span style="color:#b48ead">+bug</span>

<span style="color:#88c0d0">Sat 19 Sep</span>
    50  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">15.9</span>  Rate-limit the /search endpoint                <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>                  <span style="color:#b48ead">+perf</span>

<span style="color:#88c0d0">Mon 21 Sep</span>
<span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">⊘</span>   51  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">12.2</span>  Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0          <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>                  <span style="color:#b48ead">+docs</span>

<span style="color:#88c0d0">Tue 22 Sep</span>
    58  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">L</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄▄</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b"> 9.4</span>  Book the dentist                               <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">home</span>                 

<span style="color:#88c0d0">Fri 25 Sep</span>
    52  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄▃</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b"> 8.6</span>  Dark mode for the settings screen              <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>               <span style="color:#b48ead">+ui</span>

<span style="color:#88c0d0">Mon 28 Sep</span>
    56  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b"> 6.0</span>  Accessibility pass on the signup flow          <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>              <span style="color:#b48ead">+a11y</span>

<span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">7 undated — no due or scheduled date, so nothing puts them on a day; `tasqx list` shows them</span>
</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-filters">Filter grammar</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-list"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-list">list</h3><p>Also <code>ls</code>, <code>l</code>. Maps to <a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a>.</p><p>List tasks matching a filter.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx list [filter…] [--sort key]… [--limit N] [--offset N] [--fields f,…]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-list-filter" data-param="&lt;filter…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;filter…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL, e.g. &quot;project:work status:pending +api&quot;</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-list-sort" data-param="--sort"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--sort</code><span class="badge">&lt;sort…&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Sort key(s), e.g. <code>due</code> or <code>-due</code> for descending (repeatable, or comma-separated). Maps straight onto <code>task.list</code>&#39;s own <code>sort</code> param — see <code>tasqx docs</code> for the valid names. Default: <code>-urgency</code>, unchanged from before this flag existed</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-list-limit" data-param="--limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--limit</code><span class="badge">&lt;limit&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cap the number of rows returned. Maps to <code>task.list</code>&#39;s <code>limit</code>. Defaults to 100 when omitted, and is clamped to 10,000 even when given explicitly</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-list-offset" data-param="--offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--offset</code><span class="badge">&lt;offset&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Skip this many matching rows before <code>--limit</code> is applied. Maps to <code>task.list</code>&#39;s <code>offset</code></dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-list-fields" data-param="--fields"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--fields</code><span class="badge">&lt;fields…&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Return only these task fields (repeatable, or comma-separated) — see <code>tasqx docs</code> for the valid names. Maps to <code>task.list</code>&#39;s <code>fields</code>; an unknown name is refused by the engine, same as above</dd></div></dl><p>Callers of the JSON API — and <code>--sort</code> here — may use any of <code>urgency</code>, <code>short_id</code>, <code>priority</code>, <code>due</code>, <code>created</code>, <code>modified</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>tokens</code>, <code>estimate</code>, <code>tracked</code>, each optionally prefixed with <code>-</code> for descending. An unknown key is rejected rather than ignored.</p><p><code>--fields</code> trims each row to the keys you need. The valid fields are <code>_rev</code>, <code>active_since</code>, <code>blocked</code>, <code>budget_tokens</code>, <code>completed</code>, <code>created</code>, <code>depends_on</code>, <code>due</code>, <code>estimate</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>modified</code>, <code>priority</code>, <code>project</code>, <code>recurrence</code>, <code>remind</code>, <code>scheduled</code>, <code>short_id</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>status_unrecognized</code>, <code>tags</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>tokens</code>, <code>tracked</code>, <code>tracked_adjustment</code>, <code>urgency</code>, <code>wait</code>. An unknown field is rejected rather than dropped, so a typo fails loudly instead of rendering an empty column forever.</p><ul class="notes"><li>Bare <code>tasqx</code> is <code>tasqx list</code> over the working set.</li><li>A value containing a space is double-quoted, and the quotes must reach tasqx: <code>tasqx list &#39;project:&quot;Home Renovation&quot;&#39;</code>. Nothing is guessed back together, so the shell-stripped form is refused rather than answered wrongly.</li><li><code>--sort</code>, <code>--limit</code>, <code>--offset</code> and <code>--fields</code> map straight onto <code>task.list</code>&#39;s own params (<code>core.capabilities</code> names all five) — <code>tasqx list --sort due --limit 20 --fields short_id,title,due</code>. An unknown sort key or field name is refused, naming the valid set.</li><li>The piped table (no TTY) is a fixed 100 cells wide; on a terminal it sizes to <code>$COLUMNS</code> (clamped 40–160) or the terminal&#39;s own width, whichever it can read. Widen a truncated title with <code>COLUMNS=200 tasqx list</code> or narrow the row with <code>--fields</code>.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a> · <a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx list project:work status:pending +api</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx list due.before:friday</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx list</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">@working</span>   <span style="font-weight:700">14 tasks</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">·</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">1 overdue</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">·</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">1 due today</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">·</span> <span style="color:#a3be8c">#48 running</span>

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">    ID          URG  TASK                                          PROJECT  DUE             TAGS</span>
    47  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">18.1</span>  Renew the TLS certificate for api.example.d…  <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>    <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">2d ago</span>          <span style="color:#b48ead">+ops</span>
<span style="color:#a3be8c">▶</span>   48  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">17.8</span>  Ship the v2 pricing page                      <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>  today 17:00     <span style="color:#b48ead">+launch</span>
    49  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">17.0</span>  Fix token refresh race on Android             <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>   tomorrow 17:00  <span style="color:#b48ead">+bug</span>
    50  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">H</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">▄▄▄▄</span> <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">15.9</span>  Rate-limit the /search endpoint               <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>      Sat             <span style="color:#b48ead">+perf</span>
    58  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">L</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄▄</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b"> 9.4</span>  Book the dentist                              <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">home</span>     Tue             
    52  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄▃</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b"> 8.6</span>  Dark mode for the settings screen             <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>   25 Sep          <span style="color:#b48ead">+ui</span>
    56  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b">▄▄</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#ebcb8b"> 6.0</span>  Accessibility pass on the signup flow         <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>  28 Sep          <span style="color:#b48ead">+a11y</span>
    54  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 4.3</span>  Cut build time under five minutes             <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>                    <span style="color:#b48ead">+ci</span>
    53  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 4.2</span>  Move nightly backups to object storage        <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>                    <span style="color:#b48ead">+ops</span>
    55  <span style="color:#ebcb8b">M</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▄▂</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 4.0</span>  Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint       <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>                      <span style="color:#b48ead">+docs</span>
    57  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">L</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▃</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 2.0</span>  Replace the carousel on the home page         <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>                  <span style="color:#b48ead">+ui</span>
    59  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">L</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a">▃</span><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 2.0</span>  Archive last year&#39;s analytics dashboards      <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>                  
    61  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">-</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 0.4</span>  Sketch ideas for the Q4 offsite               <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">home</span>                     
    60  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">-</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">▁▁▁▁</span> <span style="color:#8a8a8a"> 0.1</span>  Investigate flaky checkout test               <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>                   <span style="color:#b48ead">+bug +ci</span>
</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-reports">Reports &amp; charts</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-why"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-why">why</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>.</p><p>Explain a task&#39;s urgency score.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx why &lt;ref&gt; [--card [--ascii]]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-why-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-why-card" data-param="--card"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--card</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Print the task as a 72-column box-drawn card, for pasting into a document</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-why-ascii" data-param="--ascii"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--ascii</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">With --card: draw the borders with + - | instead of box-drawing characters</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Explains the urgency score component by component (DESIGN D1).</li><li><code>--card</code> prints the fixed 72-column box-drawn card (D146) first, with the arithmetic underneath instead of the plain text header; <code>--ascii</code> draws the card&#39;s borders with <code>+ - |</code>.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx why 1</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx why 1 --card</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx why 51</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#8a8a8a">#51</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0</span>

  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">priority  </span> M           3.9
  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">deadline  </span> due Mon     8.0
  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">age       </span> 30 days     0.3
  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">urgency   </span>          <span style="font-weight:700">  12.2</span>
  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">blocked by</span> #50 Rate-limit the /search endpoint — `next` skips this task
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-report"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-report">report</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-report.summary"><code>report.summary</code></a> + <a href="#api-report.outcomes"><code>report.outcomes</code></a>.</p><p>Summary counts, or outcomes, optionally grouped, as text or HTML.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx report [group_by] [filter…] [--all] [--outcomes] [--since WHEN] [--until WHEN] [--metrics list] [--html] [--out FILE]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-report-args" data-param="&lt;args…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;args…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional group_by (project|status|priority) then optional filter DSL</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-report-html" data-param="--html"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--html</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Emit a single self-contained HTML report (inline CSS + SVG, no external requests) instead of the terminal table</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-report-out" data-param="--out"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--out</code><span class="badge">&lt;path&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Write the HTML report to this file (default: stdout). Requires --html</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-report-all" data-param="--all"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--all</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Count cancelled tasks too. By default a report excludes cancelled tasks, unless the filter itself names a status (DESIGN D24)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-report-since" data-param="--since"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--since</code><span class="badge">&lt;when&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Window <code>tracked_total</code>/the token buckets to work done or spend measured at or after this instant, instead of each task&#39;s lifetime total — same date grammar as <code>--due</code> (D97)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-report-until" data-param="--until"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--until</code><span class="badge">&lt;when&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The other end of <code>--since</code>&#39;s window: excludes anything at or after this instant</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-report-metrics" data-param="--metrics"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--metrics</code><span class="badge">&lt;metrics…&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Show the four token buckets (cache read/write, in, out) as their own columns instead of the single largest-bucket cell (#212, D48a) — comma-separated, from the same vocabulary <code>report.summary</code>&#39;s <code>metrics</code> param accepts. Naming a non-token metric here is accepted but has no effect: COUNT/EST/OVERDUE/ TRACKED already always show, and this flag only changes the TOKENS display</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-report-outcomes" data-param="--outcomes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--outcomes</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Report outcomes instead of counts (D137): rework, estimate calibration, cost, silent completions and abandoned work, over the tasks that CLOSED</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>group_by ∈ project|status|priority. <code>--html</code> defaults to stdout.</li><li>A filter scopes BOTH output modes — the HTML page and the terminal table answer the same question.</li><li>Cancelled tasks are not counted, unless you pass <code>--all</code> or your filter names a status.</li><li>The terminal&#39;s TOKENS column names the largest of four buckets by volume; <code>--metrics</code> naming a tokens_* bucket shows all four as their own columns instead, same as <code>--html</code> and <code>--json</code>.</li><li><code>--since</code>/<code>--until</code> window <code>tracked_total</code> and the token buckets by WHEN the time or spend happened (D97) — a different axis from <code>completed.after:</code>/<code>completed.before:</code> in the filter, which selects tasks by completion date. Rejected alongside <code>--html</code>, which has no windowed path yet.</li><li>--socket is refused with <code>--html</code> (DESIGN.md D73): the HTML page renders from a direct local read of the store, never through a daemon.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-chart"><code>chart</code></a> · <a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report project</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report --all</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report --metrics tokens_in,tokens_out,tokens_cache_read,tokens_cache_creation</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report --since -7d</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report --outcomes</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report --outcomes project --since -30d</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report --html --out review.html</code></pre></div><p class="muted">self-contained HTML</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report +urgent --html --out sprint.html</code></pre></div><p class="muted">scoped HTML</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx report</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#8a8a8a">PROJECT  COUNT  EST  OVERDUE  TRACKED                TOKENS</span>
<span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>          9  16h        <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">0</span>   4h 15m   cacheR 7.0M ~medium
<span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">home</span>         2    -        <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">0</span>        -                     -
<span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>       11  15h        <span style="color:#ebcb8b">1</span>   5h 10m   cacheR 2.8M ~medium
<span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>      16  18h        <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">0</span>   9h 50m   cacheR 7.7M ~medium
<span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>     17  38h        <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">0</span>  36h 25m   cacheR 2.4M ~medium

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">TOTAL</span>       55  87h        <span style="color:#ebcb8b">1</span>  55h 40m  cacheR 20.1M ~medium

<span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">TOKENS shows the largest of four buckets (cacheR/cacheW/in/out) by volume; --metrics</span>
<span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">tokens_in,tokens_out,tokens_cache_read,tokens_cache_creation or --html shows all four.</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-chart"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-chart">chart</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-event.list"><code>event.list</code></a>.</p><p>Render throughput, heatmap, or burndown charts.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx chart &lt;throughput|heatmap|burndown&gt; [filter…] [--weeks n|--days n] [--year] [--project p]</code></pre><h4 id="h-cli-chart--throughput">tasqx chart throughput</h4><p>Tasks added vs done per ISO week (from the events table)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-chart--throughput-filter" data-param="&lt;filter…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;filter…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL, e.g. &quot;project:work&quot; (default: the whole store). Same grammar <code>list</code>/<code>report</code>/<code>agenda</code> take (#663/D173): only the scoped tasks&#39; events move a bar</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-chart--throughput-weeks" data-param="--weeks"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--weeks</code><span class="badge">&lt;weeks&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Number of weeks to show (1-520; default 12)</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-chart--heatmap">tasqx chart heatmap</h4><p>GitHub-style completion density per day (from done events)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-chart--heatmap-filter" data-param="&lt;filter…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;filter…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL — see <code>throughput</code>&#39;s</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-chart--heatmap-year" data-param="--year"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--year</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Show a full year (52 weeks)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-chart--heatmap-weeks" data-param="--weeks"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--weeks</code><span class="badge">&lt;weeks&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Number of weeks to show (1-520; default 12; overrides --year)</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-chart--burndown">tasqx chart burndown</h4><p>Remaining open tasks over the last N days (reconstructed backwards from each task&#39;s current status, not read forwards off the events table — D59/D60)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-chart--burndown-filter" data-param="&lt;filter…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;filter…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL, e.g. &quot;project:work&quot; (default: the whole store) — see <code>throughput</code>&#39;s</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-chart--burndown-project" data-param="--project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--project</code><span class="badge">&lt;project&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Restrict to a project (else all tasks). Shorthand for appending <code>project:&lt;name&gt;</code> (quoted) to <code>filter</code> above — kept for scripts and docs already spelling it this way; <code>project:work</code> on the positional says the same thing and composes with a second predicate the flag alone cannot (<code>chart burndown project:work +urgent</code>)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-chart--burndown-days" data-param="--days"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--days</code><span class="badge">&lt;days&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Number of days to show (1-3650; default 30)</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>--socket is refused here rather than honoured (DESIGN.md D73): charts render from a direct local read of the store, never through a daemon.</li><li>Each subcommand takes the same filter DSL <code>list</code>/<code>report</code>/<code>agenda</code> do (DESIGN.md D173), e.g. <code>tasqx chart burndown project:work</code> — only that project&#39;s tasks and events count. Omit it for the whole store, the same default as before.</li><li><code>--project work</code> is shorthand for the <code>project:work</code> filter term above, kept for scripts already spelling it that way. The filter term is the more general form — it composes with a second predicate, which <code>--project</code> alone cannot.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx chart throughput</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx chart heatmap --year</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx chart burndown --days 30</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx chart burndown project:work</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx chart burndown</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#88c0d0;font-weight:700">remaining open · all tasks</span>   <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">15 left · up 3 over 30 days</span>

  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">18</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">┤</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">                                                           ╭───────────╮                  </span>
  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">  </span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">│</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">                   ╭───────────────────────╮      ╭────────╯           ╰──────────────────</span>
  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">  </span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">│</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">──────────╮     ╭──╯                       ╰──────╯                                       </span>
  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">  </span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">│</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">    </span><span style="color:#8a8a8a;opacity:.6">······</span><span style="color:#88c0d0">╰─────╯</span><span style="color:#8a8a8a;opacity:.6">······</span><span style="color:#88c0d0">                                                                   </span>
  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">  </span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">│</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">                       </span><span style="color:#8a8a8a;opacity:.6">···················</span><span style="color:#88c0d0">                                                </span>
  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">  </span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">│</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">                                          </span><span style="color:#8a8a8a;opacity:.6">···················</span><span style="color:#88c0d0">                             </span>
  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">  </span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">│</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">                                                             </span><span style="color:#8a8a8a;opacity:.6">···················</span><span style="color:#88c0d0">          </span>
  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6"> 0</span> <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">┤</span> <span style="color:#88c0d0">                                                                                </span><span style="color:#8a8a8a;opacity:.6">··········</span>
     <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
     <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">18 Aug                                                                               16 Sep</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-theme"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-theme">theme</h3><p>Maps to — (no store).</p><p>List or preview terminal themes.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx theme &lt;list|show [name]|set &lt;name&gt;&gt;</code></pre><h4 id="h-cli-theme--list">tasqx theme list</h4><p>List available themes (built-ins + user files)</p><h4 id="h-cli-theme--show">tasqx theme show</h4><p>Preview a theme&#39;s roles (default: the active theme)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-theme--show-name" data-param="&lt;name&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;name&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Theme name to preview</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-theme--set">tasqx theme set</h4><p>Persist a theme choice to <code>config.toml</code></p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-theme--set-name" data-param="&lt;name&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;name&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Theme name: a built-in or a user file in the themes directory</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li><code>theme list</code> marks the theme in effect with <code>*</code>, the mark <code>tasqx projects</code> puts on the default project.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a> · <a href="#cli-manual"><code>manual</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx theme show nord</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx theme list</code></pre><pre class="term">  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">THEME</span>
<span style="color:#88c0d0">*</span> nord
  gruvbox
  dracula
  solarized
  mono
</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-daemon">Daemon &amp; watch</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-daemon"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-daemon">daemon</h3><p>Maps to (serves all).</p><p>Long-lived single-writer server.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx daemon [--db PATH]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-daemon-db" data-param="--db"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--db</code><span class="badge">&lt;path&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Store path for the daemon&#39;s single Engine (default: $TASQX_DB or the platform data dir). The socket address comes from the global <code>--socket</code> / $TASQX_SOCK / the platform default</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Long-lived single-writer; one-shot commands auto-route through it. Ctrl-C stops it cleanly.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-watch"><code>watch</code></a> · <a href="#cli-api"><code>api</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx daemon</code></pre></div><p class="muted">bind the socket/named pipe and serve</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it binds a socket and serves until it is stopped; there is no last line to capture. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-watch"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-watch">watch</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a> + <code>push</code>.</p><p>Live-updating task view.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx watch [filter…]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-watch-filter" data-param="&lt;filter…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;filter…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL (default: the working set)</dd></div></dl><p>See also <a href="#cli-daemon"><code>daemon</code></a> · <a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx watch project:work</code></pre></div><p class="muted">live view; needs a running daemon</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it redraws until you leave it, and it needs a running daemon to follow. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-automation">Automation (MCP &amp; API)</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-memory"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-memory">memory</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-memory.search"><code>memory.search</code></a> + <code>get/add/remove/list/update</code> + <a href="#api-memory.import"><code>memory.import</code></a> + <a href="#api-memory.refresh"><code>memory.refresh</code></a>.</p><p>Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx memory &lt;add &lt;title&gt; &lt;body&gt; [--source s] [--project p] [--standing]|search &lt;words…&gt; [--limit n] [--scope s] [--raw]|list [--limit n] [--offset n] [--project p] [--standing]|show &lt;id&gt;|update &lt;id&gt; [--title t] [--body b] [--source s] [--project p] [--standing true|false] [--expected-rev n]|rm &lt;id&gt;|import &lt;path&gt; [--project p]|import --refresh&gt;</code></pre><h4 id="h-cli-memory--add">tasqx memory add</h4><p>Store a knowledge doc (maps to memory.add). Body is stored verbatim</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-memory--add-title" data-param="&lt;title&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;title&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Doc title</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--add-body" data-param="&lt;body&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;body&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Body text — multi-line markdown is fine</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--add-source" data-param="--source"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--source</code><span class="badge">&lt;source&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where this came from: a path, URL, or ticket</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--add-project" data-param="--project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--project</code><span class="badge">&lt;project&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional project scope. Omitted, the doc stays global</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--add-standing" data-param="--standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--standing</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Mark the doc standing: a ruling meant for every session of its scope, kept until cleared and sent to MCP clients at session start (D156, D157)</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-memory--list">tasqx memory list</h4><p>Browse docs without a query (maps to memory.list). Newest first</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-memory--list-limit" data-param="--limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--limit</code><span class="badge">&lt;limit&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Max rows to return. Omit for everything from <code>--offset</code> on. Asking for a page prints the table, never the browser</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--list-offset" data-param="--offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--offset</code><span class="badge">&lt;offset&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>0</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many matching docs to skip. Like <code>--limit</code>, prints the table</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--list-project" data-param="--project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--project</code><span class="badge">&lt;project&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Restrict to docs stored with this project</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--list-standing" data-param="--standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--standing</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only standing docs. Like <code>--limit</code>, prints the table</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-memory--update">tasqx memory update</h4><p>Correct a doc in place (maps to memory.update)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-memory--update-id" data-param="&lt;id&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;id&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc UUID, as printed by <code>memory add</code>/<code>memory search</code>/<code>memory list</code></dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--update-title" data-param="--title"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--title</code><span class="badge">&lt;title&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New title. Omit to leave it unchanged</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--update-body" data-param="--body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--body</code><span class="badge">&lt;body&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New body. Omit to leave it unchanged</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--update-source" data-param="--source"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--source</code><span class="badge">&lt;source&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New source. Omit to leave it unchanged</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--update-project" data-param="--project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--project</code><span class="badge">&lt;project&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New project scope. Omit to leave it unchanged</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--update-standing" data-param="--standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--standing</code><span class="badge">true|false</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Set or clear the standing flag. Omit to leave it unchanged</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--update-expected-rev" data-param="--expected-rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--expected-rev</code><span class="badge">&lt;rev&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optimistic concurrency: fail with <code>conflict</code> (exit 5) unless the doc is still at this rev. Supplied automatically from the doc&#39;s current rev when omitted</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-memory--search">tasqx memory search</h4><p>Search docs + annotations, bm25-ranked (maps to memory.search)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-memory--search-query" data-param="&lt;query…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;query…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Search words. Matched as phrases, so hyphens and dots are safe</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--search-limit" data-param="--limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--limit</code><span class="badge">&lt;limit&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Max hits (default 10)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--search-scope" data-param="--scope"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--scope</code><span class="badge">all|docs|annotations</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What to search (default: all)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--search-raw" data-param="--raw"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--raw</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Treat the query as raw FTS5 syntax (prefix*, AND/OR, columns)</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-memory--show">tasqx memory show</h4><p>Also <code>get</code>.</p><p>Show one doc whole, by id (maps to memory.get)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-memory--show-id" data-param="&lt;id&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;id&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc UUID, as printed by <code>memory add</code> and <code>memory search</code></dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-memory--rm">tasqx memory rm</h4><p>Remove a doc by id (maps to memory.remove)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-memory--rm-id" data-param="&lt;id&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;id&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc UUID, as printed by <code>memory add</code> and <code>memory search</code></dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-memory--import">tasqx memory import</h4><p>Import markdown files as docs: one doc per file (maps to memory.add)</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-memory--import-path" data-param="&lt;path&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;path&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">A file, or a directory whose *.md files are imported (non-recursive)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--import-refresh" data-param="--refresh"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--refresh</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Re-read every already-imported doc whose file changed since, and name the ones whose file is gone (maps to memory.refresh)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-memory--import-project" data-param="--project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--project</code><span class="badge">&lt;project&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Scope every imported doc to this project. Omitted, they stay global, same as <code>memory add</code> with no <code>--project</code>; re-importing the same directory with a different one MOVES the scope (#657)</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>A hit is two lines: the title, where it came from and the handle that opens it, then the words that matched. The handle is a doc&#39;s id, which <code>tasqx memory show &lt;id&gt;</code> reads, or <code>annotation on #N</code>, which <code>tasqx show N</code> opens — <code>memory show</code> refuses an annotation&#39;s id and names the task instead (exit 4).</li><li>Search covers your imported docs AND task annotations, bm25-ranked, with stemming (&quot;reviewing&quot; matches &quot;review&quot;). Plain words are matched as phrases (hyphens and dots are safe); pass --raw for FTS5 operator syntax. The response&#39;s total/has_more say what --limit left out.</li><li>list browses every doc without a query — the enumeration search can&#39;t do without one — newest-modified first, paged the same way as <code>tasqx list</code>.</li><li>update replaces title/body/source/project in place, guarded by the same optimistic-concurrency rev <code>tasqx modify</code> uses. rm is permanent; update is the correction path that keeps the id and doesn&#39;t pollute search with a stale duplicate.</li><li>Import is one transaction: a bad file imports nothing, and re-importing a directory replaces docs from the same source instead of duplicating them. --project scopes the whole batch; omitted, an existing doc keeps whatever scope it already had (like --standing), a new one stays global, and naming a different project on a re-import moves the doc&#39;s scope there.</li><li><code>import --refresh</code> takes no path: it re-reads every doc that recorded an origin file (D180) whose file has changed since, keeping each doc&#39;s id, scope and standing flag and bumping its rev; a file that only got a newer timestamp counts as unchanged, because the bytes are compared. A doc whose file can no longer be read is named and kept, never deleted — the file may be on another machine or an unmounted volume — and the command still exits 0.</li><li>A file&#39;s stored source is its path relative to the git toplevel above it, or, outside a git work tree, relative to the current directory — so docs/, ./docs/ and its absolute path are one document per file from any starting directory or machine (D179); an older spelling already in memory is named in a note rather than removed.</li><li>An MCP agent reaches the same store: tasqx_search_memory works even read-only, so agents can consult knowledge while executing tasks.</li><li>A standing doc (<code>--standing</code>) is a ruling meant for every session of its scope — a correction given once, sent to MCP clients at session start — and <code>list --standing</code> shows them; more than 15 in one scope earns a hint to merge or retract (D156).</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-annotate"><code>annotate</code></a> · <a href="#cli-mcp"><code>mcp</code></a> · <a href="#cli-api"><code>api</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory add &quot;Deploy runbook&quot; &quot;deploys go through the blue-green pipeline&quot;</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory search blue-green</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory search &#39;pipel*&#39; --raw</code></pre></div><p class="muted">FTS5 operator syntax: prefix search, AND/OR, column filters</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory import docs/adr</code></pre></div><p class="muted">one doc per .md file; title from the first # heading</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory import docs/adr --project ledger</code></pre></div><p class="muted">scopes every doc in the batch; a re-import naming a different project moves it (#657)</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory import --refresh</code></pre></div><p class="muted">re-reads every imported doc whose file changed; takes no path</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory update 019f8422-7b3e-7c41-a2d9-6f1b0e5c8a12 --body &quot;corrected text&quot;</code></pre></div><p class="muted">in-place correction; add/remove leave the stale doc searchable or lose it for good</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory rm 019f8422-7b3e-7c41-a2d9-6f1b0e5c8a12</code></pre></div><p class="muted">by the id search printed</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx memory list</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="font-weight:700">5 docs</span>

<span style="color:#8a8a8a">TITLE                   PROJECT  UPDATED  ID</span>
pricing-page-decisions  <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">website</span>  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">2d ago</span>   <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">0787b26d-9e2e-4be5-ab66-ec953102fad3</span>
release-process         <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">api</span>      <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">6d ago</span>   <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e</span>
on-call-handover        <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">infra</span>    <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">3 Sep</span>    <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">1bce1a9b-5134-4ab7-8665-34cd79fe0c5f</span>
android-token-refresh   <span style="color:#81a1c1;opacity:.6">mobile</span>   <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">27 Aug</span>   <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">b3bd4390-2124-42ac-829d-f542ecde8a07</span>
dentist                          <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">13 Aug</span>   <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">091eb5ff-05d5-4cb2-ba2f-0afdc77f7935</span>
</pre></div><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx memory search release canary</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">&quot;release&quot; &quot;canary&quot;</span>   <span style="font-weight:700">1 hit</span>

release-process  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">docs/release.md</span>  <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e</span>
    <span style="color:#4c566a;opacity:.6">…Cut the release branch on Monday, tag after the canary has run…</span>
</pre></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-tokens"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-tokens">tokens</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-tokens.recompute"><code>tokens.recompute</code></a> + <a href="#api-token.add"><code>token.add</code></a>.</p><p>Record token spend after the fact, or repair stored attribution (D50, D167).</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx tokens recompute [--apply] | tasqx tokens add &lt;ref&gt; [--total N] [--in N] [--out N] [--cache-read N] [--cache-creation N] [--tool TOOL] [--model MODEL]</code></pre><h4 id="h-cli-tokens--add">tasqx tokens add</h4><p>Record token spend on a task after the fact (maps to token.add), e.g. a count that arrived after the task was completed. Stored as a self-report at medium confidence (D50, D167). Give --total alone when only one number is known, or the split counts — never both</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-ref" data-param="&lt;ref&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;ref&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">short_id or UUID</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-total" data-param="--total"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--total</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, kept apart from the four buckets (D167)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-in" data-param="--in"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--in</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Input tokens</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-out" data-param="--out"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--out</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-cache-read" data-param="--cache-read"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--cache-read</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cache-read tokens</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-cache-creation" data-param="--cache-creation"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--cache-creation</code><span class="badge">&lt;n&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cache-creation tokens</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-tool" data-param="--tool"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--tool</code><span class="badge">&lt;tool&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>unknown</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The AI tool that spent them, free-form. Default &quot;unknown&quot;</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--add-model" data-param="--model"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--model</code><span class="badge">&lt;model&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work</dd></div></dl><h4 id="h-cli-tokens--recompute">tasqx tokens recompute</h4><p>Re-run log-parse attribution over stored history and locate transcripts for done tasks (maps to tokens.recompute): samples claimed by more than one task&#39;s window drop out, a task whose transcript is gone keeps its counts with confidence downgraded to low, and a done Claude Code task with no measured (log-parse or OTLP) row gets a HIGH measurement if its transcript is found. Dry-run by default: prints the per-task delta and writes nothing</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-tokens--recompute-apply" data-param="--apply"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--apply</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Actually write the repair. The dry-run default is not a convenience but the safety: this is the one verb in the API built to delete measurement rows, so destruction must be asked for by name</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li><code>add</code> records a self-report at confidence <code>medium</code> — what <code>done</code>&#39;s token flags record, for a count that arrives later (D167). <code>--total</code> is one unsplit number, kept apart from the four buckets and counted in full by a budget; give it alone or give the split flags, never both.</li><li>A bare <code>tasqx tokens recompute</code> prints the per-task delta and writes NOTHING; <code>--apply</code> is the explicit opt-in for the one verb in the API built to delete measurement rows.</li><li>The pass runs two phases: rewrite D50-refusal rows (<code>source=log-parse</code> only, self-report/OTLP never touched), and downgrade confidence to <code>low</code> for any task whose transcript is gone; then locate the transcript of every done Claude Code task with no measured (log-parse or OTLP) row and append a HIGH measurement if found. Tasks it cannot measure — no transcript found, or every sample contested — are reported as <code>skipped</code>.</li><li>Stop any daemon on the store before <code>--apply</code>: the verb parses transcripts and runs in-process only (a daemon refuses it over the socket), and applying beside a live daemon is two writers — convergence on rerun is the safety net, not a license.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a> · <a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a> · <a href="#cli-api"><code>api</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tokens add 602 --total 37898</code></pre></div><p class="muted">a count that arrived after completion, as one unsplit number</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tokens add 602 --in 18400 --out 2600 --tool claude-code</code></pre></div><p class="muted">the same, split</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tokens recompute</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tokens recompute --apply</code></pre></div><p class="muted">write the repair, after reviewing the dry-run delta</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: the demo store records no AI token spend, so the dry run has nothing to repair and its whole screen is the one line that says so. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-mcp"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-mcp">mcp</h3><p>Maps to (subset).</p><p>Serve MCP over stdio with an operator-selected scope.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx mcp serve [--scope read|write]</code></pre><h4 id="h-cli-mcp--serve">tasqx mcp serve</h4><p>Run the MCP stdio server: newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin/stdout</p><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-mcp--serve-scope" data-param="--scope"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--scope</code><span class="badge">read|write</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>read</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Operator-selected capability scope for this stdio process</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Scope configures the local process; it is not authentication. Omitted scope is read-only.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-api"><code>api</code></a> · <a href="#cli-daemon"><code>daemon</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx mcp serve</code></pre></div><p class="muted">serve read-only over stdio JSON-RPC</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx mcp serve --scope write</code></pre></div><p class="muted">serve with explicit write access</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it speaks JSON-RPC on stdin and stdout for as long as the agent holds the pipe. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-setup"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-setup">setup</h3><p>Maps to — (no store).</p><p>Install the Claude Code integration: the MCP server and the bundled skills.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx setup [--list | --yes [--force]] [--only NAME]... [--home DIR]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-setup-list" data-param="--list"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--list</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Print each item and its status, then exit</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-setup-yes" data-param="--yes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--yes</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Install every item that is not installed, without the screen</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-setup-force" data-param="--force"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--force</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">With --yes, also replace a skill file that differs from the bundled one</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-setup-only" data-param="--only"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--only</code><span class="badge">&lt;name…&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only this item (mcp, tasqx-workflow, retro); repeat for more</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-setup-home" data-param="--home"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--home</code><span class="badge">&lt;dir&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Treat DIR as the home directory, the one holding <code>.claude</code></dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Three items: <code>mcp</code> registers <code>tasqx mcp serve --scope write</code> with Claude Code at user scope by running <code>claude mcp add</code>; <code>tasqx-workflow</code> and <code>retro</code> are skills written to <code>~/.claude/skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md</code> from copies compiled into this binary, so they match the tasqx you run (D159).</li><li>A skill that exists and is not byte-equal to the bundled copy reads <code>differs</code> — an older copy and your own edit look the same — and is kept unless you pass --force or tick it on the screen. So is an MCP registration that runs anything else, such as the read-only <code>tasqx mcp serve</code>; replacing it runs <code>claude mcp remove</code> first.</li><li>It never writes <code>~/.claude.json</code> itself. Without the <code>claude</code> command on PATH, the mcp item prints the exact command to run instead. Piped, with no flags, it prints the list and exits 0.</li><li>ripwire not found on PATH: install it from <code>https://github.com/redhat-et/ripwire</code> and put it on PATH.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-mcp"><code>mcp</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx setup --list</code></pre></div><p class="muted">what is installed; writes nothing</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx setup</code></pre></div><p class="muted">a checklist: space ticks, enter installs what is ticked</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx setup --yes</code></pre></div><p class="muted">installs everything not installed, and keeps a skill you edited</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx setup --yes --force --only retro</code></pre></div><p class="muted">replaces the retro skill with the copy this build carries</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it reports what is installed in the home directory of the machine it runs on, which the demo store knows nothing about. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-json-api">JSON API</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-export"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-export">export</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a>.</p><p>Dump tasks as canonical JSON.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx export [filter…] [--include-unscoped]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-export-filter" data-param="&lt;filter…&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;filter…&gt;</code><span class="badge">strings</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional filter DSL</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-export-include-unscoped" data-param="--include-unscoped"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--include-unscoped</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Widen a filtered export&#39;s docs/projects to ones that carry no project (D171). Refused on an unfiltered export — there is nothing to widen from</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>Canonical JSON; a filtered export trims edges leaving the set and reports <code>dropped_dependencies</code> (D12).</li><li>The document carries <code>projects</code> and <code>default_project</code> too, so a restore gives back the store and not only its tasks (D37).</li><li>A filter narrows <code>projects</code>/<code>docs</code>/<code>links</code>/<code>events</code> to what the exported tasks need — an unfiltered export still carries all of them; <code>--include-unscoped</code> widens a filtered one back to docs with no project (D171).</li><li>The document carries the graph&#39;s explicit links too, so a restore gives back the edges and not only the nodes; a filtered export keeps a link only when BOTH its ends are in it, and counts the rest as <code>dropped_links</code> (D181).</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-import"><code>import</code></a> · <a href="#cli-api"><code>api</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx export</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx export project:work</code></pre></div></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: the document carries every project and knowledge doc whatever the filter says, so the shortest export on the demo store runs past two hundred lines. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-import"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-import">import</h3><p>Maps to <a href="#api-store.import"><code>store.import</code></a>.</p><p>Load tasks from a JSON file or stdin.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx import &lt;file|-&gt; [--dry-run] [--merge]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-import-file" data-param="&lt;file&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;file&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Path to a canonical JSON document (<code>{tasks, projects, default_project, docs}</code>, as <code>tasqx export</code> writes) or a bare array of tasks, or <code>-</code> for stdin</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-import-dry-run" data-param="--dry-run"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--dry-run</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Run the import and roll it back (D184): report every renumbering, merge and refusal against this store without writing anything</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-import-merge" data-param="--merge"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--merge</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Merge a task this store already holds instead of replacing it (D185): union its notes, checks, tags and edges, take each field from the side whose event last wrote it, and count tracked time from both stores&#39; histories together (D189)</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>A task whose number a DIFFERENT task here already holds keeps its id and takes the next free one; every move is printed and reported as <code>renumbered</code> (D177). A task this store already holds keeps the number it has here.</li><li>A memory doc whose <code>source</code> a DIFFERENT doc here already holds merges onto that doc rather than being refused: the stored id is kept, the later <code>modified</code> wins the text, and every merge is printed and reported as <code>docs_merged</code> (D183).</li><li>Links are restored after everything they point at, counted in <code>links_imported</code>; a link naming an end neither the document nor this store holds refuses the whole import by name (D181).</li><li><code>--dry-run</code> runs the whole import against this store and rolls it back: every renumbering, merge and refusal prints exactly as a real import would, and the run ends with <code>nothing was written</code> (D184).</li><li><code>--merge</code> folds a second live store in rather than restoring over this one: a task this store already holds keeps its own annotations, checks, tags and edges and takes the payload&#39;s beside them, its <code>_rev</code> guard is skipped, and each of its fields follows the side whose event last wrote it, while tracked time from both sides adds up — one line per task names the fields that differed and where each came from, reported as <code>merged</code> (D185, D189). Without it the payload replaces a known task&#39;s child rows wholesale, which is what a restore wants.</li><li>A project this store already knows keeps its own non-empty description over the payload&#39;s — a project carries no <code>modified</code> stamp, so there is no later-wins call to make — reported as <code>project_description_conflicts</code> (D190). <code>archived</code> is still taken from the payload either way.</li><li>Two stores that both completed one recurring task each spawned its next occurrence. With or without <code>--merge</code>, two tasks sharing their predecessor and dates fold into the older: it takes the other&#39;s notes, checks, tags and edges, the status of whichever copy changed it last and the tracked time of both copies&#39; histories, and the fold is printed and reported as <code>deduplicated</code> (D191).</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a> · <a href="#cli-api"><code>api</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx import backup.json</code></pre></div><p class="muted">from a file</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx export | tasqx import -</code></pre></div><p class="muted">from stdin</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx import backup.json --dry-run</code></pre></div><p class="muted">preview it first</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx import other-machine.json --merge</code></pre></div><p class="muted">fold in another store</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it names a file, and a path from the machine that captured it is the one thing no second machine can reproduce. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="cli-api"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-api">api</h3><p>Maps to (any).</p><p>One JSON envelope in on stdin → one out on stdout.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx api   # one JSON envelope on stdin → one on stdout</code></pre><p>Takes no arguments of its own; the global flags still apply.</p><ul class="notes"><li>The stdio one-shot transport; the envelope key is <code>&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;</code>.</li><li>--socket is refused here rather than honoured (DESIGN.md D73): <code>api</code> runs against an in-process engine, never a daemon. --theme is likewise never read — there is nothing here to render.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-mcp"><code>mcp</code></a> · <a href="#cli-daemon"><code>daemon</code></a> · <a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx api &lt;&lt;&lt; &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.list&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{}}&#39;</code></pre></div><p class="muted">call any method</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.list&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+docs&quot;,&quot;sort&quot;:[&quot;-urgency&quot;]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="term">{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e1&quot;,&quot;ok&quot;:true,&quot;result&quot;:{&quot;count&quot;:2,&quot;next_offset&quot;:null,&quot;store_empty&quot;:false,&quot;tasks&quot;:[{&quot;_rev&quot;:1,&quot;active_since&quot;:null,&quot;blocked&quot;:true,&quot;budget_tokens&quot;:null,&quot;completed&quot;:null,&quot;created&quot;:&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:&quot;2026-09-21T00:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;estimate&quot;:&quot;PT5H&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;M&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;api&quot;,&quot;recurrence&quot;:null,&quot;remind&quot;:null,&quot;scheduled&quot;:null,&quot;short_id&quot;:51,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;pending&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;docs&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0&quot;,&quot;tracked&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;urgency&quot;:12.2,&quot;wait&quot;:null},{&quot;_rev&quot;:1,&quot;active_since&quot;:null,&quot;blocked&quot;:false,&quot;budget_tokens&quot;:null,&quot;completed&quot;:null,&quot;created&quot;:&quot;2026-09-05T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:null,&quot;estimate&quot;:&quot;PT4H&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;94362459-7e19-4ec0-a143-aa65f21c805c&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:&quot;2026-09-05T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;M&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;api&quot;,&quot;recurrence&quot;:null,&quot;remind&quot;:null,&quot;scheduled&quot;:null,&quot;short_id&quot;:55,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;pending&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;docs&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint&quot;,&quot;tracked&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;urgency&quot;:4.0,&quot;wait&quot;:null}],&quot;total&quot;:2},&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}
</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="cli-topic-completion">Shell completion</h3><section class="ref" id="cli-completions"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-cli-completions">completions</h3><p>Maps to — (no store).</p><p>Turn on Tab completion for your shell.</p><pre class="plain"><code style="white-space: pre-wrap">tasqx completions [&lt;shell&gt;] [--install | --uninstall] [--profile PATH] [--yes]</code></pre><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="cli-completions-shell" data-param="&lt;shell&gt;"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">&lt;shell&gt;</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which shell (bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh). Detected from $SHELL when omitted; on Windows nothing sets $SHELL, so name it</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-completions-install" data-param="--install"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--install</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Add the activation line to the shell&#39;s startup file (asks first)</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-completions-uninstall" data-param="--uninstall"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--uninstall</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Take the block a previous --install added back out again</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-completions-profile" data-param="--profile"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">--profile</code><span class="badge">&lt;path&gt;</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The file to edit instead of the shell&#39;s default startup file. Required for PowerShell: run it as <code>--profile $PROFILE</code> and let PowerShell expand the path it alone knows</dd></div><div class="param" id="cli-completions-y-yes" data-param="-y, --yes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">-y, --yes</code><span class="badge">flag</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Confirm the edit on the command line. Required when stdin is not a terminal — a pipeline has nobody to ask, and this feature will not edit a startup file on a guess</dd></div></dl><ul class="notes"><li>--install edits your shell&#39;s startup file inside a marked block, asks before writing, and refuses when stdin is not a terminal (pass --yes from a script).</li><li>cmd.exe cannot be completed by any program and is a permanent non-goal; nushell is a gap clap_complete has no generator for.</li></ul><p>See also <a href="#cli-manual"><code>manual</code></a> · <a href="#cli-docs"><code>docs</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx completions bash</code></pre></div><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx completions bash &gt;&gt; ~/.bashrc</code></pre></div><p class="muted">the printed line is one line for exactly this</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx completions --install</code></pre></div><p class="muted">detects the shell from $SHELL, shows the block, asks first</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx completions powershell --install --profile $PROFILE</code></pre></div><p class="muted">PowerShell expands $PROFILE; tasqx will not guess it</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx completions zsh --uninstall</code></pre></div><p class="muted">removes the block, restoring the file byte for byte</p></div><div class="ref-wide" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>No captured screen: it prints one line of shell for your startup file — the same line <code>--install</code> writes into it for you. Every other block of output on this page is a recording of this build running against the demo store (D149).</p></div></div></section><h3 id="h-exit-codes">Exit codes</h3><p>Stable contract. Script against these.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-25-h0">Code</th><th id="tbl-25-h1">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-25-h0"><code>0</code></td><td data-label="Meaning" headers="tbl-25-h1">Success.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-25-h0"><code>1</code></td><td data-label="Meaning" headers="tbl-25-h1"><code>internal</code>, or a failure beneath the request: the store would not open, a local write failed, or <code>watch</code> had no daemon to follow.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-25-h0"><code>2</code></td><td data-label="Meaning" headers="tbl-25-h1"><code>bad_request</code> — a bad value, an unparseable date, contradictory flags.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-25-h0"><code>4</code></td><td data-label="Meaning" headers="tbl-25-h1"><code>not_found</code> — no such task, project, or reference.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-25-h0"><code>5</code></td><td data-label="Meaning" headers="tbl-25-h1"><code>conflict</code> — a lost <code>--expected-rev</code> race, or a lifecycle rule.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-25-h0"><code>6</code></td><td data-label="Meaning" headers="tbl-25-h1"><code>unsupported_version</code> — the <code>tasqx</code> major you sent is not this build's.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx modify 1 --expected-rev 1 -p H ; echo &quot;exit=$?&quot;</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>error [conflict]: expected_rev 1 but task is at rev 2
exit=5</code></pre></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#guide-token-accounting"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Counting AI token spend per task</span></a><a class="next" href="#api"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">JSON API</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="api"><h2>The JSON API</h2><p class="lead">The load-bearing artifact. The CLI is a client; so is the MCP server; so could yours be. One envelope in, one envelope out.</p><section class="ref" id="api-transport"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-transport">The transport</h3><p><code>tasqx api</code> reads ONE request envelope on stdin and writes ONE response on stdout. No framing, no handshake, no daemon needed. For many calls on one connection, talk to the <a href="#daemon">daemon</a> socket instead — same envelopes, newline-delimited.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.list&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.list&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+docs&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e1&quot;,&quot;ok&quot;:true,&quot;result&quot;:{ … },&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}</code></pre></div></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-request">Request</h3><pre class="plain"><code>{
  &quot;tasqx&quot;:  &quot;1&quot;,            // API major. Required.
  &quot;id&quot;:     &quot;e1&quot;,           // Optional. Echoed back if present.
  &quot;method&quot;: &quot;task.list&quot;,    // Required.
  &quot;params&quot;: { }             // Optional; defaults to {}.
}</code></pre><h3 id="h-response">Response</h3><p>Success carries <code>result</code>; failure carries <code>error</code>. <code>ok</code> tells you which without inspecting further.</p><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.list&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+docs&quot;,&quot;sort&quot;:[&quot;-urgency&quot;]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="term">{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e1&quot;,&quot;ok&quot;:true,&quot;result&quot;:{&quot;count&quot;:2,&quot;next_offset&quot;:null,&quot;store_empty&quot;:false,&quot;tasks&quot;:[{&quot;_rev&quot;:1,&quot;active_since&quot;:null,&quot;blocked&quot;:true,&quot;budget_tokens&quot;:null,&quot;completed&quot;:null,&quot;created&quot;:&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:&quot;2026-09-21T00:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;estimate&quot;:&quot;PT5H&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;M&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;api&quot;,&quot;recurrence&quot;:null,&quot;remind&quot;:null,&quot;scheduled&quot;:null,&quot;short_id&quot;:51,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;pending&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;docs&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0&quot;,&quot;tracked&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;urgency&quot;:12.2,&quot;wait&quot;:null},{&quot;_rev&quot;:1,&quot;active_since&quot;:null,&quot;blocked&quot;:false,&quot;budget_tokens&quot;:null,&quot;completed&quot;:null,&quot;created&quot;:&quot;2026-09-05T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:null,&quot;estimate&quot;:&quot;PT4H&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;94362459-7e19-4ec0-a143-aa65f21c805c&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:&quot;2026-09-05T10:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;M&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;api&quot;,&quot;recurrence&quot;:null,&quot;remind&quot;:null,&quot;scheduled&quot;:null,&quot;short_id&quot;:55,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;pending&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;docs&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint&quot;,&quot;tracked&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;:&quot;PT0S&quot;,&quot;urgency&quot;:4.0,&quot;wait&quot;:null}],&quot;total&quot;:2},&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}
</pre></div><section class="ref" id="api-errors"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-errors">Errors</h3><p>An error is a value, not a crash. It carries a stable <code>code</code>, a human <code>message</code>, and machine-readable <code>data</code> — and the CLI's exit codes are these same codes.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-26-h0">Code</th><th id="tbl-26-h1">Exit</th><th id="tbl-26-h2">Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-26-h0"><code>bad_request</code></td><td data-label="Exit" headers="tbl-26-h1">2</td><td data-label="Means" headers="tbl-26-h2">Malformed params, an unparseable date, contradictory input.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-26-h0"><code>not_found</code></td><td data-label="Exit" headers="tbl-26-h1">4</td><td data-label="Means" headers="tbl-26-h2">No such task/project/reference.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-26-h0"><code>conflict</code></td><td data-label="Exit" headers="tbl-26-h1">5</td><td data-label="Means" headers="tbl-26-h2">A lost <code>expected_rev</code> race, or a lifecycle rule.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-26-h0"><code>unsupported_version</code></td><td data-label="Exit" headers="tbl-26-h1">6</td><td data-label="Means" headers="tbl-26-h2">The <code>tasqx</code> major you sent is not this build's.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Code" headers="tbl-26-h0"><code>internal</code></td><td data-label="Exit" headers="tbl-26-h1">1</td><td data-label="Means" headers="tbl-26-h2">A bug or an I/O failure. Should not happen.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Version mismatches are caught before dispatch, and the error's <code>data</code> names the major that <em>is</em> supported.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e2&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.get&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;999&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>{&quot;error&quot;:{&quot;code&quot;:&quot;not_found&quot;,&quot;data&quot;:{&quot;short_id&quot;:999},&quot;message&quot;:&quot;no task with short_id 999&quot;},&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e2&quot;,&quot;ok&quot;:false,&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}</code></pre></div><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;2&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;v1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.list&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>{&quot;error&quot;:{&quot;code&quot;:&quot;unsupported_version&quot;,&quot;data&quot;:{&quot;supported&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;message&quot;:&quot;unsupported api major version: 2&quot;},&quot;id&quot;:&quot;v1&quot;,&quot;ok&quot;:false,&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="soon"><p>Coming in the CLI reference: the exit code every verb returns, verb by verb.</p></div></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-feature-detection">Feature detection</h3><p>Do not guess what a build supports — ask it. <code>core.capabilities</code> is the handshake, and it also reports the current default project.</p><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;c1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;core.capabilities&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;c1&quot;,&quot;ok&quot;:true,&quot;result&quot;:{&quot;api&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;default_project&quot;:&quot;work.tasqx&quot;,&quot;features&quot;:[&quot;dependencies&quot;,&quot;filter.boolean&quot;,&quot;reminders&quot;],&quot;methods&quot;:[&quot;project.create&quot;,&quot;project.list&quot;,&quot;project.use&quot;,&quot;project.archive&quot;,&quot;task.add&quot;,&quot;task.list&quot;,&quot;task.get&quot;,&quot;task.brief&quot;,&quot;task.start&quot;,&quot;task.stop&quot;,&quot;task.adjust_tracked&quot;,&quot;task.done&quot;,&quot;task.modify&quot;,&quot;task.cancel&quot;,&quot;task.reopen&quot;,&quot;tag.add&quot;,&quot;tag.remove&quot;,&quot;annotation.add&quot;,&quot;check.add&quot;,&quot;check.set&quot;,&quot;check.remove&quot;,&quot;annotation.remove&quot;,&quot;annotation.update&quot;,&quot;token.add&quot;,&quot;token.remove&quot;,&quot;dependency.add&quot;,&quot;dependency.remove&quot;,&quot;link.add&quot;,&quot;link.remove&quot;,&quot;link.list&quot;,&quot;graph.query&quot;,&quot;memory.add&quot;,&quot;memory.search&quot;,&quot;memory.get&quot;,&quot;memory.remove&quot;,&quot;memory.import&quot;,&quot;memory.refresh&quot;,&quot;memory.list&quot;,&quot;memory.update&quot;,&quot;tokens.recompute&quot;,&quot;report.summary&quot;,&quot;report.outcomes&quot;,&quot;store.export&quot;,&quot;store.import&quot;,&quot;event.list&quot;,&quot;event.revert&quot;,&quot;reminder.fire&quot;,&quot;core.capabilities&quot;,&quot;otlp.status&quot;],&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;annotation.add&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;body&quot;],&quot;annotation.remove&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;annotation_id&quot;],&quot;annotation.update&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;annotation_id&quot;,&quot;body&quot;,&quot;expected_rev&quot;],&quot;check.add&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;body&quot;],&quot;check.remove&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;check_id&quot;,&quot;position&quot;],&quot;check.set&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;check_id&quot;,&quot;position&quot;,&quot;state&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;],&quot;core.capabilities&quot;:[],&quot;dependency.add&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;depends_on&quot;],&quot;dependency.remove&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;depends_on&quot;],&quot;event.list&quot;:[&quot;limit&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;entity&quot;,&quot;from&quot;],&quot;event.revert&quot;:[],&quot;graph.query&quot;:[&quot;root&quot;,&quot;depth&quot;,&quot;node_types&quot;,&quot;relation_types&quot;,&quot;project&quot;,&quot;status&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;,&quot;modified_after&quot;,&quot;modified_before&quot;,&quot;include_inferred&quot;,&quot;max_nodes&quot;,&quot;max_edges&quot;],&quot;link.add&quot;:[&quot;from&quot;,&quot;to&quot;,&quot;relation&quot;,&quot;metadata&quot;,&quot;expected_rev&quot;],&quot;link.list&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;relation&quot;,&quot;limit&quot;,&quot;offset&quot;],&quot;link.remove&quot;:[&quot;id&quot;],&quot;memory.add&quot;:[&quot;title&quot;,&quot;body&quot;,&quot;source&quot;,&quot;project&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;],&quot;memory.get&quot;:[&quot;id&quot;],&quot;memory.import&quot;:[&quot;docs&quot;,&quot;project&quot;],&quot;memory.list&quot;:[&quot;limit&quot;,&quot;offset&quot;,&quot;project&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;],&quot;memory.refresh&quot;:[&quot;dry_run&quot;],&quot;memory.remove&quot;:[&quot;id&quot;],&quot;memory.search&quot;:[&quot;query&quot;,&quot;limit&quot;,&quot;scope&quot;,&quot;raw&quot;,&quot;project&quot;,&quot;include_unscoped&quot;],&quot;memory.update&quot;:[&quot;id&quot;,&quot;title&quot;,&quot;body&quot;,&quot;source&quot;,&quot;project&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;,&quot;expected_rev&quot;],&quot;otlp.status&quot;:[],&quot;project.archive&quot;:[&quot;name&quot;],&quot;project.create&quot;:[&quot;name&quot;,&quot;description&quot;],&quot;project.list&quot;:[&quot;include_archived&quot;],&quot;project.use&quot;:[&quot;name&quot;],&quot;reminder.fire&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;at&quot;],&quot;report.outcomes&quot;:[&quot;group_by&quot;,&quot;filter&quot;,&quot;metrics&quot;,&quot;since&quot;,&quot;until&quot;],&quot;report.summary&quot;:[&quot;group_by&quot;,&quot;filter&quot;,&quot;metrics&quot;,&quot;all&quot;,&quot;since&quot;,&quot;until&quot;],&quot;store.export&quot;:[&quot;filter&quot;,&quot;include_unscoped&quot;],&quot;store.import&quot;:[&quot;tasks&quot;,&quot;projects&quot;,&quot;default_project&quot;,&quot;docs&quot;,&quot;events&quot;,&quot;links&quot;,&quot;dry_run&quot;,&quot;merge&quot;],&quot;tag.add&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;],&quot;tag.remove&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;],&quot;task.add&quot;:[&quot;title&quot;,&quot;project&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;,&quot;due&quot;,&quot;scheduled&quot;,&quot;wait&quot;,&quot;estimate&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;,&quot;recurrence&quot;,&quot;remind&quot;,&quot;budget_tokens&quot;],&quot;task.adjust_tracked&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;delta&quot;,&quot;reason&quot;],&quot;task.brief&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;memory_limit&quot;,&quot;max_body_bytes&quot;],&quot;task.cancel&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;],&quot;task.done&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;session_id&quot;,&quot;transcript_path&quot;,&quot;client&quot;,&quot;tool&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;checks_passed&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;,&quot;force&quot;,&quot;input_tokens&quot;,&quot;output_tokens&quot;,&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;,&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;,&quot;total_tokens&quot;],&quot;task.get&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;annotations_limit&quot;,&quot;annotations_offset&quot;,&quot;max_body_bytes&quot;,&quot;explain&quot;],&quot;task.list&quot;:[&quot;filter&quot;,&quot;sort&quot;,&quot;limit&quot;,&quot;offset&quot;,&quot;fields&quot;],&quot;task.modify&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;set&quot;,&quot;expected_rev&quot;],&quot;task.reopen&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;],&quot;task.start&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;keep&quot;,&quot;session_id&quot;,&quot;transcript_path&quot;,&quot;client&quot;,&quot;actor&quot;],&quot;task.stop&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;],&quot;token.add&quot;:[&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;tool&quot;,&quot;source&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;input_tokens&quot;,&quot;output_tokens&quot;,&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;,&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;,&quot;total_tokens&quot;,&quot;confidence&quot;,&quot;idempotency_key&quot;],&quot;token.remove&quot;:[&quot;measurement_id&quot;],&quot;tokens.recompute&quot;:[&quot;dry_run&quot;]},&quot;store&quot;:&quot;~/.local/share/tasqx/tasks.db&quot;},&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}</code></pre></div><h3 id="h-reading-tasks-without-the-api">Reading tasks without the API</h3><p>Any CLI command with <code>--json</code> prints the raw API result — the same bytes the envelope's <code>result</code> would carry. That is usually the shortest path from a shell script to structured data:</p><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx show 53 --json</code></pre><pre class="term">{
  &quot;_rev&quot;: 1,
  &quot;active_since&quot;: null,
  &quot;annotations&quot;: [],
  &quot;annotations_next_offset&quot;: null,
  &quot;annotations_offset&quot;: 0,
  &quot;annotations_removed&quot;: [],
  &quot;annotations_total&quot;: 0,
  &quot;blocked&quot;: false,
  &quot;blocks&quot;: [],
  &quot;budget_tokens&quot;: null,
  &quot;checks&quot;: [],
  &quot;completed&quot;: null,
  &quot;created&quot;: &quot;2026-08-15T10:00:00Z&quot;,
  &quot;delivered_annotation&quot;: null,
  &quot;delivered_annotation_id&quot;: null,
  &quot;depends_on&quot;: [],
  &quot;due&quot;: null,
  &quot;estimate&quot;: &quot;PT3H&quot;,
  &quot;first_annotation&quot;: null,
  &quot;fresh_tokens&quot;: 0,
  &quot;id&quot;: &quot;ea7f7301-c9b4-43b5-afc3-eec055c2d7f4&quot;,
  &quot;modified&quot;: &quot;2026-08-15T10:00:00Z&quot;,
  &quot;over&quot;: null,
  &quot;priority&quot;: &quot;M&quot;,
  &quot;project&quot;: &quot;infra&quot;,
  &quot;recurrence&quot;: null,
  &quot;remind&quot;: null,
  &quot;scheduled&quot;: null,
  &quot;short_id&quot;: 53,
  &quot;spawned_from&quot;: null,
  &quot;status&quot;: &quot;pending&quot;,
  &quot;tags&quot;: [
    &quot;ops&quot;
  ],
  &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Move nightly backups to object storage&quot;,
  &quot;tokens&quot;: [],
  &quot;tracked&quot;: &quot;PT0S&quot;,
  &quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;: &quot;PT0S&quot;,
  &quot;unmet_blockers&quot;: [],
  &quot;urgency&quot;: 4.2,
  &quot;wait&quot;: null
}
</pre></div><h3 id="h-every-method">Every method</h3><p>All 49, grouped by the object they act on. Every section below carries the method's parameters, the shape of what it answers with, and a real request and response — and every one of those columns is generated from the engine rather than described beside it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-27-h0">Object</th><th id="tbl-27-h1">Methods</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Project methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-project.create"><code>project.create</code></a> · <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a> · <a href="#api-project.use"><code>project.use</code></a> · <a href="#api-project.archive"><code>project.archive</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Task methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-task.add"><code>task.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.start"><code>task.start</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.stop"><code>task.stop</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.adjust_tracked"><code>task.adjust_tracked</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.modify"><code>task.modify</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.cancel"><code>task.cancel</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.reopen"><code>task.reopen</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Tag methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-tag.add"><code>tag.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-tag.remove"><code>tag.remove</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Annotation methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-annotation.add"><code>annotation.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a> · <a href="#api-annotation.update"><code>annotation.update</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Check methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-check.add"><code>check.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-check.set"><code>check.set</code></a> · <a href="#api-check.remove"><code>check.remove</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Dependency methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-dependency.add"><code>dependency.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-dependency.remove"><code>dependency.remove</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Link methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-link.add"><code>link.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-link.remove"><code>link.remove</code></a> · <a href="#api-link.list"><code>link.list</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Graph methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-graph.query"><code>graph.query</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Memory methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-memory.add"><code>memory.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-memory.search"><code>memory.search</code></a> · <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-memory.remove"><code>memory.remove</code></a> · <a href="#api-memory.import"><code>memory.import</code></a> · <a href="#api-memory.refresh"><code>memory.refresh</code></a> · <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a> · <a href="#api-memory.update"><code>memory.update</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Token methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-token.add"><code>token.add</code></a> · <a href="#api-token.remove"><code>token.remove</code></a> · <a href="#api-tokens.recompute"><code>tokens.recompute</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Report methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-report.summary"><code>report.summary</code></a> · <a href="#api-report.outcomes"><code>report.outcomes</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Store methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a> · <a href="#api-store.import"><code>store.import</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Event methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-event.list"><code>event.list</code></a> · <a href="#api-event.revert"><code>event.revert</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Reminder methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-reminder.fire"><code>reminder.fire</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">Core methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-core.capabilities"><code>core.capabilities</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="Object" headers="tbl-27-h0">OTLP methods</td><td data-label="Methods" headers="tbl-27-h1"><a href="#api-otlp.status"><code>otlp.status</code></a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 id="h-project-methods">Project methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-project.create"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-project.create">project.create</h3><p>The project, plus <code>default</code> (did it claim the default?) and <code>current_default</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-project">Project</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-project.create-name" data-param="name"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project's name. Dotted names (`work.tasqx`) are free-form: nothing nests, and a filter on `work` does not match `work.tasqx`.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-project.create-description" data-param="description"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">description</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the project is for. Shown by `project.list` and nowhere load-bearing.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The new project&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s name, as stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether this create claimed the default project — true only when the store had none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">current_default</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The default project after the call, whichever it is. Null only in a store with no default at all.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;pc1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;project.create&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;research&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Prototypes and spikes&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pc1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;current_default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7c42-9a08-1f0c4e5b62d7&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;research&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> a create mints a fresh v7 id, whose low bits are random — the pinned clock fixes the timestamp half and nothing fixes the rest, so a captured answer would differ on every run.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_create_project"><code>tasqx_create_project</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Prototypes and spikes&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;research&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_create_project&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx init</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-init"><code>init</code></a> — Create a project — just a name, no folder.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-project.list"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-project.list">project.list</h3><p><code>{projects}</code>; each row carries <code>default</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-project">Project</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-project.list-include-archived" data-param="include_archived"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_archived</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>false</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Include archived projects in the list. Omitted, an archive is out of sight.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many projects came back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">store_empty</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the store has ever held a task at all — how &quot;nothing yet&quot; is told apart from &quot;nothing matched&quot;.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">projects</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One row per project, sorted by name.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.projects[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s name — the value <code>project:</code> filters on and <code>task.add</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">description</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s description, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">archived</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the project is archived. Archived projects are omitted unless <code>include_archived</code> asked for them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether this is the project a bare <code>task.add</code> lands in.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;p1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;project.list&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;p1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">5</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;projects&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Public REST API and its SDKs&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;309d6b79-965e-4a32-9ae4-45508201e2bd&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;73f778aa-f6fa-4db8-a56a-bd72fb710734&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;home&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;CI, deploys and on-call&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;e3eff9c0-cf44-4d3f-89e7-d15f17362f25&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;infra&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;iOS and Android apps&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2fa91425-cb00-4853-9d2c-67eda13ffe79&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mobile&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Marketing site and docs portal&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;db5b5fab-8f4d-4e27-9da1-494c73cf256d&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;store_empty&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_projects"><code>tasqx_list_projects</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_list_projects&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx dashboard</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> — Open the overview screen, or ask for its panels as data.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx projects</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-projects"><code>projects</code></a> — List projects (default marked with <code>*</code>).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-project.use"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-project.use">project.use</h3><p><code>{name, default, previous}</code>. Sets the default project.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-project">Project</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-project.use-name" data-param="name"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project that becomes the default — where a `task.add` with no `project` lands.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project that is now the default.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Always true on success — the call&#39;s whole effect, echoed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">previous</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project that was the default before, or null if there was none.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;pu1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;project.use&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;api&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pu1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;previous&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>ruled out by D22: an agent has <code>project</code> on <code>task.add</code> and should name it, rather          than silently re-aiming the human&#39;s default for every later call, including the          human&#39;s own.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx use</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-use"><code>use</code></a> — Set the default project for bare adds.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-project.archive"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-project.archive">project.archive</h3><p>The archived project, plus <code>default_cleared</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-project">Project</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-project.archive-name" data-param="name"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project to archive. Archiving hides it from the list; it removes nothing.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project that was archived.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">archived</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Always true on success.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default_cleared</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether archiving it also cleared the store&#39;s default project (D22).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">open_tasks</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How much open work the archive left behind, counted in the same transaction (D89).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">open_overdue</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many of those open tasks are past their due date.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;pa1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;project.archive&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;mobile&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pa1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;default_cleared&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mobile&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;open_overdue&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;open_tasks&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">3</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>retiring a project is a decision about the human&#39;s workspace, not about the work.          An agent asked to tidy the project list is being asked to make that decision on          their behalf, and the CLI is where it belongs.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx archive</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-archive"><code>archive</code></a> — Retire a project — out of rotation, tasks untouched.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-task-methods">Task methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-task.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.add">task.add</h3><p>The new task, incl. the <code>project</code> it landed in (the default, if none given). <code>budget_tokens</code> (D139) is a size gauge over FRESH tokens — input, output and cache creation, never cache reads — which stops nothing and is read back as <code>fresh_tokens</code> and <code>over</code> on <code>task.get</code>. The title is stored verbatim: a title carrying the CLI's inline sugar (<code>+tag</code>, <code>due:</code>, <code>!prio</code>…) adds a <code>warnings</code> entry naming it.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.add-title" data-param="title"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Stored verbatim: this server does not parse the CLI&#39;s inline sugar (<code>+tag</code>, <code>project:</code>, <code>due:</code>, <code>!prio</code>). Use the fields below.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project to file it under. Omitted, the task lands in the store's default project — and the response says which, because that is the only place a caller learns it.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-priority" data-param="priority"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">priority</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Priority: H (high), M (medium), or L (low).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-due" data-param="due"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The deadline; drives urgency and anchors relative reminders, and never hides the task. Date grammar: &quot;tomorrow&quot;, &quot;friday&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20&quot;, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, &quot;eom&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20T17:00&quot; (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-scheduled" data-param="scheduled"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When you intend to start; a future value holds the task in <code>backlog</code> until it arrives. Date grammar: &quot;tomorrow&quot;, &quot;friday&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20&quot;, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, &quot;eom&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20T17:00&quot; (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-wait" data-param="wait"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">wait</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Hides the task until then, in <code>backlog</code> like <code>scheduled</code> but meaning &quot;not my problem yet&quot;. Date grammar: &quot;tomorrow&quot;, &quot;friday&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20&quot;, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, &quot;eom&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20T17:00&quot; (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-estimate" data-param="estimate"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Duration: &quot;4h&quot;, &quot;90m&quot;, &quot;1h30m&quot;, &quot;2d&quot;, &quot;1w&quot;, or ISO-8601 &quot;PT4H&quot;.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-tags" data-param="tags"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tags</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tags to put on the task. Lowercased and deduplicated as they are stored.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-recurrence" data-param="recurrence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Recurrence rule (D2 subset): &quot;daily&quot;, &quot;every 3 days&quot;, &quot;weekly on mon,wed&quot;, &quot;monthly on day 15&quot;, &quot;monthly on the last friday&quot;.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-remind" data-param="remind"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">remind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Reminder: a signed offset from <code>due</code> (&quot;-1h&quot;, &quot;-30m&quot;, &quot;-2d&quot;, &quot;+15m&quot;) or an absolute date in the <code>due</code> grammar.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.add-budget-tokens" data-param="budget_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">budget_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Token budget (D139): a size gauge over FRESH tokens — input, output, cache creation, never cache reads. It STOPS NOTHING; a blown budget signals a task too big to hand over whole. <code>tasqx_get_task</code> reports <code>over</code> against it.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The new task&#39;s uuid — stable, and what an export and an import agree on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The status the task landed in: <code>pending</code>, or <code>backlog</code> when a future <code>wait</code> parks it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the task actually landed in — for an inherited default this is the only place the caller learns it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The urgency score the fixed formula gives it (D1).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The recurrence rule as stored, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The title as STORED — the CLI&#39;s inline sugar can rewrite what you typed, so this is what to verify against.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The due date resolved to an instant: <code>due: &quot;friday&quot;</code> comes back as its ISO timestamp.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tags as stored, lowercased and deduplicated.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The scheduled date resolved to an instant, the same way <code>due</code> is.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">warnings</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present only when the title carries CLI inline sugar (<code>+tag</code>, <code>due:</code>, <code>!prio</code>…), which this door stores verbatim and never parses: one line naming those words.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;a1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Draft the Q4 roadmap&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;website&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;H&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:&quot;friday&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;planning&quot;]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;a1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;due&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-18T00:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7c42-9a08-1f0c4e5b62d7&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;recurrence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;scheduled&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">62</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tags&quot;</span>: [
      <span class="j-s">&quot;planning&quot;</span>
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Draft the Q4 roadmap&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;urgency&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">16.6</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> a new task&#39;s v7 id is half clock and half entropy, so no pin can reproduce it. The CLI&#39;s own <code>add</code> echo, which prints the short id, is captured instead.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_task"><code>tasqx_add_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;due&quot;:&quot;friday&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;H&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;website&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;planning&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Draft the Q4 roadmap&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx add</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-add"><code>add</code></a> — Capture a task — title plus inline sugar.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.list"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.list">task.list</h3><p><code>{count, total, next_offset, tasks}</code>. An omitted <code>filter</code> matches everything; <code>count</code> is how many rows came back and <code>total</code> how many matched, so a windowed list is never mistaken for a complete one. <code>next_offset</code> is null once nothing is left. An omitted <code>limit</code> defaults to 100; a named <code>limit</code> is clamped to 10,000. <code>fields</code> may include <code>depends_on</code>, which no other projection emits.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a> · <a href="#obj-dependency">Dependency</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.list-filter" data-param="filter"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL, e.g. &quot;status:pending +api&quot;. &quot;@working&quot; is the actionable set. Omit it (or send &quot;&quot;) for every task.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.list-sort" data-param="sort"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">sort</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Sort keys, e.g. [&quot;-urgency&quot;, &quot;due&quot;]; &quot;-&quot; descends. Valid: urgency, short_id, priority, due, created, modified, title, tokens, estimate, tracked. An unknown key is rejected.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.list-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Rows to return. Omit for this tool&#39;s page (100), shrunk to fit the response byte budget; a named limit is honoured up to 10000.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.list-offset" data-param="offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Matching rows to skip; pass the previous <code>next_offset</code>. Ordering is stable across pages.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.list-fields" data-param="fields"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">fields</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Restrict each row to these fields. Omit for short_id, title, status, priority, urgency, blocked, due, project, tags, with null-valued keys dropped; send [] for the whole row.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many rows came back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many tasks matched the filter, before <code>limit</code> truncated.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">next_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The <code>offset</code> that fetches the next page; null once nothing is left.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">store_empty</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the store has ever held a task at all — how &quot;nothing yet&quot; is told apart from &quot;nothing matched&quot;.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tasks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The matching tasks, one row each.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s uuid, stable across exports and machines.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>pending</code>, <code>backlog</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>cancelled</code> — or, on a stored row whose status text this build does not recognize, that text verbatim, with <code>status_unrecognized: true</code> beside it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">priority</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>H</code>, <code>M</code>, <code>L</code>, or null for none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the task belongs to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it is due, as an instant, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When work is planned to start, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>, out of the working set, as with <code>wait</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">wait</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Holds the task out of the working set until this instant, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The estimate as an ISO 8601 duration (<code>PT4H</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The recurrence rule (<code>every 3 days</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">remind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The reminder spec — an offset from <code>due</code> or an absolute instant — or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The urgency score (D1): priority, due proximity and age, summed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every tag on the task, as plain strings.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the task was captured.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When <code>task.done</code> completed it, or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it, and <code>task.cancel</code> does not set it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">budget_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The size gauge over FRESH tokens (D139), or null for no threshold. It stops nothing.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter. The methods that change the task or its tags, notes, checks and dependencies bump it; <code>token.add</code>, <code>token.remove</code> and <code>reminder.fire</code> leave it alone. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Time on the clock as an ISO duration, the interval still running included up to the moment of the read (D166). <code>active_since</code> marks where that one began.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_adjustment</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The net of every <code>task.adjust_tracked</code> correction already inside <code>tracked</code>, as a signed ISO duration (<code>-PT2H25M</code>); <code>PT0S</code> when there is none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">active_since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the open interval started, or null when the timer is not running.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether an unmet dependency is holding this task back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status_unrecognized</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present, and true, only on a row whose <code>status</code> no writer of this build could have produced — a store an older import wrote unvalidated, or a hand-edited one. <code>store.import</code> now refuses such a status.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.list&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+docs&quot;,&quot;sort&quot;:[&quot;-urgency&quot;]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;e1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;next_offset&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;store_empty&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tasks&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;active_since&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;blocked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;budget_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;completed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;due&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-21T00:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;estimate&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT5H&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;priority&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;M&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;recurrence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;remind&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;scheduled&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;tags&quot;</span>: [
          <span class="j-s">&quot;docs&quot;</span>
        ],
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;urgency&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">12.2</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;wait&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;active_since&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;blocked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;budget_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;completed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-05T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;due&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;estimate&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT4H&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;94362459-7e19-4ec0-a143-aa65f21c805c&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-05T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;priority&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;M&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;recurrence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;remind&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;scheduled&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">55</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;tags&quot;</span>: [
          <span class="j-s">&quot;docs&quot;</span>
        ],
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Add OpenAPI examples for every endpoint&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;urgency&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">4.0</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;wait&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_tasks"><code>tasqx_list_tasks</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+docs&quot;,&quot;sort&quot;:[&quot;-urgency&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_list_tasks&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx list</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a> — List tasks matching a filter.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx agenda</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-agenda"><code>agenda</code></a> — What is coming up, when — <code>list</code> ordered by time.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx next</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a> — The one highest-urgency unblocked task.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx dashboard</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> — Open the overview screen, or ask for its panels as data.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx pick</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> — Browse tasks on a full-screen list: read one, search them, start one.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx watch</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-watch"><code>watch</code></a> — Live-updating task view.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.get"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.get">task.get</h3><p>Full detail incl. annotations, deps, <code>blocked</code>. A limit takes the newest annotations; <code>annotations_total</code> and <code>annotations_next_offset</code> say what was left out. <code>max_body_bytes</code> caps each annotation body IN THE RESPONSE (D148): a longer one is cut on a character boundary and the row gains <code>body_bytes</code> (its real size) and <code>body_truncated</code>, so a single enormous note cannot blow a caller's payload limit; omit it and every body comes back whole, which is what the CLI and <code>tasqx api</code> do. <code>annotations_removed</code> lists the tombstones <code>annotation.remove</code> left — <code>{id, removed}</code> per scrubbed note, never its text — while <code>annotations</code> and <code>annotations_total</code> keep excluding them. <code>explain: true</code> adds <code>urgency_breakdown</code> (<code>priority</code>, <code>due_proximity</code>, <code>age</code>, <code>total</code>) — the terms <code>urgency</code> sums (D1); the plumbing <code>tasqx why --json</code> uses (#150).</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a> · <a href="#obj-annotation">Annotation</a> · <a href="#obj-check">Check</a> · <a href="#obj-dependency">Dependency</a> · <a href="#obj-measurement">Token measurement</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.get-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.get-annotations-limit" data-param="annotations_limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotations_limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Most-recent annotations to return; omit for this tool&#39;s page (20). An over-budget page is cut to what fits and the view names the <code>annotations_offset</code> for the rest; <code>include_json: true</code> spends that budget first. 0 returns none.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.get-annotations-offset" data-param="annotations_offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotations_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Annotations to skip, counted back from the newest; pass the previous <code>annotations_next_offset</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.get-max-body-bytes" data-param="max_body_bytes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">max_body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.get-explain" data-param="explain"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">explain</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Add <code>urgency_breakdown</code> (<code>priority</code>, <code>due_proximity</code>, <code>age</code>, <code>total</code>) — the terms <code>urgency</code> sums (D1). Default false.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note <code>task.done</code> pinned as the delivery note — the newest one at the instant of completion — or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">first_annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The oldest note, whatever page <code>annotations_limit</code>/<code>annotations_offset</code> asked for — the card&#39;s Description — or null when there is none (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The pinned delivery note — on a closed task with no pin, the newest note — or null on an open task, or when the pinned note was removed (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">fresh_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh tokens spent on this task — input, output and cache creation, never cache reads (D139), plus any unsplit <code>total_tokens</code> in full (D167).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">over</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether <code>fresh_tokens</code> is past <code>budget_tokens</code>; null when no budget was set, because there is no verdict to give.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">checks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The acceptance criteria on the task, in position order (D138).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s uuid, stable across exports and machines.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>pending</code>, <code>backlog</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>cancelled</code> — or, on a stored row whose status text this build does not recognize, that text verbatim, with <code>status_unrecognized: true</code> beside it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">priority</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>H</code>, <code>M</code>, <code>L</code>, or null for none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the task belongs to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it is due, as an instant, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When work is planned to start, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>, out of the working set, as with <code>wait</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">wait</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Holds the task out of the working set until this instant, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The estimate as an ISO 8601 duration (<code>PT4H</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The recurrence rule (<code>every 3 days</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">remind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The reminder spec — an offset from <code>due</code> or an absolute instant — or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The urgency score (D1): priority, due proximity and age, summed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every tag on the task, as plain strings.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the task was captured.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When <code>task.done</code> completed it, or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it, and <code>task.cancel</code> does not set it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">budget_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The size gauge over FRESH tokens (D139), or null for no threshold. It stops nothing.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter. The methods that change the task or its tags, notes, checks and dependencies bump it; <code>token.add</code>, <code>token.remove</code> and <code>reminder.fire</code> leave it alone. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Time on the clock as an ISO duration, the interval still running included up to the moment of the read (D166). <code>active_since</code> marks where that one began.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_adjustment</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The net of every <code>task.adjust_tracked</code> correction already inside <code>tracked</code>, as a signed ISO duration (<code>-PT2H25M</code>); <code>PT0S</code> when there is none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">active_since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the open interval started, or null when the timer is not running.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this task waits on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The notes on this task, oldest first within the page. Pages are counted back from the newest note, so <code>annotations_offset: 0</code> is the most recent page.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this task is holding back — the reverse edge of <code>depends_on</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">spawned_from</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short id of the task whose completion spawned this one (a recurrence, D170); null on any other task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many notes the task has, whether or not this page carries them all.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many notes this page skipped.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_next_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The offset of the next page of notes; null on the last one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_removed</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One tombstone per scrubbed note (D113) — id and instant, never the text. Excluded from <code>annotations</code> and its total.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every token measurement banked against this task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether an unmet dependency is holding this task back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status_unrecognized</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present, and true, only on a row whose <code>status</code> no writer of this build could have produced — a store an older import wrote unvalidated, or a hand-edited one. <code>store.import</code> now refuses such a status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency_breakdown</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The terms <code>urgency</code> sums — present only when <code>explain: true</code> asked for them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unmet_blockers</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The open prerequisites, named — what <code>blocked: true</code> is blocked ON.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.checks[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion&#39;s uuid — what <code>check.set</code> and <code>check.remove</code> take.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion itself, stored verbatim. tasqx never runs it; it is a claim, not a command.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>open</code>, <code>passed</code> or <code>failed</code>. A failure is a normal outcome, not an error.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The citation for the state, or null — some criteria are met by something nobody can quote.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it sits in the list, from zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the criterion was added.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When its state or evidence last changed.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.annotations[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The body&#39;s real size in bytes. Present only on a body this response cut (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present and true only on a body this response cut, so &quot;was this cut?&quot; stays a presence question.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.first_annotation</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The body&#39;s real size in bytes. Present only on a body this response cut (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present and true only on a body this response cut, so &quot;was this cut?&quot; stays a presence question.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.delivered_annotation</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">