  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_task"><code>tasqx_get_task</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_get_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx pick</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> — Browse tasks on a full-screen list: read one, search them, start one.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx show</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> — Show one task in full detail.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx why</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a> — Explain a task&#39;s urgency score.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.brief"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.brief">task.brief</h3><p><code>{task, neighbourhood, memory}</code>. Everything needed before starting one task (D136): <code>task</code> is <code>task.get</code>'s own result verbatim; <code>neighbourhood.depends_on</code> names each prerequisite with its NEWEST annotation — what that task concluded — and <code>neighbourhood.blocks</code> names what this one releases, title and status only; on a recurrence spawn, <code>last_time</code> names the previous occurrence and the first paragraph of its newest note (D170); <code>memory</code> is a <code>memory.search</code> result under an expression tasqx DERIVES from the task's title, tags and project, echoed in <code>matched</code>, scoped to that project PLUS unscoped docs (the same <code>include_unscoped</code> shape <code>memory.search</code> has) or, for a task with no project, store-wide — reported either way in <code>project</code> — and excluding the task's OWN annotations, which the <code>task</code> half already carries in full (#657, D168). The derived expression is a disjunction: a caller's query states what they want and is ANDed, a derived one is a bag of the task's own words and would answer nothing if it were. Half the page (rounded up) is reserved for knowledge docs and annotations fill the rest, either kind taking the other's unused slots, docs listed first (D147); <code>reserved_docs</code>, <code>docs_total</code> and <code>annotations_total</code> say what was done. <code>memory_limit</code> defaults to 5 (D154). <code>max_body_bytes</code> caps each annotation body of the TASK half in the response, exactly as on <code>task.get</code> (D148) — no <code>annotations_limit</code>, because a brief is what you read BEFORE starting and dropping whole notes from it is the wrong cut.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a> · <a href="#obj-annotation">Annotation</a> · <a href="#obj-check">Check</a> · <a href="#obj-dependency">Dependency</a> · <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a> · <a href="#obj-measurement">Token measurement</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.brief-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id or UUID.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.brief-memory-limit" data-param="memory_limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">memory_limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Memory hits to return; default 5. Half the slots (rounded up) are reserved for knowledge docs, annotations fill the rest, and either kind takes the other&#39;s unused slots.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.brief-max-body-bytes" data-param="max_body_bytes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">max_body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">task</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>task.get</code>&#39;s own result for this task, without <code>urgency_breakdown</code> — the brief does not take <code>explain</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">neighbourhood</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What this task waits on and what it releases.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">memory</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">A <code>memory.search</code> result under an expression derived from the task&#39;s own words.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">last_time</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present only on a recurrence spawn: the previous occurrence and what it delivered (D170).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note <code>task.done</code> pinned as the delivery note — the newest one at the instant of completion — or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">first_annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The oldest note, whatever page <code>annotations_limit</code>/<code>annotations_offset</code> asked for — the card&#39;s Description — or null when there is none (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The pinned delivery note — on a closed task with no pin, the newest note — or null on an open task, or when the pinned note was removed (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">fresh_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh tokens spent on this task — input, output and cache creation, never cache reads (D139), plus any unsplit <code>total_tokens</code> in full (D167).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">over</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether <code>fresh_tokens</code> is past <code>budget_tokens</code>; null when no budget was set, because there is no verdict to give.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">checks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The acceptance criteria on the task, in position order (D138).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s uuid, stable across exports and machines.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>pending</code>, <code>backlog</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>cancelled</code> — or, on a stored row whose status text this build does not recognize, that text verbatim, with <code>status_unrecognized: true</code> beside it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">priority</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>H</code>, <code>M</code>, <code>L</code>, or null for none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the task belongs to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it is due, as an instant, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When work is planned to start, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>, out of the working set, as with <code>wait</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">wait</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Holds the task out of the working set until this instant, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The estimate as an ISO 8601 duration (<code>PT4H</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The recurrence rule (<code>every 3 days</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">remind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The reminder spec — an offset from <code>due</code> or an absolute instant — or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The urgency score (D1): priority, due proximity and age, summed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every tag on the task, as plain strings.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the task was captured.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When <code>task.done</code> completed it, or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it, and <code>task.cancel</code> does not set it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">budget_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The size gauge over FRESH tokens (D139), or null for no threshold. It stops nothing.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter. The methods that change the task or its tags, notes, checks and dependencies bump it; <code>token.add</code>, <code>token.remove</code> and <code>reminder.fire</code> leave it alone. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Time on the clock as an ISO duration, the interval still running included up to the moment of the read (D166). <code>active_since</code> marks where that one began.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_adjustment</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The net of every <code>task.adjust_tracked</code> correction already inside <code>tracked</code>, as a signed ISO duration (<code>-PT2H25M</code>); <code>PT0S</code> when there is none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">active_since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the open interval started, or null when the timer is not running.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this task waits on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The notes on this task, oldest first within the page. Pages are counted back from the newest note, so <code>annotations_offset: 0</code> is the most recent page.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this task is holding back — the reverse edge of <code>depends_on</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">spawned_from</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short id of the task whose completion spawned this one (a recurrence, D170); null on any other task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many notes the task has, whether or not this page carries them all.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many notes this page skipped.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_next_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The offset of the next page of notes; null on the last one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_removed</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One tombstone per scrubbed note (D113) — id and instant, never the text. Excluded from <code>annotations</code> and its total.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every token measurement banked against this task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether an unmet dependency is holding this task back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status_unrecognized</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present, and true, only on a row whose <code>status</code> no writer of this build could have produced — a store an older import wrote unvalidated, or a hand-edited one. <code>store.import</code> now refuses such a status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unmet_blockers</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The open prerequisites, named — what <code>blocked: true</code> is blocked ON.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task.checks[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion&#39;s uuid — what <code>check.set</code> and <code>check.remove</code> take.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion itself, stored verbatim. tasqx never runs it; it is a claim, not a command.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>open</code>, <code>passed</code> or <code>failed</code>. A failure is a normal outcome, not an error.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The citation for the state, or null — some criteria are met by something nobody can quote.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it sits in the list, from zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the criterion was added.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When its state or evidence last changed.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task.annotations[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The body&#39;s real size in bytes. Present only on a body this response cut (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present and true only on a body this response cut, so &quot;was this cut?&quot; stays a presence question.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task.first_annotation</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The body&#39;s real size in bytes. Present only on a body this response cut (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present and true only on a body this response cut, so &quot;was this cut?&quot; stays a presence question.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task.delivered_annotation</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The body&#39;s real size in bytes. Present only on a body this response cut (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present and true only on a body this response cut, so &quot;was this cut?&quot; stays a presence question.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task.annotations_removed[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The scrubbed note&#39;s id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was scrubbed. Never the text — that is the point of the method.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task.tokens[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement&#39;s uuid — what <code>token.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which tool spent the tokens (<code>claude-code</code>, <code>codex</code>, …).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How the figure was obtained: <code>self-report</code>, <code>log-parse</code> or <code>otel</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache — never blended with the others (D48).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How checkable the figure is: <code>high</code>, <code>medium</code> or <code>low</code>. A self-report may not claim <code>high</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the measurement was banked.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, from a reporter that could not split it — 0 on a split measurement, and never folded into the four (D167).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.task.unmet_blockers[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s short id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s title, so a refusal can be read without a second call.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.neighbourhood</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Each prerequisite, with its newest annotation — what that task concluded.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What this task releases when it completes, title and status only.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.neighbourhood.depends_on[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The prerequisite&#39;s status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The prerequisite&#39;s newest note, or null when nobody wrote one.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.neighbourhood.blocks[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The dependent&#39;s status.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.memory</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many hits came back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many rows matched before the page was cut.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">has_more</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether anything was left behind.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">hits</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The hits themselves — the same rows <code>memory.search</code> returns.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">matched</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The FTS expression tasqx derived from the task; null when the task had no searchable word.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the search was scoped to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">reserved_docs</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many of the page&#39;s slots were held for knowledge docs (D147).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">docs_total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many docs matched.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many annotations matched.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.last_time</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the previous occurrence was completed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The first paragraph of its newest note — the delivery note — or null when nobody wrote one.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.memory.hits[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s id, or the annotation&#39;s.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">kind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>doc</code> or <code>annotation</code> — which store the hit came from.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s title; for an annotation, the task it is written on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where the doc came from (a file path, <code>task:#51</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">snippet</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The matching passage, with the hit in context. Never the whole body.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rank</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The bm25 score. Lower is a better match; the number itself is not comparable between searches.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">For a doc hit, whether it is a standing ruling (D156); null on an annotation hit, which has no such flag.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which project this hit is scoped to — a doc&#39;s own column, or the annotation&#39;s task&#39;s — or null for global knowledge (#657).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">stale</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">true when the doc&#39;s origin file no longer matches what was imported; null for annotations and docs with no origin (D180).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;b1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.brief&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;memory_limit&quot;:3}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;b1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;memory&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;annotations_total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">3</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;docs_total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;has_more&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;hits&quot;</span>: [
        {
          <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;kind&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;doc&quot;</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;rank&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">-0.9096037228757</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;snippet&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Cut the release branch on Monday, tag after the canary has run…&quot;</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/release.md&quot;</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;stale&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;release-process&quot;</span>
        }
      ],
      <span class="j-k">&quot;matched&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;guide OR migration OR sdk OR docs OR api&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;reserved_docs&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">4</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;neighbourhood&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;blocks&quot;</span>: [],
      <span class="j-k">&quot;depends_on&quot;</span>: [
        {
          <span class="j-k">&quot;annotation&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">50</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Rate-limit the /search endpoint&quot;</span>
        }
      ]
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;task&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;…&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task.get&#39;s own result, verbatim&quot;</span>
    }
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> every hit carries an FTS bm25 <code>rank</code>, computed through the platform&#39;s <code>log()</code> — captured on macOS the last digits differ on Linux, and the drift job goes red for everyone but whoever captured last. The <code>tasqx brief</code> SCREEN is captured instead; it prints snippets and never the number.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;memory_limit&quot;:3,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_brief_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx brief</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-brief"><code>brief</code></a> — Everything needed before starting a task, in one read.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.start"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.start">task.start</h3><p>The task, timer running. Correlation params land in the start event. <code>auto_stopped</code> lists whichever other task D6's single-active rule just stopped to make room for this one — empty unless <code>keep</code> was omitted and something else was running. <code>actor</code> (D140) says who is asking for the clock: a start against a timer a DIFFERENT actor holds is refused <code>conflict</code> rather than silently stopping it, since that would leave the other party's work untracked. Absent on both sides — a shell — keeps D6's behaviour exactly; the MCP server fills it in with its own connection id.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.start-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.start-keep" data-param="keep"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">keep</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Keep other active tasks running (opt out of single-active).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.start-session-id" data-param="session_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">session_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your agent-session id, recorded on this task&#39;s event for token attribution.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.start-transcript-path" data-param="transcript_path"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">transcript_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Absolute path to your session transcript, recorded on the same event.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.start-client" data-param="client"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">client</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Calling tool as &quot;&lt;name&gt; &lt;version&gt;&quot;. Filled in from the MCP handshake when omitted.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.start-actor" data-param="actor"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">actor</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Who is asking for the clock (D140); filled in with this connection&#39;s id when omitted. Starting while ANOTHER actor holds an active clock is a <code>conflict</code>, not a silent stop of their timer; pass <code>keep: true</code> to run both.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>active</code> once the clock is running.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">interval_started</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the running interval opened. On the idempotent re-start of a task already running, that interval&#39;s existing start. Null only if an active row has lost its start, which no tasqx write produces.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">already_running</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">True when the call opened no new interval because the timer was already on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">auto_stopped</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whatever D6&#39;s single-active rule stopped to make room. Empty unless <code>keep</code> was omitted and something else was running.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.auto_stopped[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The stopped task&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The stopped task&#39;s short id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That task&#39;s running total after the stop.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;s1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.start&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;50&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;s1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;already_running&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;auto_stopped&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;63e5a05b-e665-459b-be06-d750369a9ad7&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">48</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;813547e2-5937-41f0-8401-82fcdb14a009&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;interval_started&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">50</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;active&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Rate-limit the /search endpoint&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_start_timer"><code>tasqx_start_timer</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;50&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_start_timer&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx pick</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> — Browse tasks on a full-screen list: read one, search them, start one.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx start</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-start"><code>start</code></a> — Mark a task active.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.stop"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.stop">task.stop</h3><p><code>{status, interval, tracked}</code>. <code>interval</code> is the duration just closed; <code>tracked</code> is the running total, the same word <code>task.get</code> uses for it.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.stop-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The status the task fell back to.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">interval</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The interval just closed, as an ISO duration.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The running total after the stop — the same word <code>task.get</code> uses.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;st1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.stop&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;48&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;st1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;interval&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">48</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Ship the v2 pricing page&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_stop_timer"><code>tasqx_stop_timer</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;48&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_stop_timer&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx stop</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-stop"><code>stop</code></a> — Pause an active task.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.adjust_tracked"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.adjust_tracked">task.adjust_tracked</h3><p><code>{short_id, title, delta, tracked, tracked_adjustment, _rev}</code>. A signed correction (<code>-2h25m</code>, <code>+30m</code>) to tracked time, in any status; a total below zero or an empty reason is <code>bad_request</code>. Recorded as its own event, which <code>event.revert</code> takes back (D166).</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.adjust_tracked-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.adjust_tracked-delta" data-param="delta"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">delta</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Signed duration: <code>-2h25m</code>, <code>+30m</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.adjust_tracked-reason" data-param="reason"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">reason</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Why the time is corrected.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delta</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The correction this call applied, as a signed ISO duration.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The total after it — the same word <code>task.get</code> uses.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_adjustment</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The net of every correction on the task, this one included.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision after the correction.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;at1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.adjust_tracked&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;42&quot;,&quot;delta&quot;:&quot;-2h25m&quot;,&quot;reason&quot;:&quot;idle gap&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;at1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;delta&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;-PT2H25M&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">42</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Paginate the audit log&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT6H25M&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;-PT2H25M&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked"><code>tasqx_adjust_tracked</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;delta&quot;:&quot;-2h25m&quot;,&quot;reason&quot;:&quot;idle gap&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;42&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_adjust_tracked&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx adjust</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-adjust"><code>adjust</code></a> — Correct a task&#39;s tracked time.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.done"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.done">task.done</h3><p>The task; plus the spawned next instance if recurring. Correlation params land in the done event, and so do <code>tool</code> and <code>model</code> on their own (D65) — a caller that cannot count its tokens still records who did the work. Any present token count additionally records a self-report measurement — <code>total_tokens</code> alone is one unsplit count, never beside the four (D167) — the primary channel: only the caller knows which task a turn's spend served, and the log-parse fallback refuses samples claimed by more than one task's window. A task with open blockers is refused <code>conflict</code> naming them; <code>force: true</code> completes it anyway, and the response then carries <code>forced: true</code> and <code>blocked_by</code> (D150).</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a> · <a href="#obj-dependency">Dependency</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.done-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-session-id" data-param="session_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">session_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your agent-session id, recorded on this task&#39;s event for token attribution.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-transcript-path" data-param="transcript_path"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">transcript_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Absolute path to your session transcript, recorded on the same event.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-client" data-param="client"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">client</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Calling tool as &quot;&lt;name&gt; &lt;version&gt;&quot;. Filled in from the MCP handshake when omitted.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-tool" data-param="tool"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The AI tool doing the work, free-form (e.g. &quot;claude-code&quot;). Also names a token measurement, defaulting to <code>client</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-model" data-param="model"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model doing the work, e.g. &quot;claude-opus-5&quot;. Recorded with or without token counts.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-checks-passed" data-param="checks_passed"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">checks_passed</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Ids of the acceptance criteria this work proved (D138). Completing with criteria open is not refused, but <code>tasqx_outcomes</code> counts it unproven.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-evidence" data-param="evidence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One citation covering <code>checks_passed</code>: a test name, an excerpt of output, a commit sha.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-force" data-param="force"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">force</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Complete despite still-open dependencies; without it that is a <code>conflict</code> naming them (D150). The override is recorded and counted under <code>forced</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-input-tokens" data-param="input_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported input tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-output-tokens" data-param="output_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported output tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-cache-read-tokens" data-param="cache_read_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported cache-read tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-cache-creation-tokens" data-param="cache_creation_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported cache-creation tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.done-total-tokens" data-param="total_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, instead of the four (D167).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>done</code> — the status the task is now in.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The instant recorded as the completion.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unblocked</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this completion released.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">spawned</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The next instance, present only when the completed task carried a recurrence rule (D2) and no task already holds that next slot, as after a reopen and a second completion (D191).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens_hint</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present only when the completion self-reported no token counts — the nudge, not an error.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Time on the clock when it closed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What it was estimated at, or null — beside <code>tracked</code>, the calibration in one line.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">forced</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present and true only on a completion that overrode still-open blockers (D150).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked_by</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blockers that override left open. Present only beside <code>forced</code>.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.blocked_by[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s short id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s title, so a refusal can be read without a second call.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;d1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.done&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;47&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;d1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;completed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;estimate&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT1H&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">47</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;done&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Renew the TLS certificate for api.example.dev&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tokens_hint&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;no token counts were self-reported; log-parse attribution is a best-effort fallback — pass input_tokens/output_tokens/cache_read_tokens/cache_creation_tokens on completion for a reliable measurement&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;unblocked&quot;</span>: []
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_complete_task"><code>tasqx_complete_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;47&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_complete_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx done</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a> — Complete a task.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.modify"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.modify">task.modify</h3><p><code>{short_id, _rev, set}</code>; <code>set</code> echoes the RESOLVED value actually stored for each field this call named (e.g. <code>due:"friday"</code> comes back as its ISO instant). <code>null</code> in the request's own <code>set</code> clears a field. A stale <code>expected_rev</code> is a <code>conflict</code> carrying the current rev; a <code>set.title</code> carrying inline sugar adds <code>warnings</code>, as on <code>task.add</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.modify-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.modify-set" data-param="set"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">set</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Field → new value, e.g. {&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;M&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:&quot;2026-07-22T17:00:00+02:00&quot;}.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-task.modify-expected-rev" data-param="expected_rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">expected_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optimistic-concurrency guard. Supplied by the server from the task&#39;s current <code>_rev</code> when omitted; pass it to pin a rev you read earlier. There is no last-writer-wins mode.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter. The methods that change the task or its tags, notes, checks and dependencies bump it; <code>token.add</code>, <code>token.remove</code> and <code>reminder.fire</code> leave it alone. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">set</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The RESOLVED value stored for each field this call named — <code>due: &quot;friday&quot;</code> comes back as its instant.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">warnings</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present only when <code>set.title</code> carries CLI inline sugar, stored verbatim: one line naming those words, as on <code>task.add</code>.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;m1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.modify&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;52&quot;,&quot;set&quot;:{&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;H&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:&quot;friday&quot;}}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;m1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;set&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;due&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-18T00:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;priority&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;H&quot;</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">52</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_modify_task"><code>tasqx_modify_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;52&quot;,&quot;set&quot;:{&quot;due&quot;:&quot;friday&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;H&quot;}},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_modify_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx modify</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-modify"><code>modify</code></a> — Change a task — set fields or --clear them.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.cancel"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.cancel">task.cancel</h3><p><code>{short_id, status}</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.cancel-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>cancelled</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unblocked</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids the cancellation released — a cancelled blocker stops blocking (D114).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;c1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.cancel&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;60&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;c1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">60</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;cancelled&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;unblocked&quot;</span>: []
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_cancel_task"><code>tasqx_cancel_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;60&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_cancel_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx cancel</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-cancel"><code>cancel</code></a> — Cancel a task.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-task.reopen"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-task.reopen">task.reopen</h3><p><code>{short_id, status, blocked}</code>. <code>blocked</code> names the open dependents this reopen put back — the mirror of <code>unblocked</code> on <code>task.done</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-task.reopen-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The status the task went back to.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The open dependents this reopen put back into <code>blocked</code> — the mirror of <code>unblocked</code>.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ro1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;task.reopen&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;12&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ro1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;blocked&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">12</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_reopen_task"><code>tasqx_reopen_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;12&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_reopen_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx reopen</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-reopen"><code>reopen</code></a> — Reopen a completed or cancelled task.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-tag-methods">Tag methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-tag.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-tag.add">tag.add</h3><p>The task's tags.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-tag.add-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-tag.add-tags" data-param="tags"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tags</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tags to add. Already-present tags are a no-op rather than an error.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every tag on the task after the call.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;t1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tag.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;53&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;q4&quot;]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;t1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">53</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tags&quot;</span>: [
      <span class="j-s">&quot;ops&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-s">&quot;q4&quot;</span>
    ]
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_tag_task"><code>tasqx_tag_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;53&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;q4&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_tag_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tag</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-tag"><code>tag</code></a> — Attach tags to a task.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-tag.remove"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-tag.remove">tag.remove</h3><p>The task's remaining tags, plus <code>removed</code>. A tag the task does not have is <code>not_found</code> and removes <em>nothing</em> — all or nothing, so a typo can never answer ok.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-tag.remove-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-tag.remove-tags" data-param="tags"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tags</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tags to take off. All or nothing: a tag the task does not have is `not_found` and removes none of them, so a typo cannot answer ok.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tags left on the task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tags this call took off. A tag the task does not have is <code>not_found</code> and removes nothing.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;t2&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tag.remove&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;53&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ops&quot;]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;t2&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;removed&quot;</span>: [
      <span class="j-s">&quot;ops&quot;</span>
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">53</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tags&quot;</span>: []
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_untag_task"><code>tasqx_untag_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;53&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ops&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_untag_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx untag</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-untag"><code>untag</code></a> — Remove tags from a task.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-annotation-methods">Annotation methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-annotation.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-annotation.add">annotation.add</h3><p>The annotation.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-annotation">Annotation</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-annotation.add-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-annotation.add-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Note text, stored verbatim. Multi-line markdown is fine.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note as stored, echoed back so a caller can see its bytes survived.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.annotation</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;an1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;annotation.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release.&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;an1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;annotation&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release.&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7401-a1e6-c040f1ddbe51&quot;</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the note&#39;s id is minted fresh, v7, half of it random. The <code>tasqx annotate</code> screen is captured instead.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_annotate_task"><code>tasqx_annotate_task</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release.&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_annotate_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx annotate</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-annotate"><code>annotate</code></a> — Attach a timestamped note to a task.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-annotation.remove"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-annotation.remove">annotation.remove</h3><p><code>{short_id, removed}</code>. Scrubs the annotation's body in the store (D113) — a hard delete, not a hide — and <code>removed</code> names only the id and the instant, never the text. An unknown or already-removed id is <code>not_found</code>; <code>event.revert</code> does not cover this op.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-annotation">Annotation</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-annotation.remove-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-annotation.remove-annotation-id" data-param="annotation_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The annotation&#39;s id, as tasqx_annotate_task or tasqx_get_task reports.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tombstone: the id and the instant, never the text (D113).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.removed</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The scrubbed note&#39;s id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was scrubbed. Never the text — that is the point of the method.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ar1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;annotation.remove&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;annotation_id&quot;:&quot;17dd6621-7db4-43b5-9f36-ddf89018081e&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ar1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;removed&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;17dd6621-7db4-43b5-9f36-ddf89018081e&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;removed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_annotation"><code>tasqx_remove_annotation</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;annotation_id&quot;:&quot;17dd6621-7db4-43b5-9f36-ddf89018081e&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_annotation&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx unannotate</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-unannotate"><code>unannotate</code></a> — Permanently scrub one annotation&#39;s text, by id.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-annotation.update"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-annotation.update">annotation.update</h3><p><code>{short_id, annotation, _rev}</code>. Replaces one note's body IN PLACE (D165): its id, <code>created</code> and position are kept, so a corrected first note stays the card's Description, and search re-indexes the new text. <code>expected_rev</code> is the TASK's <code>_rev</code>, as on <code>task.modify</code>. A removed note is <code>not_found</code>; <code>event.revert</code> puts the previous body back.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-annotation">Annotation</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-annotation.update-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-annotation.update-annotation-id" data-param="annotation_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The annotation&#39;s id, as tasqx_annotate_task or tasqx_get_task reports.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-annotation.update-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The corrected text; replaces the old body whole.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-annotation.update-expected-rev" data-param="expected_rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">expected_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Guard on the task&#39;s <code>_rev</code>; supplied by the server when omitted.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note as it now stands: the same id and <code>created</code>, the new body (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter after the edit. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make the next change conditional.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.annotation</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;au1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;annotation.update&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;annotation_id&quot;:&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7401-a1e6-c040f1ddbe51&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Ruling: the guide ships AFTER the 3.0 release.&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;au1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">7</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;annotation&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Ruling: the guide ships AFTER the 3.0 release.&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7401-a1e6-c040f1ddbe51&quot;</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the note it edits has an id minted fresh, v7, half of it random, so no fixed request can name it.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_update_annotation"><code>tasqx_update_annotation</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;annotation_id&quot;:&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7401-a1e6-c040f1ddbe51&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Ruling: the guide ships AFTER the 3.0 release.&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_update_annotation&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx annotate</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-annotate"><code>annotate</code></a> — Attach a timestamped note to a task.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-check-methods">Check methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-check.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-check.add">check.add</h3><p><code>{short_id, check{id, body, state, evidence, position, created, modified}}</code>. One acceptance criterion (D138), appended at the end and starting <code>open</code>. tasqx NEVER RUNS a check: the body is a claim and <code>evidence</code> is a citation, both stored verbatim and neither interpreted. What runs commands is a hook the operator installed, calling <code>check.set</code> like any other client.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-check">Check</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-check.add-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-check.add-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion, in your own words. Stored verbatim.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">check</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion as stored, appended at the end and starting <code>open</code>.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.check</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion&#39;s uuid — what <code>check.set</code> and <code>check.remove</code> take.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion itself, stored verbatim. tasqx never runs it; it is a claim, not a command.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>open</code>, <code>passed</code> or <code>failed</code>. A failure is a normal outcome, not an error.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The citation for the state, or null — some criteria are met by something nobody can quote.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it sits in the list, from zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the criterion was added.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When its state or evidence last changed.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ca1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;check.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Every renamed symbol has a row in the table&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ca1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;check&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Every renamed symbol has a row in the table&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;evidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7a90-b0c1-52f0a7d3c611&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;position&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">4</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;state&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;open&quot;</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the criterion&#39;s id is minted fresh, v7, half of it random.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_check"><code>tasqx_add_check</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Every renamed symbol has a row in the table&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_check&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx check</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-check"><code>check</code></a> — Acceptance criteria on a task: add, mark, drop.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-check.set"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-check.set">check.set</h3><p><code>{short_id, check_id, state}</code>. <code>state</code> is <code>open|passed|failed</code>; <code>failed</code> is a normal outcome, not an error. <code>evidence</code> is optional — some criteria are met by something nobody can quote, and inventing a citation is worse than an unproven pass. Name the check by exactly one of <code>check_id</code> or <code>position</code> (1-based, in the order <code>task.get</code> lists them); an unknown one is <code>not_found</code> listing the task's checks.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-check">Check</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-check.set-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-check.set-check-id" data-param="check_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">check_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The check&#39;s id, from <code>tasqx_get_task</code> or the add.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-check.set-position" data-param="position"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Or its 1-based place in tasqx_get_task&#39;s list.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-check.set-state" data-param="state"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">open | passed | failed.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-check.set-evidence" data-param="evidence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your proof: a test name, an excerpt of output, a commit sha. Optional — an invented citation is worse than an unproven <code>passed</code>.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">check_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion that moved.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its new state.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;cs1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;check.set&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;check_id&quot;:&quot;7e37a508-7921-4cb2-bf0c-0a2944eb31e4&quot;,&quot;state&quot;:&quot;passed&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;:&quot;docs/guides/sdk-3.0.md#rate-limits&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;cs1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;check_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;7e37a508-7921-4cb2-bf0c-0a2944eb31e4&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;state&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;passed&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_set_check"><code>tasqx_set_check</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;check_id&quot;:&quot;7e37a508-7921-4cb2-bf0c-0a2944eb31e4&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;:&quot;docs/guides/sdk-3.0.md#rate-limits&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;state&quot;:&quot;passed&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_set_check&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx check</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-check"><code>check</code></a> — Acceptance criteria on a task: add, mark, drop.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-check.remove"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-check.remove">check.remove</h3><p><code>{short_id, check_id, removed}</code>. For a criterion that was the wrong thing to ask; use <code>check.set failed</code> when the criterion was right and the work did not meet it. The check is named as on <code>check.set</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-check">Check</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-check.remove-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-check.remove-check-id" data-param="check_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">check_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The check&#39;s id.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-check.remove-position" data-param="position"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Or its 1-based place in tasqx_get_task&#39;s list.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">check_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion that was dropped.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Always true on success; an unknown id is <code>not_found</code> instead.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;cr1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;check.remove&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;check_id&quot;:&quot;e6a1096b-6f05-4e95-96f5-52452080f2ac&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;cr1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;check_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;e6a1096b-6f05-4e95-96f5-52452080f2ac&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;removed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_check"><code>tasqx_remove_check</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;check_id&quot;:&quot;e6a1096b-6f05-4e95-96f5-52452080f2ac&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_check&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx check</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-check"><code>check</code></a> — Acceptance criteria on a task: add, mark, drop.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-dependency-methods">Dependency methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-dependency.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-dependency.add">dependency.add</h3><p>Dep state + <code>blocked</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-dependency">Dependency</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-dependency.add-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-dependency.add-depends-on" data-param="depends_on"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task <code>ref</code> must wait for: short_id or UUID.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every short id this task now waits on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the task is blocked after the call.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">inserted</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">False when the edge was already there — a re-run told apart from a new edge.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;da1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;dependency.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;55&quot;,&quot;depends_on&quot;:&quot;50&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;da1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;blocked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;depends_on&quot;</span>: [
      <span class="j-n">50</span>
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;inserted&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">55</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_dependency"><code>tasqx_add_dependency</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;depends_on&quot;:&quot;50&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;55&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_dependency&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx dep</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-dep"><code>dep</code></a> — Make one task depend on another.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-dependency.remove"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-dependency.remove">dependency.remove</h3><p>Dep state + <code>blocked</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-dependency">Dependency</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-dependency.remove-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-dependency.remove-depends-on" data-param="depends_on"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocker to stop waiting for: short_id or UUID.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every short id this task still waits on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the task is still blocked — whether it is actionable now.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;dr1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;dependency.remove&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;depends_on&quot;:&quot;50&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;dr1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;blocked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;depends_on&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_dependency"><code>tasqx_remove_dependency</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;depends_on&quot;:&quot;50&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_dependency&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx undep</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-undep"><code>undep</code></a> — Remove a dependency edge.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-link-methods">Link methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-link.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-link.add">link.add</h3><p><code>{id, from, to, relation, metadata, created_at, created}</code> — one explicit edge of the knowledge graph (D160). <code>from</code> and <code>to</code> are NODE references: a task short id or uuid, a bare uuid, or <code>task:</code>/<code>memory:</code>/<code>annotation:</code>/<code>project:</code> plus an id (a project also by name), and they come back resolved as <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code>. <code>relation</code> is one of <code>references</code>, <code>supersedes</code>, <code>implements_decision</code>, <code>derived_from</code>, <code>contradicts</code>; anything else is refused by name. Adding the same from/to/relation twice is idempotent and answers <code>created: false</code> with the id the first call minted; a self-link is refused and a cycle is not. <code>expected_rev</code> guards the <code>from</code> endpoint when it has one (a task or a doc) and is ignored for an annotation or project, which carry no rev.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-link">Link</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-link.add-from" data-param="from"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">from</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link starts at. A task short id (`42`), a bare uuid (tried against tasks, memory docs, annotations and projects in that order), or `task:`/`memory:`/`annotation:`/`project:` plus an id — a project also by name (`project:work`). An unknown prefix is refused; a well-formed reference naming nothing is `not_found`.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-link.add-to" data-param="to"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">to</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link points at, in the same grammar as `from`. Linking a node to itself is refused; a cycle between two nodes is not — nothing schedules work off a link.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-link.add-relation" data-param="relation"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the link asserts: `references`, `supersedes`, `implements_decision`, `derived_from` or `contradicts`. Anything else is refused with the list, not stored.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-link.add-metadata" data-param="metadata"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">metadata</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your own object, stored verbatim and never interpreted. A repeat of an existing link never overwrites it.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-link.add-expected-rev" data-param="expected_rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">expected_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optimistic-concurrency guard on the `from` endpoint, mismatched a `conflict` naming both revs. Ignored when that endpoint is an annotation or a project, which carry no rev.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The link&#39;s uuid. On a duplicate this is the id the first call minted, not a new one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link starts at, as <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code> — the resolved form of whatever reference was sent.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">to</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link points at, spelled the same way.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The relation as stored, one of the five D160 fixes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">metadata</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The metadata this link carries, or null. On a duplicate it is what the FIRST call stored — a repeat never overwrites.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created_at</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the link was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">False when the link was already there, so a re-run is told apart from a new edge. Adding the same from/to/relation twice is idempotent, never an error.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;la1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;link.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;from&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;to&quot;:&quot;memory:eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;,&quot;relation&quot;:&quot;implements_decision&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;la1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;created_at&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-17T09:12:04Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;from&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:019f7c0a-3d51-7c42-9a08-1f0c4e5b62d7&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f8b31-77a4-7f10-8c55-2d7e9a13b004&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;metadata&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;relation&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;implements_decision&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;to&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;memory:eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> a new link mints a fresh v7 id whose low bits are random, and the response also carries the task&#39;s own uuid — the pinned clock fixes the timestamp half of each and nothing fixes the rest, so a captured answer would differ on every run.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>D160&#39;s explicit links are a curation surface: an agent proposing edges between docs, tasks and decisions is exactly the noise the graph&#39;s inferred half already covers without persisting anything. A link is durable and shows as fact, so it stays a human act until a promotion flow exists for an agent to ask for one.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-link.remove"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-link.remove">link.remove</h3><p><code>{id, removed}</code>. By the link's own id — removing one that is not there is <code>not_found</code>, not a no-op.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-link">Link</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-link.remove-id" data-param="id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The link's own uuid, as `link.add` and `link.list` report it.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The link that is gone.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Always true on success. Removing a link that is not there is <code>not_found</code>, not a no-op.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;lr1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;link.remove&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;019f8b31-77a4-7f10-8c55-2d7e9a13b004&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;lr1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f8b31-77a4-7f10-8c55-2d7e9a13b004&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;removed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> it echoes the link id it was given, and that id came from a <code>link.add</code> whose own answer cannot be captured — so a fixture here would pin a uuid no other example on this page can produce.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>the corrective half of <code>link.add</code>, off for the same reason: an agent that cannot write an edge has nothing of its own to retract, and deleting a human&#39;s curated link unsupervised is a bigger foot-gun than the gap it closes (<code>token.remove</code>&#39;s reasoning).</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-link.list"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-link.list">link.list</h3><p><code>{count, total, next_offset, links}</code> — the same paging shape as <code>task.list</code> (D70), newest first. <code>ref</code> is a node reference and matches EITHER endpoint, so a node's whole neighbourhood is one call; omit it to list the store's links. <code>relation</code> narrows to one of the five. An omitted <code>limit</code> defaults to 100 and a named one is clamped to 1,000.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-link">Link</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-link.list-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only links with this node at EITHER end, in `link.add`'s reference grammar. Omitted, the whole store's links come back.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-link.list-relation" data-param="relation"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only links asserting this relation. An unknown one is refused, not read as a filter matching nothing.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-link.list-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>100</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many links to return, newest first. Clamped to 1,000.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-link.list-offset" data-param="offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>0</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where the page starts. `next_offset` from the previous page keeps the walk going.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many links came back in this page.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many matched before <code>limit</code> and <code>offset</code> cut the page.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">next_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The offset that keeps walking, or null once nothing is left.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">links</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The links themselves, newest first. A <code>ref</code> matches EITHER endpoint, so a node&#39;s neighbourhood is one call.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.links[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The link&#39;s uuid — what <code>link.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link starts at, as <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code>: <code>task:</code>, <code>memory:</code>, <code>annotation:</code> or <code>project:</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">to</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link points at, spelled the same way.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the link asserts: <code>references</code>, <code>supersedes</code>, <code>implements_decision</code>, <code>derived_from</code> or <code>contradicts</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">metadata</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The caller&#39;s own object, stored verbatim and never interpreted, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created_at</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the link was written. Named <code>created_at</code> because <code>link.add</code> answers with a boolean <code>created</code> beside it.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ll1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;link.list&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ll1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;links&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;next_offset&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>nothing asks for it yet: an agent reaching the graph wants a node&#39;s neighbourhood with labels, which is <code>graph.query</code>&#39;s job, not a page of endpoint ids it would then have to resolve one by one.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-graph-methods">Graph methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-graph.query"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-graph.query">graph.query</h3><p><code>{root, depth, nodes, edges, node_count, edge_count, truncated, omitted_nodes, omitted_edges, include_inferred}</code> — one bounded projection of the knowledge graph around <code>root</code> (D160), which is a node reference in <code>link.add</code>'s grammar. Nodes come back ordered by depth, kind then id and edges by relation, <code>from</code> then <code>to</code>, so the same call twice is the same JSON. <code>depth</code> is 0–4 (default 2), <code>max_nodes</code> 1–1,000 (default 250) and <code>max_edges</code> 1–5,000 (default 750), each refused by name rather than clamped; <code>truncated</code> and the two omitted counts say when a cap bit. Every edge names its <code>kind</code> and <code>source</code>: <code>structural</code> for one read out of the store, <code>inferred</code> with a <code>confidence</code> for the <code>search_match</code> and <code>shared_tag</code> edges <code>include_inferred</code> computes and nothing stores.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-graph">Graph</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-root" data-param="root"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">root</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the projection is anchored at, in `link.add`'s reference grammar: a task short id (`42`), a bare uuid, or `task:`/`memory:`/`annotation:`/`project:` plus an id. It is returned resolved as `<type>:<uuid>`, and it is kept whatever the filters below say — a projection with no anchor in it has nothing to project from.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-depth" data-param="depth"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">depth</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>2</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many hops to walk, 0 to 4. Out of range is refused, never clamped: a caller who asked for 5 cannot tell a clamped answer from the graph really ending there.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-node-types" data-param="node_types"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">node_types</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Keep only these kinds of node: `task`, `memory`, `annotation`, `project`. A dropped node is not expanded either, so this bounds the cost as well as the answer. An empty array filters nothing.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-relation-types" data-param="relation_types"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">relation_types</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only cross these relations: `depends_on`, `has_annotation`, `belongs_to_project`, the five link relations, and `search_match`/`shared_tag` for the inferred ones. An unknown name is refused with the list. An empty array crosses every relation.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Keep only the nodes filed under this project — tasks and memory documents. A project node and the notes on a kept task pass through, because neither is filed anywhere of its own.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-status" data-param="status"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Keep only tasks in this status, read the way every other surface reads it (a future `wait` shows `backlog`). Nodes that are not tasks are unaffected.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-tags" data-param="tags"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tags</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Keep only tasks carrying at least one of these tags. Nodes that are not tasks are unaffected.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-modified-after" data-param="modified_after"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">modified_after</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">An RFC 3339 lower bound on a task's or document's `modified` and a note's `created`. A project carries no such date and is never excluded by the window.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-modified-before" data-param="modified_before"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">modified_before</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The upper bound of the same window, also RFC 3339.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-include-inferred" data-param="include_inferred"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_inferred</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>false</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Add the computed edges: up to ten `search_match` hits for the root's own title, and a `shared_tag` edge between every pair of returned tasks sharing a tag. Each carries a `confidence` and the `source` that produced it, and none of them is ever stored.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-max-nodes" data-param="max_nodes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">max_nodes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>250</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many nodes the answer may carry, 1 to 1,000. Applied to the deterministic order, so the cut is the same every time; `omitted_nodes` says how many went.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-graph.query-max-edges" data-param="max_edges"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">max_edges</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>750</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many edges the answer may carry, 1 to 5,000. Applied after the edges whose endpoints were cut have already gone; `omitted_edges` says how many were left out.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">root</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the projection is anchored at, resolved to its stable <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code> id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depth</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many hops were walked — the <code>depth</code> that was asked for, or 2.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">nodes</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The nodes, ordered by depth, then kind, then id. Deterministic: the same call twice is the same list.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">edges</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The edges, ordered by relation, then <code>from</code>, then <code>to</code>. Only edges with both endpoints among the nodes above.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">node_count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many nodes came back — the length of <code>nodes</code>, always present so a caller need not count.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">edge_count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many edges came back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether a cap bit, i.e. whether either omitted figure below is non-zero. A client that cannot tell a graph that ends from one that was cut draws the wrong picture.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">omitted_nodes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many nodes the walk found and <code>max_nodes</code> cut.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">omitted_edges</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many edges <code>max_edges</code> cut, after the ones whose endpoints were cut had already gone.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">include_inferred</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the computed edges were asked for, echoed so a cached answer says which kind of graph it is.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.nodes[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node&#39;s stable id, <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code> — the same spelling a link&#39;s endpoints use, and what a follow-up <code>graph.query</code> takes as its <code>root</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">type</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which kind of node: <code>task</code>, <code>memory</code>, <code>annotation</code> or <code>project</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">label</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The one line to draw in the box: a task&#39;s title, a document&#39;s title, a note&#39;s first line (cut to 80 characters) or a project&#39;s name.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">summary</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The second line: <code>#&lt;short_id&gt; · &lt;status&gt; · &lt;priority&gt;</code> for a task, the source for a document, the owning task for a note, the description for a project. Null when a project has no description.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project this node is filed under, or null — including on a project node, which is not filed under itself.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">A task&#39;s status, read the way every other surface reads it (a future <code>wait</code> shows <code>backlog</code>). Null on every other kind of node.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the node last changed: <code>modified</code> for a task or a document, <code>created</code> for a note, which is never edited. Null for a project, which carries no such column — so the date window cannot exclude one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The small number a human types for a task. Null on every other kind of node.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">task</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node id of the task a note is written on. Null on every other kind of node.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.edges[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The edge&#39;s id, stable for the same edge across calls: <code>dep:</code>, <code>ann:</code>, <code>member:</code> or <code>link:</code> for a stored one, <code>search:</code> or <code>tag:</code> for a computed one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node id the edge starts at. A <code>depends_on</code> edge always points from the task that waits to the one it waits on, whichever end the walk reached it from.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">to</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node id the edge points at.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the edge asserts: <code>depends_on</code>, <code>has_annotation</code>, <code>belongs_to_project</code>, one of the five link relations, or <code>search_match</code>/<code>shared_tag</code> when <code>include_inferred</code> asked for them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">kind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>structural</code> for an edge read out of a table, <code>inferred</code> for one computed for this call and never stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How strong a computed edge is, 0 to 1 within this answer. Null on a structural edge: a stored fact has no confidence to report.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where the edge came from: the table (<code>dependencies</code>, <code>annotations</code>, <code>tasks.project</code>, <code>docs.project</code>, <code>links</code>) or what computed it (<code>memory.search: &lt;words&gt;</code>, <code>tags: &lt;shared&gt;</code>).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;gq1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;graph.query&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;root&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;depth&quot;:1}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;gq1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;depth&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;edge_count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">6</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;edges&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;confidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;from&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;member:task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;kind&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;structural&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;relation&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;belongs_to_project&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;tasks.project&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;to&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;project:309d6b79-965e-4a32-9ae4-45508201e2bd&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;confidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;from&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:813547e2-5937-41f0-8401-82fcdb14a009&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;member:task:813547e2-5937-41f0-8401-82fcdb14a009&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;kind&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;structural&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;relation&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;belongs_to_project&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;tasks.project&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;to&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;project:309d6b79-965e-4a32-9ae4-45508201e2bd&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;confidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;from&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
