        <span class="j-k">&quot;task&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;type&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;annotation&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;annotation:ee4a9a3b-10de-465a-aab1-84eeb0e48236&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;label&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Blocked until the rate limit lands: the guide has to state the real ceiling, an…&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-15T11:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;summary&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;task&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;type&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;annotation&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;annotation:fd496ca3-cd12-4457-8b43-5ef0668cab3c&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;label&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Scope: the 2.x → 3.0 rename table, the auth change, and a worked example per SD…&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-04T11:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;summary&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;task&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;type&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;annotation&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;project:309d6b79-965e-4a32-9ae4-45508201e2bd&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;label&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;summary&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Public REST API and its SDKs&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;task&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;type&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;project&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;omitted_edges&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;omitted_nodes&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;root&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;truncated&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>an agent already reaches the graph&#39;s ends: <code>tasqx_search_memory</code> returns the docs and annotations the inferred half would match, and <code>tasqx_get_task</code> returns a task&#39;s notes, checks and dependencies. What <code>graph.query</code> adds over those is a LAYOUT — nodes, edges and provenance to draw — and that is a desktop client&#39;s question (D160), not something a model gains by reading two hundred node objects into its context.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-memory-methods">Memory methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-memory.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.add">memory.add</h3><p><code>{id, title, project, standing, created}</code>. Body stored verbatim (D41). <code>project</code> is optional free-standing scoping (#134); an unset doc stays global rather than defaulting onto whatever project is current. <code>standing</code> (default false) marks a ruling meant for every session of its scope, and above fifteen such docs in one scope the result also carries a <code>hint</code> to merge or retract (D156).</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.add-title" data-param="title"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc's title. Indexed with the body, so the words a future search will use belong in it.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.add-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Stored verbatim; multi-line markdown is fine.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.add-source" data-param="source"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where this came from: a path, URL, or ticket. One doc per source: one another doc holds is a <code>conflict</code> naming it (D174).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.add-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional project scope. Omit to leave the doc unscoped; it is never defaulted onto a current project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.add-standing" data-param="standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">True marks a ruling that belongs in every session of its scope until retracted; default false (D156).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The new doc&#39;s uuid — what a search hit carries and <code>memory.get</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s title, as stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the doc is scoped to, or null for a global one (#134).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the doc was stored as a standing ruling — one meant for every session of its scope (D156).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">hint</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present only when this add pushed its scope past the soft cap on standing docs: a nudge to merge or retract one. Test for the key, not its value (D156).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ma1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;rate-limit-ceiling&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;60 requests a minute per key, burst 120.&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;notes/limits.md&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;api&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ma1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7b18-8d44-6e1a92c07f35&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;rate-limit-ceiling&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the doc&#39;s id is minted fresh, v7, half of it random.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_memory"><code>tasqx_add_memory</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;60 requests a minute per key, burst 120.&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;api&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;notes/limits.md&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;rate-limit-ceiling&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-memory.search"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.search">memory.search</h3><p><code>{count, total, has_more, hits, matched, relaxed}</code> — bm25-ranked over docs + annotations, stemmed (porter tokenizer, #128) so "reviewing" matches a doc that only says "review". <code>matched</code> is the FTS5 expression actually run, which is how <code>count: 0</code> is told apart from a store holding nothing on the subject. A plain query requires every word first; when nothing holds them all, the same words joined with OR answer instead, and <code>relaxed</code> is true (D193). <code>total</code> is every row matched before <code>limit</code> truncates (#132), and <code>project</code> scopes to one project's docs plus its tasks' annotations (#134). Each hit carries its own <code>project</code> too (null for global knowledge, #657), so a store-wide search says which project it came from.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.search-query" data-param="query"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">query</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Plain-text search words. Matched as quoted phrases, so hyphens and dots are safe.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.search-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Max hits (0 or more); default 10. The response&#39;s <code>total</code>/<code>has_more</code> say what this left out.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.search-scope" data-param="scope"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">scope</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What to search. Optional; defaults to all.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.search-raw" data-param="raw"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">raw</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Pass the query through as FTS5 syntax. Invalid syntax is refused as bad_request.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.search-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Scope to one project: docs stored with it, and annotations whose task carries it. Omit to search every project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.search-include-unscoped" data-param="include_unscoped"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_unscoped</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Widen a <code>project</code> scope to docs and annotations with NO project — what <code>tasqx memory import</code> produces. Never admits another project&#39;s. Refused without <code>project</code>.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many hits came back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many rows matched before <code>limit</code> truncated (#132).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">has_more</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether anything was left behind.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">hits</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The hits, bm25-ranked, docs and annotations together.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">matched</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The FTS5 expression actually run — how <code>count: 0</code> is told apart from a store holding nothing on the subject.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">relaxed</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether no hit had every word of a plain query, so the words were joined with OR instead and <code>matched</code> is that OR (D193). Always false for <code>raw</code>.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.hits[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s id, or the annotation&#39;s.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">kind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>doc</code> or <code>annotation</code> — which store the hit came from.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s title; for an annotation, the task it is written on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where the doc came from (a file path, <code>task:#51</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">snippet</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The matching passage, with the hit in context. Never the whole body.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rank</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The bm25 score. Lower is a better match; the number itself is not comparable between searches.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">For a doc hit, whether it is a standing ruling (D156); null on an annotation hit, which has no such flag.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which project this hit is scoped to — a doc&#39;s own column, or the annotation&#39;s task&#39;s — or null for global knowledge (#657).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">stale</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">true when the doc&#39;s origin file no longer matches what was imported; null for annotations and docs with no origin (D180).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ms1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.search&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;query&quot;:&quot;release canary&quot;,&quot;limit&quot;:2}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ms1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;has_more&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;hits&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;kind&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;doc&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;rank&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">-1.2419537228757</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;snippet&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Cut the release branch on Monday, tag after the canary has run for a day…&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/release.md&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;stale&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;release-process&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;matched&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;release AND canary&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;relaxed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> every hit carries an FTS bm25 <code>rank</code> whose last digits are the platform&#39;s <code>log()</code>, so a capture is reproducible only on the machine that took it. The <code>tasqx memory search</code> screen is captured instead — it prints the snippet, never the number.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_search_memory"><code>tasqx_search_memory</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;limit&quot;:2,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;release canary&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_search_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-memory.get"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.get">memory.get</h3><p><code>{id, title, body, source, project, rev, created, modified}</code> — one doc whole, by the id a search hit carries. An annotation id is refused, naming the task to read it from.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.get-id" data-param="id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc UUID, as a search hit or <code>tasqx_add_memory</code> prints it.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it came from — the path <code>memory.import</code> keyed on, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s title.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The whole body, stored and returned verbatim (D41).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was first stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project it is scoped to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The row&#39;s revision counter, bumped by every write. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether it is a standing ruling, meant for every session of its scope (D156). Stated on every doc, so a restore carries it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The absolute path of the file <code>memory.import</code> read this doc from, or null when no import set one (D180).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_mtime</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That file&#39;s modification time in unix seconds when it was read, or null (D180).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_size</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That file&#39;s size in bytes when it was read, or null (D180).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mg1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.get&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mg1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;---\ndescription: How an SDK release is cut, tagged and announced\n---\nCut the release branch on Monday, tag after the canary has run for a day, and announce in the changelog feed once the packages are live.&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-05T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-10T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_mtime&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_path&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_size&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/release.md&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;release-process&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_memory"><code>tasqx_get_memory</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_get_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-memory.remove"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.remove">memory.remove</h3><p><code>{id, removed}</code>.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.remove-id" data-param="id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The document&#39;s id, as tasqx_search_memory reports it on a <code>doc</code> hit.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc that is gone.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Always true on success. Removal is permanent and outside <code>undo</code>.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mr1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.remove&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;091eb5ff-05d5-4cb2-ba2f-0afdc77f7935&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mr1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;091eb5ff-05d5-4cb2-ba2f-0afdc77f7935&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;removed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_memory"><code>tasqx_remove_memory</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;091eb5ff-05d5-4cb2-ba2f-0afdc77f7935&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-memory.import"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.import">memory.import</h3><p><code>{imported, replaced, docs}</code>, each doc <code>{id, title, source, project, replaced, _rev}</code>. One transaction; same <code>source</code> replaces IN PLACE (id and creation date kept), bumps that doc's <code>_rev</code> (D143) and is counted in <code>replaced</code>; a batch naming one <code>source</code> twice is refused whole (D174). <code>project</code> scopes every doc in the batch (#657): omitted, an existing doc keeps its prior scope (like <code>standing</code>) and a new one lands global; named, it moves an existing doc's scope on re-import, the same way <code>memory.update --project</code> would.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.import-docs" data-param="docs"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">docs</code><span class="badge">array of object</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The documents to store, each `{title, body, source?}`. One transaction: same `source` replaces in place, keeping the doc's id and creation date (D143); a batch naming one `source` twice is refused whole (D174). A doc may also carry `origin_path` (the absolute path of the file it was read from), `origin_mtime` (that file's modification time in unix seconds) and `origin_size` (its size in bytes) — all optional, stored as given and overwritten on every re-import, never used as identity (D180).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.import-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Scopes every doc in the batch (#657) — one value for the whole import, not per-doc. Omitted, a new doc lands global and an existing one (a re-import) keeps whatever scope it already had, like `standing`; named, it MOVES an existing doc's scope on re-import.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">imported</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many docs the batch stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">replaced</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many of those replaced a doc with the same <code>source</code>, in place.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">docs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One row per document in the batch.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.docs[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s id — the one it already had when it was replaced in place.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its title.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The source it was keyed on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The batch&#39;s <code>project</code>, echoed per doc — null when the import named none (#657).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">replaced</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether this row replaced an existing doc rather than creating one (D143).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The row&#39;s revision counter, bumped by every write. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mi1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.import&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;docs&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;release-process&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Cut the release branch on Monday.&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;docs/release.md&quot;}]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mi1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;docs&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;replaced&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/release.md&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;release-process&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;imported&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;replaced&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>it takes a batch of documents read off a filesystem, and the filesystem the CLI          reads is not the one an MCP client is on. <code>memory.add</code> is the per-document tool          that does reach across the wire.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-memory.refresh"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.refresh">memory.refresh</h3><p><code>{checked, refreshed, missing, unchanged}</code> — re-reads every doc that recorded an origin file (D180) whose file has changed since, through the same upsert a re-import uses: id and creation date kept, <code>rev</code> bumped (D143), <code>project</code> and <code>standing</code> left alone. Stored mtime and size are the fast filter and the bytes are the truth, so a <code>touch</code> counts as <code>unchanged</code>. A doc whose file cannot be read is listed under <code>missing</code> and left exactly as it is — nothing is ever deleted. <code>dry_run</code> reports the same answer and writes nothing.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.refresh-dry-run" data-param="dry_run"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">dry_run</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>false</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Check every doc and report, without writing anything. The same answer the real sweep would give — which docs would be re-read, which files are gone — so it can be looked at before a store full of documents is rewritten.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">checked</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many docs named an origin file and were examined. <code>refreshed</code>, <code>missing</code> and <code>unchanged</code> account for all of them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">refreshed</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The docs whose file had changed and were re-read from it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">missing</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The docs whose file could not be read — gone, renamed, or on a volume that is not mounted. Reported, never removed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unchanged</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many docs still matched their file, byte for byte, and were left alone — their <code>rev</code> did not move.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.refreshed[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s id, unchanged — a refresh replaces the text in place.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The source it is keyed on, or null for a doc that has an origin file and no source.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.missing[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc, still stored with the text it already had.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The source it is keyed on, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The file that could not be read, as the import recorded it (D180).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mf1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.refresh&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;dry_run&quot;:true}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mf1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;checked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">3</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;missing&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;091eb5ff-05d5-4cb2-ba2f-0afdc77f7935&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_path&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;/home/you/repo/docs/retired.md&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/retired.md&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;refreshed&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/release.md&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;unchanged&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the answer is whatever the files under the store&#39;s own imports look like right now, so a captured one would describe the capturing machine&#39;s disk rather than the method.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>the sweep re-reads the files <code>memory.import</code> recorded on THIS machine (D180), and the filesystem an MCP client is on is not that one — <code>memory.import</code>&#39;s own reason, one method over. Keeping a server&#39;s own docs fresh is the server&#39;s job, reached by calling the engine, not an agent&#39;s to trigger across the wire.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-memory.list"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.list">memory.list</h3><p><code>{count, total, next_offset, docs}</code> — the same paging shape as <code>task.list</code> (#133). Browses docs newest-modified first, without a query; each row carries a <code>body_preview</code>, not the full body, and a <code>standing</code> flag; <code>standing</code> filters to only standing docs (<code>true</code>) or only the rest (<code>false</code>), omitted for all (D156).</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.list-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Rows to return; default 20, because an unbounded browse page grows with the store.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.list-offset" data-param="offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Matching docs to skip; pass the previous response&#39;s <code>next_offset</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.list-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Restrict to docs stored with this <code>project</code>. Omit to list every doc.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.list-standing" data-param="standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">true lists only standing docs, false only the rest; omit for all (D156).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many docs came back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many docs the scope holds.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">next_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The <code>offset</code> that fetches the next page; null once nothing is left.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">docs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The docs, newest-modified first.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.docs[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its title.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it came from, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project it is scoped to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed — the column this list sorts by.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The row&#39;s revision counter, bumped by every write. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_preview</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The opening of the body, or all of it when the body is short (<code>body_truncated</code> says which) — browsing pays for a preview, not a payload.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the preview is shorter than the body.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether it is a standing ruling (D156) — on every row, not only on a page filtered by <code>standing</code>.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;m1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.list&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;m1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">5</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;docs&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_preview&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;# Pricing page\nThree tiers, annual billing shown first. The release of v2 waits for legal to sign off the new terms.&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_truncated&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-09T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;0787b26d-9e2e-4be5-ab66-ec953102fad3&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-14T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;notes/pricing.md&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pricing-page-decisions&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_preview&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;---\ndescription: How an SDK release is cut, tagged and announced\n---\nCut the release branch on Monday, tag after the canary has run for a day, and announce in t&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_truncated&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-05T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-10T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/release.md&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;release-process&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_preview&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;The handover happens Friday at 16:00. Walk the open incidents, the error budget and anything paged twice in the week, then rotate the pager.&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_truncated&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-29T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1bce1a9b-5134-4ab7-8665-34cd79fe0c5f&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-03T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;infra&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;on-call-handover&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_preview&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;The refresh race happens when two requests see an expired token at once. Serialise refresh behind one lock and retry the losing request.&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_truncated&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-22T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;b3bd4390-2124-42ac-829d-f542ecde8a07&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-27T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mobile&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;android-token-refresh&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_preview&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Dr. Visser, Tuesdays and Thursdays, book two weeks ahead.&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body_truncated&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-08T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;091eb5ff-05d5-4cb2-ba2f-0afdc77f7935&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-13T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;dentist&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;next_offset&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">5</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_memory"><code>tasqx_list_memory</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_list_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-memory.update"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-memory.update">memory.update</h3><p><code>{id, title, source, project, standing, rev, modified}</code> — replaces a doc's fields IN PLACE (#135), the correction path <code>memory.remove</code>'s permanence has none of. <code>standing</code> sets or clears the flag and bumps <code>rev</code> like any other edit (D156). <code>expected_rev</code> is <code>task.modify</code>'s optimistic-concurrency guard, unchanged: mismatched, it is a <code>conflict</code> naming both revs.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-memory.update-id" data-param="id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc UUID, as a search hit, <code>tasqx_add_memory</code> or <code>tasqx_list_memory</code> prints it.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.update-title" data-param="title"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New title. Omit to leave unchanged.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.update-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New body, stored verbatim. Omit to leave unchanged.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.update-source" data-param="source"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New source. Omit to leave unchanged. One another doc holds is a <code>conflict</code> naming it (D174).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.update-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New project scope. Omit to leave unchanged.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.update-standing" data-param="standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Set or clear the standing flag; omit to leave unchanged (D156).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-memory.update-expected-rev" data-param="expected_rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">expected_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optimistic-concurrency guard. Supplied by the server from the doc&#39;s current <code>rev</code> when omitted; pass it to pin a rev you read earlier.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc that changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its title after the update.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its source after the update, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its project after the update, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The standing flag as it now stands, whether this call set it, cleared it or left it alone (D156).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The row&#39;s revision counter, bumped by every write. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the update landed.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mu1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;memory.update&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;1bce1a9b-5134-4ab7-8665-34cd79fe0c5f&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;The handover happens Friday at 16:00, in the on-call channel.&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mu1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1bce1a9b-5134-4ab7-8665-34cd79fe0c5f&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;infra&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;on-call-handover&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_update_memory"><code>tasqx_update_memory</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;The handover happens Friday at 16:00, in the on-call channel.&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;1bce1a9b-5134-4ab7-8665-34cd79fe0c5f&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_update_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx memory</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a> — Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-token-methods">Token methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-token.add"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-token.add">token.add</h3><p><code>{short_id, measurement}</code>. Records AI token spend; never bumps <code>_rev</code>. <code>total_tokens</code> is one unsplit count, refused beside the split four (D167); a missing required field is refused together with every other one missing. A repeated <code>idempotency_key</code> on the same task returns the measurement it already banked, unchanged.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-measurement">Token measurement</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-token.add-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-tool" data-param="tool"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The AI tool that spent them; defaults to the handshake&#39;s client.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-source" data-param="source"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How the figure was obtained: `self-report`, `log-parse` or `otel`. It is what `confidence` is graded against.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-model" data-param="model"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work. Recorded, never interpreted.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-input-tokens" data-param="input_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>0</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-output-tokens" data-param="output_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>0</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-cache-read-tokens" data-param="cache_read_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>0</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache. Kept in its own bucket and never blended with the others (D48).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-cache-creation-tokens" data-param="cache_creation_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>0</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-total-tokens" data-param="total_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, instead of the four.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-confidence" data-param="confidence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">confidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How checkable the figure is: `medium` or `low` for a self-report — `high` is refused, because confidence describes verifiability and not preference (D50).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-token.add-idempotency-key" data-param="idempotency_key"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">idempotency_key</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The same key twice on one task banks once.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">measurement</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement as banked. A repeated <code>idempotency_key</code> returns the one already stored, unchanged.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.measurement</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement&#39;s uuid — what <code>token.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which tool spent the tokens (<code>claude-code</code>, <code>codex</code>, …).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How the figure was obtained: <code>self-report</code>, <code>log-parse</code> or <code>otel</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache — never blended with the others (D48).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How checkable the figure is: <code>high</code>, <code>medium</code> or <code>low</code>. A self-report may not claim <code>high</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the measurement was banked.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, from a reporter that could not split it — 0 on a split measurement, and never folded into the four (D167).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;tk1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;token.add&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;tool&quot;:&quot;claude-code&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;self-report&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;opus&quot;,&quot;input_tokens&quot;:18400,&quot;output_tokens&quot;:2600,&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;:91000,&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;:12000,&quot;confidence&quot;:&quot;medium&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;tk1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;measurement&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">12000</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">91000</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;confidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;medium&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7d22-b73c-9353de0a3360&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;input_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">18400</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;model&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;opus&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;output_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2600</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;self-report&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;tool&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;claude-code&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;total_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the measurement&#39;s id is minted fresh, v7, half of it random.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_tokens"><code>tasqx_add_tokens</code></a> — write scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;:12000,&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;:91000,&quot;confidence&quot;:&quot;medium&quot;,&quot;input_tokens&quot;:18400,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;opus&quot;,&quot;output_tokens&quot;:2600,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;self-report&quot;,&quot;tool&quot;:&quot;claude-code&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_tokens&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tokens</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-tokens"><code>tokens</code></a> — Record token spend after the fact, or repair stored attribution (D50, D167).</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-token.remove"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-token.remove">token.remove</h3><p><code>{short_id, removed}</code>. Deletes one measurement by id — the correction path a wrong self-report otherwise has none of (D50, D67; #210). <code>removed</code> is the measurement object that is now gone.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-measurement">Token measurement</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-token.remove-measurement-id" data-param="measurement_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">measurement_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement to delete, by the id `token.add` handed back. There is no `ref`: a measurement id is globally unique.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement that is now gone — the same object <code>token.add</code> hands back (#210).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.removed</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement&#39;s uuid — what <code>token.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which tool spent the tokens (<code>claude-code</code>, <code>codex</code>, …).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How the figure was obtained: <code>self-report</code>, <code>log-parse</code> or <code>otel</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache — never blended with the others (D48).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How checkable the figure is: <code>high</code>, <code>medium</code> or <code>low</code>. A self-report may not claim <code>high</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the measurement was banked.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, from a reporter that could not split it — 0 on a split measurement, and never folded into the four (D167).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;tr1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;token.remove&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;measurement_id&quot;:&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7d22-b73c-9353de0a3360&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;tr1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;removed&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">12000</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">91000</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;confidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;medium&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7d22-b73c-9353de0a3360&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;input_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">18400</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;model&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;opus&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;output_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2600</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;self-report&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;tool&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;claude-code&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;total_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> it deletes a measurement by id, and the only measurement to delete is one a previous call just minted — so the request itself quotes an id no fixture can pin.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>the corrective half of <code>token.add</code> (#210), kept off although its other half is <code>tasqx_add_tokens</code> (D167): an agent that reports a wrong count fixes it by reporting the right one, and a removal an agent could reach unsupervised on the ledger a lead reads for budget decisions is a bigger foot-gun than the gap it closes. A human runs <code>tasqx api token.remove</code> instead.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-tokens.recompute"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-tokens.recompute">tokens.recompute</h3><p><code>{dry_run, tasks, totals}</code>. Re-runs log-parse attribution over stored windows under the refusal rule (D50). <code>dry_run</code> defaults to <em>true</em> — report the per-task delta, write nothing; send <code>false</code> to apply. In-process only: a daemon refuses this method over the socket, so stop any daemon on the store first.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-measurement">Token measurement</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-tokens.recompute-dry-run" data-param="dry_run"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">dry_run</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>true</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Report the per-task delta and write nothing. Send `false` to apply it — this is the one method that deletes measurement rows.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">dry_run</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether this run wrote anything. Defaults to true: report the delta, change nothing.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tasks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One row per task whose attribution would change.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">totals</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The whole-store totals, before and after.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">task</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">action</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the pass would do to it: <code>insert</code>, <code>update</code> or <code>delete</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">before</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The four buckets as they stand.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">after</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The four buckets the pass computed.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[].before</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[].after</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.totals</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">before</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Total attributed tokens before the pass.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">after</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Total attributed tokens after it.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;rc1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tokens.recompute&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;rc1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;dry_run&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tasks&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;totals&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;after&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;before&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>
    }
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>a maintenance pass over the whole store&#39;s attribution. It is an operator action with          a runtime proportional to history, not a step in anybody&#39;s task.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx tokens</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-tokens"><code>tokens</code></a> — Record token spend after the fact, or repair stored attribution (D50, D167).</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-report-methods">Report methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-report.summary"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-report.summary">report.summary</h3><p><code>{groups, generated, filter, all, since, until}</code>. <code>group_by</code> defaults to <code>project</code>; the result echoes the scope it applied, so a total cannot be read against the wrong period. <code>since</code>/<code>until</code> (D97) window <code>tracked_total</code> and the token buckets by WHEN the time or spend happened — a different axis from <code>filter</code>'s <code>completed.after:</code>/<code>completed.before:</code>, which selects tasks by completion date; both are <code>null</code> unless the caller sets them.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-report.summary-group-by" data-param="group_by"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">group_by</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.summary-filter" data-param="filter"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional filter DSL to scope the report.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.summary-metrics" data-param="metrics"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">metrics</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Extra columns per group. Omit and each group carries only <code>count</code>: every other metric is opt-in here, unlike <code>tasqx report</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.summary-all" data-param="all"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">all</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Count cancelled tasks too. By default a report with no status term skips cancelled only — done work always counts (D24).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.summary-since" data-param="since"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Window <code>tracked_total</code> and the token buckets to spend at or after this instant, not the task&#39;s lifetime total — a different axis from <code>filter</code>&#39;s <code>completed.*</code> terms (D97).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.summary-until" data-param="until"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">until</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The other end of <code>since</code>: excludes anything at or after this instant. Together they window WHEN the spend happened.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">groups</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One row per group, on the axis <code>group_by</code> named.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">generated</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the report was computed — the time of the call, not the window.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The filter this total was taken over, echoed so it cannot be read against the wrong scope (D69).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">all</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether cancelled work was counted (D24).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens_excluded_cancelled_tasks</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many cancelled tasks carrying token spend the default just excluded.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The start of the time window, or null when the caller set none (D97).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">until</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The end of that window, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">store_empty</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the store has ever held a task at all — how &quot;nothing yet&quot; is told apart from &quot;nothing matched&quot;.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The group key — named by <code>group_by</code>, so this column is <code>project</code>, <code>status</code> or <code>priority</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many tasks fell in this group.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">est_total</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Their estimates summed, as an ISO duration. Only when <code>metrics</code> names it — the default is <code>count</code> alone.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">overdue</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many of them are past due. Only when <code>metrics</code> names it.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;r1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;report.summary&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;group_by&quot;:&quot;project&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;r1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;all&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;filter&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;generated&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;groups&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">9</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;home&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">11</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;infra&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">16</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;mobile&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">17</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;since&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;store_empty&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tokens_excluded_cancelled_tasks&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;until&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_summary"><code>tasqx_summary</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;group_by&quot;:&quot;project&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_summary&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx dashboard</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> — Open the overview screen, or ask for its panels as data.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a> — Summary counts, or outcomes, optionally grouped, as text or HTML.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-report.outcomes"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-report.outcomes">report.outcomes</h3><p><code>{groups, group_by, metrics, generated, filter, since, until, store_empty}</code>. What the work DID, as against what it cost (D137): <code>rework</code> (completions that were reopened), <code>calibration</code> (median tracked-over-estimate), <code>cost</code> (the four token buckets, never blended), <code>silent</code> (completions carrying no annotation), <code>abandonment</code> (started, then cancelled) and <code>forced</code> (completions that overrode open blockers, D150). Every rate comes back beside the <code>n</code> it was computed over. Scope is tasks that CLOSED, by the instant they closed — so a completion that was reopened still counts, which is the whole point. Omitting <code>metrics</code> emits all of them; there is no <code>all</code>, because here a cancellation is a measured outcome rather than noise D24 excludes.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-report.outcomes-group-by" data-param="group_by"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">group_by</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.outcomes-filter" data-param="filter"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional filter DSL to scope the report — <code>tasqx_list_tasks</code>&#39; grammar.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.outcomes-metrics" data-param="metrics"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">metrics</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which metrics to emit. Omit for ALL of them; naming none does not mean a bare count here.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.outcomes-since" data-param="since"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only count tasks that closed at or after this instant. <code>since</code>/<code>until</code> window WHEN THE TASK CLOSED, not when spend happened.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-report.outcomes-until" data-param="until"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">until</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The other end of <code>since</code>: excludes tasks that closed at or after this instant.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">groups</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One row per group, each metric beside the <code>n</code> it was computed over.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">group_by</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The axis the rows are grouped on, echoed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">metrics</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The metrics computed. Omitting <code>metrics</code> on the request emits all of them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">generated</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the report was computed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The filter applied, echoed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The start of the window over when tasks CLOSED, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">until</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The end of that window, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">store_empty</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the store has ever held a task at all — how &quot;nothing yet&quot; is told apart from &quot;nothing matched&quot;.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The group key, named by <code>group_by</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completions</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many tasks completed in the window.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">closed</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many closed — completions plus cancellations.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rework</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Completions that were later reopened.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">calibration</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tracked time over estimate, as a median.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cost</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The four token buckets, never blended.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">silent</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Completions carrying no annotation — work that left no record of what it decided.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">abandonment</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Work that was started and then cancelled, with the time inside it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">overrun</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Completions that went past their <code>budget_tokens</code> (D139).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unproven</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Completions whose acceptance criteria were not all passed (D138).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">forced</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Completions that overrode still-open blockers (D150).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].rework</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many occurrences.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rate</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>count</code> over <code>n</code>; null rather than zero when there was nothing to divide by.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">refs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids behind the count, so a number can be opened.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].calibration</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">median_ratio</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Median tracked-over-estimate. Null when nothing in the group carried both.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].cost</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens_in</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens across the group.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens_out</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens_cache_read</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cache reads.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens_cache_creation</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cache writes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens_unsplit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Unsplit <code>total_tokens</code> counts, summed apart from the four (D167).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How checkable the figures are. Absent — not null — when nothing was measured, because there is nothing to grade.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].silent</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many occurrences.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rate</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>count</code> over <code>n</code>; null rather than zero when there was nothing to divide by.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">refs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids behind the count, so a number can be opened.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].abandonment</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many started tasks were then cancelled.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rate</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>count</code> over <code>n</code>, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_total</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The time spent inside the abandoned work — how much, not only how many.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">refs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids behind the count.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].overrun</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many occurrences.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rate</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>count</code> over <code>n</code>; null rather than zero when there was nothing to divide by.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">refs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids behind the count, so a number can be opened.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].unproven</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many occurrences.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rate</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>count</code> over <code>n</code>; null rather than zero when there was nothing to divide by.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">refs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids behind the count, so a number can be opened.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.groups[].forced</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many occurrences.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">n</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The denominator this rate was computed over. A rate never travels without it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">rate</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>count</code> over <code>n</code>; null rather than zero when there was nothing to divide by.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">refs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids behind the count, so a number can be opened.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ro1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;report.outcomes&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;group_by&quot;:&quot;project&quot;,&quot;metrics&quot;:[&quot;rework&quot;,&quot;calibration&quot;]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ro1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;filter&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;&quot;</span>,
