          <span class="j-k">&quot;n&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">9</span>
        },
        <span class="j-k">&quot;closed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">15</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;completions&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">13</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;rework&quot;</span>: {
          <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;n&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">13</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;rate&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0.0</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;refs&quot;</span>: []
        }
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;metrics&quot;</span>: [
      <span class="j-s">&quot;rework&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-s">&quot;calibration&quot;</span>
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;since&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;store_empty&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;until&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><a href="#mcp-tasqx_outcomes"><code>tasqx_outcomes</code></a> — read scope.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;group_by&quot;:&quot;project&quot;,&quot;metrics&quot;:[&quot;rework&quot;,&quot;calibration&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_outcomes&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The tool hands back this method's result in a text block — or, where its own description says so, less of it by default: a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code>. What it sends and how to ask for the rest is <a href="#mcp">documented with the tool</a>.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx report</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-report"><code>report</code></a> — Summary counts, or outcomes, optionally grouped, as text or HTML.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-store-methods">Store methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-store.export"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-store.export">store.export</h3><p><code>{tasks, projects, dropped_projects, docs, dropped_docs, links, dropped_links, events, dropped_events, default_project, dropped_dependencies}</code>. <code>events</code> is the whole audit log except the bookkeeping rows a `store.import` itself writes. An unfiltered export carries every project/doc/link/event (D12); any other filter scopes those four to what the exported tasks need and reports what it dropped (D171, D181) — <code>include_unscoped</code> widens that scope back to docs with no project. A link travels only when BOTH its ends are nodes the document carries.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a> · <a href="#obj-project">Project</a> · <a href="#obj-annotation">Annotation</a> · <a href="#obj-check">Check</a> · <a href="#obj-dependency">Dependency</a> · <a href="#obj-memory">Memory document</a> · <a href="#obj-link">Link</a> · <a href="#obj-event">Event</a> · <a href="#obj-measurement">Token measurement</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-store.export-filter" data-param="filter"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">A filter-DSL query narrowing which tasks are exported. Omitted, the whole store comes back — and so do every project, every doc and the whole event log (D12). Any other filter also scopes `projects`/`docs`/`events` to what the exported tasks need (D171).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.export-include-unscoped" data-param="include_unscoped"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_unscoped</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>false</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Widen a filtered export's `docs`/`projects` to ones that carry no project at all. Refused with no `filter` — an unfiltered export already carries everything, so there is nothing to widen from (D171).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tasks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every task in scope, whole: fields, tags, notes, criteria, edges and measurements.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">dropped_dependencies</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many dependency edges pointed outside the filtered slice and were dropped.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">projects</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every project this document needs: all of them on an unfiltered export, or the ones named by the filter or by an exported task on a filtered one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">dropped_projects</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many project rows a filtered export left out because nothing exported named them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">docs</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every memory doc this document needs, scoped like <code>projects</code>; an unscoped doc ships only with <code>include_unscoped</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">dropped_docs</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many memory docs a filtered export left out, scoped or unscoped.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">links</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every explicit link (D160) whose BOTH ends are nodes this document carries — the same row <code>link.list</code> pages.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">dropped_links</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many links a filtered export left out because one of their ends is a node this document does not carry.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">events</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The whole audit log for what this document carries, minus the bookkeeping rows an import itself writes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">dropped_events</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many events a filtered export left out because they belong to a task, doc, project or link this document does not carry.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default_project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The store&#39;s default project, or null — also null when a filtered export did not carry it among <code>projects</code>.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s uuid, stable across exports and machines.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>pending</code>, <code>backlog</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>cancelled</code> — or, on a stored row whose status text this build does not recognize, that text verbatim, with <code>status_unrecognized: true</code> beside it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">priority</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>H</code>, <code>M</code>, <code>L</code>, or null for none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the task belongs to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it is due, as an instant, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When work is planned to start, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>, out of the working set, as with <code>wait</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">wait</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Holds the task out of the working set until this instant, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The estimate as an ISO 8601 duration (<code>PT4H</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The recurrence rule (<code>every 3 days</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">remind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The reminder spec — an offset from <code>due</code> or an absolute instant — or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The urgency score (D1): priority, due proximity and age, summed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every tag on the task, as plain strings.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the task was captured.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When <code>task.done</code> completed it, or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it, and <code>task.cancel</code> does not set it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">budget_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The size gauge over FRESH tokens (D139), or null for no threshold. It stops nothing.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter. The methods that change the task or its tags, notes, checks and dependencies bump it; <code>token.add</code>, <code>token.remove</code> and <code>reminder.fire</code> leave it alone. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_seconds</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tracked time in raw seconds (D42). Omitted when it would be zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_adjustment_seconds</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The signed net of the <code>task.adjust_tracked</code> corrections inside <code>tracked_seconds</code> (D166). Omitted when it would be zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">active_since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The open interval&#39;s anchor, omitted when no timer is running.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note <code>task.done</code> pinned as the delivery note (D165). Present only on a task a completion pinned one on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every token measurement against this task. Omitted entirely for a task that has none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this task waits on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every note on the task — an export carries the whole history, unpaged.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status_unrecognized</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present, and true, only on a row whose <code>status</code> no writer of this build could have produced — a store an older import wrote unvalidated, or a hand-edited one. <code>store.import</code> now refuses such a status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">checks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The acceptance criteria on the task, in position order (D138).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">spawned_from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The uuid of the task whose completion spawned this one (D170). Omitted on any other task.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[].tokens[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement&#39;s uuid — what <code>token.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which tool spent the tokens (<code>claude-code</code>, <code>codex</code>, …).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How the figure was obtained: <code>self-report</code>, <code>log-parse</code> or <code>otel</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache — never blended with the others (D48).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How checkable the figure is: <code>high</code>, <code>medium</code> or <code>low</code>. A self-report may not claim <code>high</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the measurement was banked.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, from a reporter that could not split it — 0 on a split measurement, and never folded into the four (D167).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[].annotations[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.tasks[].checks[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion&#39;s uuid — what <code>check.set</code> and <code>check.remove</code> take.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion itself, stored verbatim. tasqx never runs it; it is a claim, not a command.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>open</code>, <code>passed</code> or <code>failed</code>. A failure is a normal outcome, not an error.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The citation for the state, or null — some criteria are met by something nobody can quote.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it sits in the list, from zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the criterion was added.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When its state or evidence last changed.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.projects[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its name — what a task&#39;s <code>project</code> names.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">description</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its description, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">archived</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether it is archived.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was created.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.docs[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it came from — the path <code>memory.import</code> keyed on, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s title.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The whole body, stored and returned verbatim (D41).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was first stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project it is scoped to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The row&#39;s revision counter, bumped by every write. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether it is a standing ruling, meant for every session of its scope (D156). Stated on every doc, so a restore carries it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The absolute path of the file <code>memory.import</code> read this doc from, or null when no import set one (D180).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_mtime</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That file&#39;s modification time in unix seconds when it was read, or null (D180).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_size</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That file&#39;s size in bytes when it was read, or null (D180).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.links[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The link&#39;s uuid — what <code>link.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link starts at, as <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code>: <code>task:</code>, <code>memory:</code>, <code>annotation:</code> or <code>project:</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">to</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link points at, spelled the same way.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the link asserts: <code>references</code>, <code>supersedes</code>, <code>implements_decision</code>, <code>derived_from</code> or <code>contradicts</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">metadata</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The caller&#39;s own object, stored verbatim and never interpreted, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created_at</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the link was written. Named <code>created_at</code> because <code>link.add</code> answers with a boolean <code>created</code> beside it.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.events[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The event&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">entity</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What kind of thing it happened to: <code>task</code>, <code>project</code>, <code>doc</code> or <code>link</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">entity_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That thing&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">op</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What happened: <code>add</code>, <code>done</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>tag.remove</code>, …</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">payload</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The op&#39;s own vocabulary. Null only for a row whose payload will not parse — a corrupt store.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">ts</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it happened.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">actor</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Who did it, when the caller said, or null.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;x1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;store.export&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+docs&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;x1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;default_project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;docs&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;# Pricing page…&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-09T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;0787b26d-9e2e-4be5-ab66-ec953102fad3&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-11T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_mtime&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_path&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_size&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;notes/pricing.md&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pricing-page-decisions&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;dropped_dependencies&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;dropped_docs&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;dropped_events&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;dropped_links&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;dropped_projects&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;events&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;actor&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;user&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;entity&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;entity_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;37e2265e-0745-46cf-ab75-44127cc95bc2&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;op&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;add&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;payload&quot;</span>: {
          <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0&quot;</span>
        },
        <span class="j-k">&quot;ts&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-26T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;links&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created_at&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-11T09:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;from&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;5f0a7c21-3d64-4a0e-9b8f-2c1d7e4a6b90&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;metadata&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;relation&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;references&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;to&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;memory:0787b26d-9e2e-4be5-ab66-ec953102fad3&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;projects&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-06-18T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Public REST API and its SDKs&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;309d6b79-965e-4a32-9ae4-45508201e2bd&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>
      }
    ],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;tasks&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;…&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;one whole task per row&quot;</span>
      }
    ]
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the real answer is the entire store — every task, project, doc, link and audit row, in one payload. What matters here is its shape, so this example is a single row of each with the bodies elided.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>an agent cannot snapshot what it just wrote, and that is a real gap — but the          payload is the whole store, which is exactly the size problem D63 and D66 spent          two rounds on. It needs a filter and a budget before it is a tool rather than a          way to blow a client&#39;s limit in one call.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx export</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a> — Dump tasks as canonical JSON.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-store.import"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-store.import">store.import</h3><p><code>{imported, projects_imported, projects_created, docs_imported, docs_declared, events_imported, links_imported, default_project, renumbered, docs_merged, dry_run, merged, project_description_conflicts, deduplicated}</code>. A task already in the store at a higher <code>_rev</code> than the payload's refuses the whole import (conflict) rather than silently discarding the annotations, tags and edges added since. A task whose <code>short_id</code> a DIFFERENT task here already holds keeps its id and takes the next free number, listed in <code>renumbered</code> as <code>{id, from, to}</code> (D177). A memory doc whose <code>source</code> a DIFFERENT doc here already holds merges onto that doc — the later <code>modified</code> wins the text — listed in <code>docs_merged</code> as <code>{source, kept_id, dropped_id, took}</code> (D183). Links are restored last, both ends resolved against what this store now holds; an end it does not have refuses the import by name (D181). <code>dry_run</code> (default false) runs the entire import — every renumbering, merge and refusal — and rolls it back instead of committing, so the same answer previews what a real import would do (D184). <code>merge</code> (default false) unions a KNOWN task's annotations, checks, tags and dependency edges with what this store already holds instead of replacing them, skips its <code>_rev</code> guard (D185), takes each field from the side whose event last wrote it and counts tracked time from the union of both event logs — listed in <code>merged</code> as <code>{id, took, from_payload, from_store, tracked_delta_seconds}</code> (D189). A project this store already knows keeps its own non-empty description over the payload's — a project carries no <code>modified</code> stamp, so there is no later-wins call to make — listed in <code>project_description_conflicts</code> as <code>{name, dropped}</code> (D190); <code>archived</code> is still taken from the payload unconditionally. Two copies of one recurrence occurrence (same <code>spawned_from</code>, <code>due</code> and <code>scheduled</code>, anywhere in the store) fold into the lowest id, listed in <code>deduplicated</code> (D191).</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-store.import-tasks" data-param="tasks"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tasks</code><span class="badge">array of object</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task documents to import, in the shape `store.export` emits. Required, so a misspelled key at the top level is still refused by absence.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.import-projects" data-param="projects"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">projects</code><span class="badge">array of object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project records. A task naming a project this list does not carry mints one, reported in `projects_created`.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.import-default-project" data-param="default_project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">default_project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The default project to set after the import.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.import-docs" data-param="docs"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">docs</code><span class="badge">array of object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The knowledge docs to import.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.import-events" data-param="events"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">events</code><span class="badge">array of object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The audit rows to import, so history survives a round trip.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.import-links" data-param="links"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">links</code><span class="badge">array of object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The explicit links to restore, in the shape `store.export` emits. Written after everything they point at; an end neither the document nor this store holds refuses the import by name (D181).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.import-dry-run" data-param="dry_run"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">dry_run</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>false</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Run the whole import — every renumbering, merge and refusal — and roll it back instead of committing, so the result previews what a real import would do without writing anything (D184).</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-store.import-merge" data-param="merge"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">merge</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>false</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Merge a task this store ALREADY holds instead of replacing it (D185): its annotations, checks, token measurements, tags and dependency edges are unioned with what is here, its `_rev` guard is skipped, each scalar field group is taken from the side whose latest event touched it (D189; the later `modified` decides a group neither log touched, or a copy that carries no log), and its tracked total is counted from the union of both event logs, plus the larger of the two sides' totals the logs do not explain, so both directions of a merge agree. Reported per task in `merged`. Default false keeps the wholesale replace a restore wants (D138).</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">imported</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many tasks the document brought in.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">projects_imported</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many projects it carried.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">projects_created</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The NAMES of projects minted because a task named one the document did not carry — a list, so nothing appears out of nowhere unseen.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">docs_imported</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many knowledge docs came in.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">docs_declared</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the document had a <code>docs</code> section at all — an empty one told apart from a missing one (#179).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">events_imported</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many audit rows came in.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">links_imported</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many explicit links came in (D181) — an edge this store already held under a different id counts, because that is the same edge stated twice. Zero for a document with no <code>links</code> section.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default_project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The default project after the import, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">renumbered</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every task whose <code>short_id</code> a DIFFERENT task in this store already held, as <code>{id, from, to}</code> — it kept its id and took the next free number (D177). Empty when nothing moved.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">docs_merged</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every memory doc that landed on a doc this store already held under the same <code>source</code>, as <code>{source, kept_id, dropped_id, took}</code> — the stored id is kept, the payload&#39;s is dropped, and <code>took</code> is <code>payload</code> when the payload&#39;s <code>modified</code> was later (its title, body, project and standing were written) or <code>store</code> when it was not (nothing was written). <code>dropped_id</code> is null when the payload doc carried no <code>id</code> of its own, rather than a minted one a dry run would then roll back. D183. Empty when nothing merged.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">dry_run</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Echoes the <code>dry_run</code> param (D184). True means every row above was written and then rolled back — the answer describes what WOULD have happened, not what is now on disk.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">merged</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every task this store ALREADY held that <code>merge</code> unioned rather than replaced, as <code>{id, took, from_payload, from_store, tracked_delta_seconds}</code>. Each scalar field group follows the side whose latest event touched it (D189); <code>from_payload</code> and <code>from_store</code> name the fields that differed and the side each was taken from, and <code>took</code> is <code>payload</code> or <code>store</code> when one side supplied all of them, <code>mixed</code> when both did, and D185&#39;s later-<code>modified</code> side when none differed. <code>tracked_delta_seconds</code> is how far the tracked total moved: the total is counted from the union of both event logs, plus the larger of the two sides&#39; totals the logs do not explain. Its annotations, checks, tokens, tags and edges are unioned either way. D185. Empty when <code>merge</code> was not asked for, or when the document carried nothing this store had seen.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project_description_conflicts</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every project this store already held whose OWN non-empty description was kept over the payload&#39;s, as <code>{name, dropped}</code> — a project carries no <code>modified</code> stamp, so there is no later-wins call to make and the destination&#39;s text always wins (D190). <code>archived</code> is still taken from the payload unconditionally. Empty when nothing was dropped.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">deduplicated</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every recurrence occurrence folded into an older copy of itself, as <code>{kept, dropped, spawned_from, kept_id, dropped_id, dropped_status, status, dropped_dependencies}</code> (short ids, then uuids). Every group in the store sharing <code>spawned_from</code>, <code>due</code> and <code>scheduled</code> keeps the lowest id and takes the other&#39;s notes, checks, tags, edges, links, tokens and events. <code>status</code> is the survivor&#39;s afterwards: the copy with the latest status event wins it (D189&#39;s rule), and tracked time is counted from both copies&#39; event logs, each event once. <code>dropped_dependencies</code> names the survivor&#39;s edges dropped because the fold would have closed a cycle. D191. Empty when nothing was folded.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;si1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;store.import&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;tasks&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;9a1f3c52-0b44-4a2e-9d6f-7c5b1e08a4d1&quot;,&quot;short_id&quot;:900,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Restore the incident timeline&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;pending&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;M&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;infra&quot;,&quot;created&quot;:&quot;2026-09-10T08:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:&quot;2026-09-10T08:00:00Z&quot;,&quot;_rev&quot;:1,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ops&quot;],&quot;depends_on&quot;:[],&quot;annotations&quot;:[]}]}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;si1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;deduplicated&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;default_project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;website&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;docs_declared&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;docs_imported&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;docs_merged&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;dry_run&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;events_imported&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;imported&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;links_imported&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;merged&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;project_description_conflicts&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;projects_created&quot;</span>: [],
    <span class="j-k">&quot;projects_imported&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;renumbered&quot;</span>: []
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>it overwrites, in bulk, from a document nobody has reviewed. The confirmation model          (§7) defers to the host&#39;s gate, and a host gate on a call whose diff nobody can see          is not a safeguard.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx import</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-import"><code>import</code></a> — Load tasks from a JSON file or stdin.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-event-methods">Event methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-event.list"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-event.list">event.list</h3><p><code>{count, events}</code> — the append-only log. <code>from</code> takes the usual date grammar and is a lower bound, not an exact filter: it promises no events older than roughly that instant.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-event">Event</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-event.list-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">default <code>50</code></span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many events to return, newest first.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-event.list-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only events about this task.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-event.list-entity" data-param="entity"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">entity</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only events about this kind of thing: `task`, `project`, `doc` or `link`. An unknown name is refused, not read as a filter matching nothing.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-event.list-from" data-param="from"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">A lower bound in the usual date grammar (`yesterday`, `2026-09-01`). It promises no events older than roughly that instant, not an exact cut.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">count</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many events came back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">events</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The events, newest first for everything this engine wrote — <code>id</code> is a UUIDv7, time-ordered — but a row brought in by <code>store.import</code> keeps its document&#39;s id and can sort anywhere.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.events[]</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The event&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">entity</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What kind of thing it happened to: <code>task</code>, <code>project</code>, <code>doc</code> or <code>link</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">entity_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That thing&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">op</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What happened: <code>add</code>, <code>done</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>tag.remove</code>, …</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">payload</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The op&#39;s own vocabulary. Null only for a row whose payload will not parse — a corrupt store.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">ts</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it happened.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">actor</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Who did it, when the caller said, or null.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ev1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;event.list&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;entity&quot;:&quot;project&quot;,&quot;limit&quot;:2}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ev1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;count&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;events&quot;</span>: [
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;actor&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;user&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;entity&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;project&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;entity_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;73f778aa-f6fa-4db8-a56a-bd72fb710734&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;a66b0d38-9d95-447e-bd29-9753a7677796&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;op&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;create&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;payload&quot;</span>: {
          <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;home&quot;</span>
        },
        <span class="j-k">&quot;ts&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-06-18T00:00:00Z&quot;</span>
      },
      {
        <span class="j-k">&quot;actor&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;user&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;entity&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;project&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;entity_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;e3eff9c0-cf44-4d3f-89e7-d15f17362f25&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;986e86cb-0ab8-4b67-a26b-7f62b1852f27&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;op&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;create&quot;</span>,
        <span class="j-k">&quot;payload&quot;</span>: {
          <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;CI, deploys and on-call&quot;</span>,
          <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;infra&quot;</span>
        },
        <span class="j-k">&quot;ts&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-06-18T00:00:00Z&quot;</span>
      }
    ]
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>the audit log is unbounded and has no paging, so exposing it would repeat the          <code>task.get</code> mistake D63 fixed. It needs the same limit/offset treatment before it          can be a tool; no client has asked for it yet.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx dashboard</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> — Open the overview screen, or ask for its panels as data.</p><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx chart</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-chart"><code>chart</code></a> — Render throughput, heatmap, or burndown charts.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="api-event.revert"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-event.revert">event.revert</h3><p><code>{reverted, short_id, title, restored}</code> — <code>reverted</code> carries the event id, its op and its timestamp. Undoes the <em>newest</em> event by APPENDING a compensating one, so the reversed event stays in the log. Six ops are undoable (<code>stop</code>, <code>tag.remove</code>, <code>dependency.remove</code>, <code>annotation.add</code>, <code>annotation.update</code>, <code>adjust_tracked</code>); every other one is <code>conflict</code> naming itself and what does take it back. The newest <em>event</em>, not the last call you made: a call that changed nothing writes no event, so undo reaches past it — which is why the answer names what it undid instead of saying ok.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-event">Event</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><p>None. Send <code>params</code> as <code>{}</code>, or leave it out.</p><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">reverted</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The event that was undone.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The title of the task the undo touched.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">restored</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the inverse put back — per-op, the undo&#39;s own vocabulary.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter. The methods that change the task or its tags, notes, checks and dependencies bump it; <code>token.add</code>, <code>token.remove</code> and <code>reminder.fire</code> leave it alone. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath"><code>result.reverted</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">event</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The undone event&#39;s id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">op</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its op — undo names what it undid instead of answering ok.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">ts</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the undone event happened.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;u1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;event.revert&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;u1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">5</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;restored&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;tags&quot;</span>: [
        <span class="j-s">&quot;ops&quot;</span>
      ]
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;reverted&quot;</span>: {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;event&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;9c2b4d61-1f77-4a0c-9c1e-2b8e5d3a7f40&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;op&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;tag.remove&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;ts&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>
    },
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">53</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Move nightly backups to object storage&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> it undoes whatever is NEWEST in the log, so its answer depends on store state a fixture cannot pin — and on the demo store the newest event is a <code>start</code>, which undo refuses by name rather than reversing.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>tasqx has an undo (D54) and an agent cannot reach it, which is the sharpest single          omission on this list. It stays off until the tool can show what it is about to          undo: <code>event.revert</code> acts on the last matching event, and its blast radius depends          on store state the calling agent has not read. A destructive one-shot whose effect          the caller cannot see is not a tool, it is a coin flip.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>tasqx undo</code></pre></div><p><a href="#cli-undo"><code>undo</code></a> — Take back the last thing this store recorded.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-reminder-methods">Reminder methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-reminder.fire"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-reminder.fire">reminder.fire</h3><p><code>{fired, short_id, at}</code>. Idempotent.</p><p>Objects: <a href="#obj-task">Task</a>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="api-reminder.fire-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task whose reminder is being fired. Daemon-internal — the `reminded` event is a dedupe key, not a notification anyone reads here.</dd></div><div class="param" id="api-reminder.fire-at" data-param="at"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">at</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The instant the reminder is recorded against. Firing the same instant twice is a no-op.</dd></div></dl><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">fired</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether this call fired the reminder. False on a repeat — the method is idempotent.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">at</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The instant the reminder is recorded against.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;rf1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;reminder.fire&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;49&quot;,&quot;at&quot;:&quot;2026-09-17T16:00:00Z&quot;}}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;rf1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;at&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-17T16:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;fired&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">49</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>daemon-internal. Its <code>reminded</code> event is a dedupe key and a push surface, not a          thing a client asks for.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-core-methods">Core methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-core.capabilities"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-core.capabilities">core.capabilities</h3><p><code>{api, methods, params, features, default_project, store}</code>.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><p>None. Send <code>params</code> as <code>{}</code>, or leave it out.</p><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">api</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The API major version this build speaks.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">methods</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every method name it dispatches.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">params</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The accepted params key set, per method — a key outside it is refused, never ignored (D33).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">features</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The optional features this build carries.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default_project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The store&#39;s default project, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">store</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The store file this engine answers from (D74) — the caller&#39;s own in-process, the daemon&#39;s over a socket. Null in memory.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;c1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;core.capabilities&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
