  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> its <code>store</code> is the path of whatever store answered, so a capture would quote the machine that took it. The handshake at the top of this page is rendered live from this build&#39;s own <code>capabilities()</code> with a plausible store instead (D74).</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>the MCP handshake already answers this question: <code>initialize</code> reports the protocol          revision and scope, and <code>tools/list</code> reports the surface. A second, differently          shaped capability document is a second thing to keep in sync.</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-otlp-methods">OTLP methods</h3><section class="ref" id="api-otlp.status"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-api-otlp.status">otlp.status</h3><p><code>{received, attributed, orphaned, last_seen}</code>. Read-only visibility into the opt-in local OTLP receiver's buffer (#18): <code>received</code> is every sample still inside the 30-day retention window, <code>attributed</code> how many turned into a <code>source=otel</code> measurement, <code>orphaned</code> the rest, and <code>last_seen</code> the newest sample's timestamp (<code>null</code> on an empty buffer) — the only way to tell a misconfigured exporter from a healthy, quiet one.</p><h4>Parameters</h4><p>None. Send <code>params</code> as <code>{}</code>, or leave it out.</p><h4>Response</h4><div class="shapepath"><code>result</code></div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">received</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Samples still inside the 30-day retention window.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">attributed</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many of them turned into a measurement.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">orphaned</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How many matched no task&#39;s window.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">last_seen</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The newest sample&#39;s timestamp; null on an empty buffer — a misconfigured exporter told apart from a quiet one.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="JSON API"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;tasqx&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;o1&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;otlp.status&quot;}&#39; | tasqx api</code></pre><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;o1&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ok&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;result&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;attributed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;last_seen&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;orphaned&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;received&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tasqx&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;1&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p><strong>No MCP tool.</strong> An agent reaches this method only through a human running <code>tasqx api</code>.</p><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>an operator diagnostic for a machine-local, opt-in receiver (#18) — is telemetry reaching THIS daemon on THIS machine — not a fact about any task an agent is working. <code>tasqx config store</code> / a CLI verb is where a human checks it (#222).</p></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="CLI"><p>No verb reaches this method on its own — <code>tasqx api</code> is the way, and the envelope beside this is the whole call.</p></div></div></div></section><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#commands"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Commands</span></a><a class="next" href="#mcp"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">MCP</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="mcp"><h2>The MCP server</h2><p class="lead">tasqx bundles an MCP server, so an AI agent reads and mutates your tasks with zero glue. It is the same core API underneath — the agent and your shell are peers.</p><section class="ref" id="mcp-scope"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-scope">It fails closed</h3><p>The least-privilege default is <strong>read-only</strong>. Write access is an explicit operator choice for this local stdio process. Scope is configuration, not an authentication credential.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="CLI">CLI</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="CLI"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx mcp serve
tasqx mcp serve --scope write</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>tasqx mcp: serving over stdio (scope=read)
tasqx mcp: serving over stdio (scope=write)</code></pre></div><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx mcp serve   # scope omitted</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>tasqx mcp: serving over stdio (scope=read)</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="MCP"><p>Under read scope the 23 write tools are absent from <code>tools/list</code> entirely, so an agent is never aimed at a call it will be refused. Each tool below states the scope it needs.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-transport"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-transport">Talking to it</h3><p>Newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin/stdout. Diagnostics go to stderr <em>only</em> — stdout carries nothing but responses, so the transport is never corrupted by a log line.</p><p>The <code>initialize</code> result carries <code>instructions</code>: a scope-aware workflow the host may inject into the agent's system prompt, so the agent is told <em>when</em> to reach for tasqx and not only what it can call. It is elided beside this, because it is a few paragraphs long.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;initialize&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;protocolVersion&quot;:&quot;2024-11-05&quot;,&quot;capabilities&quot;:{},&quot;clientInfo&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;demo&quot;,&quot;version&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}}}&#39; | tasqx mcp serve 2&gt;/dev/null | sed &#39;s/&quot;instructions&quot;:&quot;[^&quot;]*&quot;/&quot;instructions&quot;:&quot;…&quot;/&#39;</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;result&quot;:{&quot;capabilities&quot;:{&quot;tools&quot;:{}},&quot;instructions&quot;:&quot;…&quot;,&quot;protocolVersion&quot;:&quot;2024-11-05&quot;,&quot;serverInfo&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx&quot;,&quot;version&quot;:&quot;0.14.0&quot;}}}</code></pre></div><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:3,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_list_tasks&quot;,&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+api&quot;}}}&#39; | tasqx mcp serve 2&gt;/dev/null</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:3,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;result&quot;:{&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;{\n  \&quot;count\&quot;: 1,\n  \&quot;next_offset\&quot;: null,\n  \&quot;store_empty\&quot;: false,\n  \&quot;tasks\&quot;: [\n    {\n      \&quot;blocked\&quot;: false,\n      \&quot;due\&quot;: \&quot;2026-07-17T00:00:00Z\&quot;,\n      \&quot;priority\&quot;: \&quot;H\&quot;,\n      \&quot;project\&quot;: \&quot;work.tasqx\&quot;,\n      \&quot;short_id\&quot;: 1,\n      \&quot;status\&quot;: \&quot;pending\&quot;,\n      \&quot;tags\&quot;: [\n        \&quot;api\&quot;,\n        \&quot;release\&quot;\n      ],\n      \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;Ship the v1 JSON API freeze\&quot;,\n      \&quot;urgency\&quot;: 17.5\n    }\n  ],\n  \&quot;total\&quot;: 1\n}&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;}],&quot;isError&quot;:false}}</code></pre></div></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same calls without the JSON-RPC wrapper are <a href="#api">the JSON API</a>: one envelope in, one out, and each tool below links to the method it routes to.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-refusing-a-write">Refusing a write</h3><p>Ask a read-only server to write, and it refuses by name:</p><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="cmd"><code>echo &#39;{&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:4,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_task&quot;,&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;nope&quot;}}}&#39; | tasqx mcp serve 2&gt;/dev/null</code></pre><pre class="out"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:4,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;result&quot;:{&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;error [bad_request]: tool `tasqx_add_task` requires write scope, but this MCP server is running read-only. This cannot be changed from a tool call: the operator must relaunch the server as `tasqx mcp serve --scope write`.&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;}],&quot;isError&quot;:true}}</code></pre></div><h3 id="h-wiring-it-into-a-client">Wiring it into a client</h3><p>Most MCP clients take a command and arguments. Pass the scope you want the child process to have:</p><pre class="plain"><code>{
  &quot;mcpServers&quot;: {
    &quot;tasqx&quot;: {
      &quot;command&quot;: &quot;tasqx&quot;,
      &quot;args&quot;: [&quot;mcp&quot;, &quot;serve&quot;, &quot;--scope&quot;, &quot;write&quot;]
    }
  }
}</code></pre><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p>Start an agent with the default read scope. Give it write only once you have watched what it does with read. A future network transport needs real authentication; this scope flag is not a credential.</p></div><h3 id="h-every-tool">Every tool</h3><p>9 read tools always; 23 write tools only with write scope. Each carries MCP annotations (<code>readOnlyHint</code>, <code>destructiveHint</code>) so a client can reason about them before calling.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-28-h0">Tool</th><th id="tbl-28-h1">Scope</th><th id="tbl-28-h2">Method</th><th id="tbl-28-h3">Does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_tasks"><code>tasqx_list_tasks</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">List tasks matching a filter-DSL query — the CLI&#39;s grammar, e.g.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_task"><code>tasqx_get_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Get one task&#39;s full detail: fields, tags, annotations, dependencies.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Everything you need before starting one task, in ONE call (D136): the task, the tasks it depends on with what each of THEM concluded, what it blocks, and memory found under a query tasqx derives from the task&#39;s title, tags and project.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_summary"><code>tasqx_summary</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-report.summary"><code>report.summary</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Aggregate report grouped by project, status or priority.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_outcomes"><code>tasqx_outcomes</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-report.outcomes"><code>report.outcomes</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">How the work went rather than what it cost: rework, estimate calibration, token cost, unannotated completions, started-then-cancelled work, and <code>forced</code> (completions that overrode open blockers).</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_projects"><code>tasqx_list_projects</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">List projects.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_search_memory"><code>tasqx_search_memory</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-memory.search"><code>memory.search</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Search the memory store — imported docs and task annotations — bm25-ranked with snippets.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_memory"><code>tasqx_list_memory</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Browse memory docs without knowing a word inside one — what <code>tasqx_search_memory</code> cannot do without a query.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_memory"><code>tasqx_get_memory</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">read</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Read one knowledge doc whole, by the <code>id</code> a search hit carries — <code>tasqx_search_memory</code> returns only an excerpt.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_task"><code>tasqx_add_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.add"><code>task.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Create a task.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_modify_task"><code>tasqx_modify_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.modify"><code>task.modify</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Change fields on a task via a <code>set</code> map.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_complete_task"><code>tasqx_complete_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Mark a task done.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_cancel_task"><code>tasqx_cancel_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.cancel"><code>task.cancel</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Cancel a task: backlog, pending or active moves to cancelled.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_reopen_task"><code>tasqx_reopen_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.reopen"><code>task.reopen</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Reopen a closed task: done or cancelled goes back to pending, and the completion timestamp is cleared so the task stops counting in the week it is no longer finished in.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_start_timer"><code>tasqx_start_timer</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.start"><code>task.start</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Start the timer on a task, moving it to active.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_stop_timer"><code>tasqx_stop_timer</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.stop"><code>task.stop</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Stop the timer on a task.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked"><code>tasqx_adjust_tracked</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-task.adjust_tracked"><code>task.adjust_tracked</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Correct tracked time by a signed <code>delta</code> (<code>-2h25m</code>, <code>+30m</code>); any status.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_tag_task"><code>tasqx_tag_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-tag.add"><code>tag.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Add one or more tags to a task.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_untag_task"><code>tasqx_untag_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-tag.remove"><code>tag.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Remove one or more tags from a task.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_check"><code>tasqx_add_check</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-check.add"><code>check.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Add an acceptance criterion to a task — one thing that must be true for it to count as done (D138).</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_set_check"><code>tasqx_set_check</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-check.set"><code>check.set</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Mark one acceptance criterion passed or failed, with the evidence for it.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_check"><code>tasqx_remove_check</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-check.remove"><code>check.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Drop an acceptance criterion that turned out to be the wrong thing to ask.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_annotate_task"><code>tasqx_annotate_task</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-annotation.add"><code>annotation.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Attach a timestamped note to a task.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_tokens"><code>tasqx_add_tokens</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-token.add"><code>token.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Record token spend on a task after the fact, e.g.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_annotation"><code>tasqx_remove_annotation</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Permanently scrub one annotation&#39;s text by id.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_update_annotation"><code>tasqx_update_annotation</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-annotation.update"><code>annotation.update</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Correct one annotation&#39;s body in place, by id (D165): id, timestamp and position are kept, and search stops finding the old text.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_dependency"><code>tasqx_add_dependency</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-dependency.add"><code>dependency.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Make one task depend on another: <code>ref</code> is blocked until <code>depends_on</code> is done or cancelled, and a <code>ref</code> already closed is never blocked.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_dependency"><code>tasqx_remove_dependency</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-dependency.remove"><code>dependency.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Cut a dependency edge: <code>ref</code> stops waiting on <code>depends_on</code>.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_memory"><code>tasqx_add_memory</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-memory.add"><code>memory.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Store a knowledge document in memory: patterns, documentation, decisions worth finding again.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_update_memory"><code>tasqx_update_memory</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-memory.update"><code>memory.update</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Correct a memory doc in place — title, body, source and/or project — by id.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_memory"><code>tasqx_remove_memory</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-memory.remove"><code>memory.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Remove one knowledge document from memory by id.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Tool" headers="tbl-28-h0"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_create_project"><code>tasqx_create_project</code></a></td><td data-label="Scope" headers="tbl-28-h1">write</td><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-28-h2"><a href="#api-project.create"><code>project.create</code></a></td><td data-label="Does" headers="tbl-28-h3">Create a project.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_list_tasks"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_list_tasks">tasqx_list_tasks</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>List tasks matching a filter-DSL query — the CLI&#39;s grammar, e.g. &quot;project:work status:pending +api due.before:tomorrow&quot;. Paged: the response carries <code>count</code>, <code>total</code> and <code>next_offset</code>, null once nothing is left. Rows carry a default field set unless you name <code>fields</code> (D152).</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_tasks-fields" data-param="fields"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">fields</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Restrict each row to these fields. Omit for short_id, title, status, priority, urgency, blocked, due, project, tags, with null-valued keys dropped; send [] for the whole row.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_tasks-filter" data-param="filter"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Filter DSL, e.g. &quot;status:pending +api&quot;. &quot;@working&quot; is the actionable set. Omit it (or send &quot;&quot;) for every task.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_tasks-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Rows to return. Omit for this tool&#39;s page (100), shrunk to fit the response byte budget; a named limit is honoured up to 10000.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_tasks-offset" data-param="offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Matching rows to skip; pass the previous <code>next_offset</code>. Ordering is stable across pages.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_tasks-sort" data-param="sort"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">sort</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Sort keys, e.g. [&quot;-urgency&quot;, &quot;due&quot;]; &quot;-&quot; descends. Valid: urgency, short_id, priority, due, created, modified, title, tokens, estimate, tracked. An unknown key is rejected.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;filter&quot;:&quot;+docs&quot;,&quot;sort&quot;:[&quot;-urgency&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_list_tasks&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_get_task">tasqx_get_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Get one task&#39;s full detail: fields, tags, annotations, dependencies. Annotations come back in pages counted from the newest, oldest first within a page — the response carries <code>annotations_total</code>, and <code>annotations_next_offset</code> whenever older ones were left out.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task-annotations-limit" data-param="annotations_limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotations_limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Most-recent annotations to return; omit for this tool&#39;s page (20). An over-budget page is cut to what fits and the view names the <code>annotations_offset</code> for the rest; <code>include_json: true</code> spends that budget first. 0 returns none.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task-annotations-offset" data-param="annotations_offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotations_offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Annotations to skip, counted back from the newest; pass the previous <code>annotations_next_offset</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task-explain" data-param="explain"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">explain</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Add <code>urgency_breakdown</code> (<code>priority</code>, <code>due_proximity</code>, <code>age</code>, <code>total</code>) — the terms <code>urgency</code> sums (D1). Default false.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task-include-json" data-param="include_json"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_json</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Send the machine-readable JSON block beside the rendered view. Default FALSE: it is one result twice and you read the view (D151). True when a SCRIPT parses this. This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>task.get</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task-max-body-bytes" data-param="max_body_bytes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">max_body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_task-view" data-param="view"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">view</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> How the rendered block is spelled. Default &quot;markdown&quot;, the view YOU read; &quot;card&quot; is the D146 72-column box card in a text fence, for a PERSON deciding on the task (D164), and quotes only the first annotation. This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>task.get</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_get_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_brief_task">tasqx_brief_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Everything you need before starting one task, in ONE call (D136): the task, the tasks it depends on with what each of THEM concluded, what it blocks, and memory found under a query tasqx derives from the task&#39;s title, tags and project. Use tasqx_get_task when you only need the task.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_brief_task-include-json" data-param="include_json"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_json</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Send the machine-readable JSON block beside the rendered view. Default FALSE: it is the brief again, snippets included (D151). True when a script parses this. This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>task.brief</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_brief_task-include-rank" data-param="include_rank"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_rank</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Add the raw FTS5 bm25 <code>rank</code> to each memory hit; default false, and visible only in the <code>include_json</code> block. LOWER is the better match and hits arrive sorted best-first. This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>task.brief</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_brief_task-max-body-bytes" data-param="max_body_bytes"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">max_body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_brief_task-memory-limit" data-param="memory_limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">memory_limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Memory hits to return; default 5. Half the slots (rounded up) are reserved for knowledge docs, annotations fill the rest, and either kind takes the other&#39;s unused slots.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_brief_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id or UUID.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_brief_task-view" data-param="view"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">view</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> How the TASK HALF is spelled. Default &quot;markdown&quot;, the view YOU read; &quot;card&quot; is the D146 72-column box card in a text fence, for a PERSON deciding on the task (D164). Prerequisites and memory hits stay markdown. This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>task.brief</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;memory_limit&quot;:3,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_brief_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_summary"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_summary">tasqx_summary</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Aggregate report grouped by project, status or priority. Pure read.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-report.summary"><code>report.summary</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_summary-all" data-param="all"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">all</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Count cancelled tasks too. By default a report with no status term skips cancelled only — done work always counts (D24).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_summary-filter" data-param="filter"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional filter DSL to scope the report.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_summary-group-by" data-param="group_by"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">group_by</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_summary-metrics" data-param="metrics"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">metrics</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Extra columns per group. Omit and each group carries only <code>count</code>: every other metric is opt-in here, unlike <code>tasqx report</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_summary-since" data-param="since"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Window <code>tracked_total</code> and the token buckets to spend at or after this instant, not the task&#39;s lifetime total — a different axis from <code>filter</code>&#39;s <code>completed.*</code> terms (D97).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_summary-until" data-param="until"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">until</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The other end of <code>since</code>: excludes anything at or after this instant. Together they window WHEN the spend happened.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;group_by&quot;:&quot;project&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_summary&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-report.summary"><code>report.summary</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_outcomes"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_outcomes">tasqx_outcomes</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>How the work went rather than what it cost: rework, estimate calibration, token cost, unannotated completions, started-then-cancelled work, and <code>forced</code> (completions that overrode open blockers). Every rate carries the <code>n</code> it was computed over. Scope is tasks that CLOSED; <code>tasqx_summary</code> reads work in flight.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-report.outcomes"><code>report.outcomes</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_outcomes-filter" data-param="filter"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">filter</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional filter DSL to scope the report — <code>tasqx_list_tasks</code>&#39; grammar.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_outcomes-group-by" data-param="group_by"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">group_by</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_outcomes-metrics" data-param="metrics"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">metrics</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which metrics to emit. Omit for ALL of them; naming none does not mean a bare count here.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_outcomes-since" data-param="since"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Only count tasks that closed at or after this instant. <code>since</code>/<code>until</code> window WHEN THE TASK CLOSED, not when spend happened.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_outcomes-until" data-param="until"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">until</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The other end of <code>since</code>: excludes tasks that closed at or after this instant.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;group_by&quot;:&quot;project&quot;,&quot;metrics&quot;:[&quot;rework&quot;,&quot;calibration&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_outcomes&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-report.outcomes"><code>report.outcomes</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_list_projects"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_list_projects">tasqx_list_projects</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>List projects. By default excludes archived projects.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_projects-include-archived" data-param="include_archived"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_archived</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Include archived projects in the list. Omitted, an archive is out of sight.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_list_projects&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_search_memory">tasqx_search_memory</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Search the memory store — imported docs and task annotations — bm25-ranked with snippets. A plain query matches phrases by word STEM, every word required; if nothing has them all, any-word matches return with <code>relaxed: true</code> (D193). <code>matched</code> is what ran; <code>raw: true</code> takes FTS5 syntax. A hit is an excerpt: <code>tasqx_get_memory</code> reads a doc whole, <code>tasqx_get_task</code> an annotation. <code>hits</code> is sorted best-first (LOWER bm25 <code>rank</code> is better); <code>total</code> and <code>has_more</code> say what <code>limit</code> cut. A doc hit adds <code>stale</code> (D180).</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-memory.search"><code>memory.search</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory-include-rank" data-param="include_rank"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_rank</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Add the raw FTS5 bm25 <code>rank</code> to each hit. Default false. LOWER (more negative) is better and <code>hits</code> is already sorted best-first, so never use it as a threshold (D154). This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>memory.search</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory-include-unscoped" data-param="include_unscoped"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_unscoped</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Widen a <code>project</code> scope to docs and annotations with NO project — what <code>tasqx memory import</code> produces. Never admits another project&#39;s. Refused without <code>project</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Max hits (0 or more); default 10. The response&#39;s <code>total</code>/<code>has_more</code> say what this left out.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Scope to one project: docs stored with it, and annotations whose task carries it. Omit to search every project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory-query" data-param="query"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">query</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Plain-text search words. Matched as quoted phrases, so hyphens and dots are safe.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory-raw" data-param="raw"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">raw</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Pass the query through as FTS5 syntax. Invalid syntax is refused as bad_request.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_search_memory-scope" data-param="scope"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">scope</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What to search. Optional; defaults to all.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;limit&quot;:2,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;release canary&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_search_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-memory.search"><code>memory.search</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_list_memory"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_list_memory">tasqx_list_memory</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Browse memory docs without knowing a word inside one — what <code>tasqx_search_memory</code> cannot do without a query. Newest-modified first, paged like <code>tasqx_list_tasks</code>. A row is <code>id</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>source</code> and <code>modified</code>, enough to RECOGNISE a doc; <code>include_preview: true</code> adds the rest, and <code>tasqx_get_memory</code> reads one whole (D154).</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_memory-include-preview" data-param="include_preview"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_preview</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Return the whole engine row — <code>project</code>, <code>created</code>, <code>_rev</code>, a 160-character <code>body_preview</code>, <code>body_truncated</code> — instead of the four identifying fields. Default false (D154). This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>memory.list</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_memory-limit" data-param="limit"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">limit</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Rows to return; default 20, because an unbounded browse page grows with the store.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_memory-offset" data-param="offset"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">offset</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Matching docs to skip; pass the previous response&#39;s <code>next_offset</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_memory-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Restrict to docs stored with this <code>project</code>. Omit to list every doc.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_list_memory-standing" data-param="standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">true lists only standing docs, false only the rest; omit for all (D156).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_list_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_get_memory"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_get_memory">tasqx_get_memory</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill opt">read scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Read one knowledge doc whole, by the <code>id</code> a search hit carries — <code>tasqx_search_memory</code> returns only an excerpt. An annotation id is refused, naming the task to read it from instead.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_get_memory-id" data-param="id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc UUID, as a search hit or <code>tasqx_add_memory</code> prints it.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_get_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_add_task">tasqx_add_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span></div><p>Create a task. Returns short_id, urgency and status — <code>backlog</code>, not <code>pending</code>, when <code>scheduled</code> or <code>wait</code> is in the future, which holds the task outside <code>@working</code> until then — plus the stored title, due, tags and resolved <code>scheduled</code>, so an ambiguous date or sugar captured into the title can be checked against what was stored. A title carrying CLI sugar adds a <code>warnings</code> entry naming it.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.add"><code>task.add</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-budget-tokens" data-param="budget_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">budget_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Token budget (D139): a size gauge over FRESH tokens — input, output, cache creation, never cache reads. It STOPS NOTHING; a blown budget signals a task too big to hand over whole. <code>tasqx_get_task</code> reports <code>over</code> against it.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-due" data-param="due"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The deadline; drives urgency and anchors relative reminders, and never hides the task. Date grammar: &quot;tomorrow&quot;, &quot;friday&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20&quot;, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, &quot;eom&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20T17:00&quot; (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-estimate" data-param="estimate"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Duration: &quot;4h&quot;, &quot;90m&quot;, &quot;1h30m&quot;, &quot;2d&quot;, &quot;1w&quot;, or ISO-8601 &quot;PT4H&quot;.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-priority" data-param="priority"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">priority</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Priority: H (high), M (medium), or L (low).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project to file it under. Omitted, the task lands in the store's default project — and the response says which, because that is the only place a caller learns it.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-recurrence" data-param="recurrence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Recurrence rule (D2 subset): &quot;daily&quot;, &quot;every 3 days&quot;, &quot;weekly on mon,wed&quot;, &quot;monthly on day 15&quot;, &quot;monthly on the last friday&quot;.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-remind" data-param="remind"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">remind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Reminder: a signed offset from <code>due</code> (&quot;-1h&quot;, &quot;-30m&quot;, &quot;-2d&quot;, &quot;+15m&quot;) or an absolute date in the <code>due</code> grammar.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-scheduled" data-param="scheduled"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When you intend to start; a future value holds the task in <code>backlog</code> until it arrives. Date grammar: &quot;tomorrow&quot;, &quot;friday&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20&quot;, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, &quot;eom&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20T17:00&quot; (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-tags" data-param="tags"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tags</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tags to put on the task. Lowercased and deduplicated as they are stored.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-title" data-param="title"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Stored verbatim: this server does not parse the CLI&#39;s inline sugar (<code>+tag</code>, <code>project:</code>, <code>due:</code>, <code>!prio</code>). Use the fields below.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_task-wait" data-param="wait"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">wait</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Hides the task until then, in <code>backlog</code> like <code>scheduled</code> but meaning &quot;not my problem yet&quot;. Date grammar: &quot;tomorrow&quot;, &quot;friday&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20&quot;, &quot;in 3 days&quot;, &quot;eom&quot;, &quot;2026-07-20T17:00&quot; (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;due&quot;:&quot;friday&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;H&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;website&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;planning&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Draft the Q4 roadmap&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.add"><code>task.add</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_modify_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_modify_task">tasqx_modify_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span></div><p>Change fields on a task via a <code>set</code> map. Returns <code>{short_id, _rev, set}</code>, where <code>set</code> echoes the RESOLVED value stored for each field named. Optimistic concurrency is ON: when <code>expected_rev</code> is omitted this server pins the task&#39;s current <code>_rev</code>, so a concurrent edit is a <code>conflict</code> naming both revs rather than a silent overwrite, and there is no way to opt out. On <code>conflict</code>, re-read the task, re-apply, retry (D75).</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.modify"><code>task.modify</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_modify_task-expected-rev" data-param="expected_rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">expected_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optimistic-concurrency guard. Supplied by the server from the task&#39;s current <code>_rev</code> when omitted; pass it to pin a rev you read earlier. There is no last-writer-wins mode.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_modify_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_modify_task-set" data-param="set"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">set</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Field → new value, e.g. {&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;M&quot;,&quot;due&quot;:&quot;2026-07-22T17:00:00+02:00&quot;}.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;52&quot;,&quot;set&quot;:{&quot;due&quot;:&quot;friday&quot;,&quot;priority&quot;:&quot;H&quot;}},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_modify_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.modify"><code>task.modify</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_complete_task">tasqx_complete_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span></div><p>Mark a task done. Returns any tasks its completion newly unblocked. Report what this task cost via the *_tokens params, or <code>total_tokens</code> alone when you only know one number (D167): a transcript measurement wins when tasqx finds the session that ran this task, and self-report is the fallback, graded <code>medium</code> because nothing can check it (D50, D188). <code>tool</code>/<code>model</code> are recorded on the event even with no count. A task with open dependencies is a <code>conflict</code> naming the blockers; <code>force: true</code> completes it anyway, counted by <code>tasqx_outcomes</code> (D150). <code>view: &quot;card&quot;</code> leads with the task&#39;s box card (D153), for a person deciding on it; a routine completion needs none (D164).</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-cache-creation-tokens" data-param="cache_creation_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported cache-creation tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-cache-read-tokens" data-param="cache_read_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported cache-read tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-checks-passed" data-param="checks_passed"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">checks_passed</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Ids of the acceptance criteria this work proved (D138). Completing with criteria open is not refused, but <code>tasqx_outcomes</code> counts it unproven.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-client" data-param="client"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">client</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Calling tool as &quot;&lt;name&gt; &lt;version&gt;&quot;. Filled in from the MCP handshake when omitted.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-evidence" data-param="evidence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One citation covering <code>checks_passed</code>: a test name, an excerpt of output, a commit sha.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-force" data-param="force"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">force</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Complete despite still-open dependencies; without it that is a <code>conflict</code> naming them (D150). The override is recorded and counted under <code>forced</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-input-tokens" data-param="input_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported input tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-model" data-param="model"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model doing the work, e.g. &quot;claude-opus-5&quot;. Recorded with or without token counts.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-output-tokens" data-param="output_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Self-reported output tokens (0 or more).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-session-id" data-param="session_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">session_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your agent-session id, recorded on this task&#39;s event for token attribution.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-tool" data-param="tool"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The AI tool doing the work, free-form (e.g. &quot;claude-code&quot;). Also names a token measurement, defaulting to <code>client</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-total-tokens" data-param="total_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, instead of the four (D167).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-transcript-path" data-param="transcript_path"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">transcript_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Absolute path to your session transcript, recorded on the same event.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_complete_task-view" data-param="view"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">view</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Default &quot;markdown&quot;: the plain JSON result. &quot;card&quot; leads with the D146 box card of the task AS COMPLETED, in a text fence, the JSON unchanged behind it, for a PERSON deciding on it (D164). This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>task.done</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;47&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_complete_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_cancel_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_cancel_task">tasqx_cancel_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span></div><p>Cancel a task: backlog, pending or active moves to cancelled. The row is kept and stops counting in reports. Returns the tasks the cancellation newly unblocked (D11: cancelling a blocker resolves it, like completing one). A task already closed is a conflict, not a no-op.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.cancel"><code>task.cancel</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_cancel_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;60&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_cancel_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.cancel"><code>task.cancel</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_reopen_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_reopen_task">tasqx_reopen_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span></div><p>Reopen a closed task: done or cancelled goes back to pending, and the completion timestamp is cleared so the task stops counting in the week it is no longer finished in. A task that is not closed is a conflict, not a no-op.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.reopen"><code>task.reopen</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_reopen_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;12&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_reopen_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.reopen"><code>task.reopen</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_start_timer">tasqx_start_timer</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span></div><p>Start the timer on a task, moving it to active. The correlation params land on the start event for token attribution.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.start"><code>task.start</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer-actor" data-param="actor"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">actor</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Who is asking for the clock (D140); filled in with this connection&#39;s id when omitted. Starting while ANOTHER actor holds an active clock is a <code>conflict</code>, not a silent stop of their timer; pass <code>keep: true</code> to run both.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer-client" data-param="client"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">client</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Calling tool as &quot;&lt;name&gt; &lt;version&gt;&quot;. Filled in from the MCP handshake when omitted.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer-include-memory" data-param="include_memory"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_memory</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Add <code>task.brief</code>&#39;s memory search, 3 hits (D186). Default true; false answers the bare result. This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>task.start</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer-keep" data-param="keep"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">keep</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Keep other active tasks running (opt out of single-active).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer-session-id" data-param="session_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">session_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your agent-session id, recorded on this task&#39;s event for token attribution.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_start_timer-transcript-path" data-param="transcript_path"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">transcript_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Absolute path to your session transcript, recorded on the same event.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;50&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_start_timer&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.start"><code>task.start</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_stop_timer"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_stop_timer">tasqx_stop_timer</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Stop the timer on a task. Returns <code>interval</code> (the duration just closed) and <code>tracked</code> (the task&#39;s running total, matching <code>tasqx_get_task</code>).</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.stop"><code>task.stop</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_stop_timer-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;48&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_stop_timer&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.stop"><code>task.stop</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked">tasqx_adjust_tracked</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span></div><p>Correct tracked time by a signed <code>delta</code> (<code>-2h25m</code>, <code>+30m</code>); any status. <code>tasqx undo</code> reverts it.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-task.adjust_tracked"><code>task.adjust_tracked</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked-delta" data-param="delta"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">delta</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Signed duration: <code>-2h25m</code>, <code>+30m</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked-reason" data-param="reason"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">reason</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Why the time is corrected.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;delta&quot;:&quot;-2h25m&quot;,&quot;reason&quot;:&quot;idle gap&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;42&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_adjust_tracked&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-task.adjust_tracked"><code>task.adjust_tracked</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_tag_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_tag_task">tasqx_tag_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Add one or more tags to a task. Tags are stored lowercase; one containing whitespace is refused. Returns the resulting tag set.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-tag.add"><code>tag.add</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_tag_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_tag_task-tags" data-param="tags"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tags</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tags to add. Already-present tags are a no-op rather than an error.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;53&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;q4&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_tag_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-tag.add"><code>tag.add</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_untag_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_untag_task">tasqx_untag_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Remove one or more tags from a task. Returns the resulting tag set. A tag the task does not carry is <code>not_found</code> and removes NONE of the tags named — all or nothing, so a typo can never answer ok.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-tag.remove"><code>tag.remove</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_untag_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_untag_task-tags" data-param="tags"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tags</code><span class="badge">array of string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The tags to take off. All or nothing: a tag the task does not have is `not_found` and removes none of them, so a typo cannot answer ok.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;53&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ops&quot;]},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_untag_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-tag.remove"><code>tag.remove</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_add_check"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_add_check">tasqx_add_check</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span></div><p>Add an acceptance criterion to a task — one thing that must be true for it to count as done (D138). tasqx NEVER RUNS a check: it is a claim you mark later with evidence, not a command.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-check.add"><code>check.add</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_check-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion, in your own words. Stored verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_check-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Every renamed symbol has a row in the table&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_check&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-check.add"><code>check.add</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_set_check"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_set_check">tasqx_set_check</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Mark one acceptance criterion passed or failed, with the evidence for it. <code>failed</code> is a normal outcome worth recording. Evidence is stored verbatim and never interpreted.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-check.set"><code>check.set</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_set_check-check-id" data-param="check_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">check_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The check&#39;s id, from <code>tasqx_get_task</code> or the add.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_set_check-evidence" data-param="evidence"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Your proof: a test name, an excerpt of output, a commit sha. Optional — an invented citation is worse than an unproven <code>passed</code>.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_set_check-position" data-param="position"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Or its 1-based place in tasqx_get_task&#39;s list.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_set_check-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_set_check-state" data-param="state"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">open | passed | failed.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;check_id&quot;:&quot;7e37a508-7921-4cb2-bf0c-0a2944eb31e4&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;:&quot;docs/guides/sdk-3.0.md#rate-limits&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;state&quot;:&quot;passed&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_set_check&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-check.set"><code>check.set</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_check"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_remove_check">tasqx_remove_check</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Drop an acceptance criterion that turned out to be the wrong thing to ask. Use <code>tasqx_set_check</code> with <code>failed</code> when the criterion was right and the work did not meet it; deleting it would hide the finding.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-check.remove"><code>check.remove</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_check-check-id" data-param="check_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">check_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The check&#39;s id.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_check-position" data-param="position"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Or its 1-based place in tasqx_get_task&#39;s list.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_check-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;check_id&quot;:&quot;e6a1096b-6f05-4e95-96f5-52452080f2ac&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_check&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-check.remove"><code>check.remove</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_annotate_task"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_annotate_task">tasqx_annotate_task</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span></div><p>Attach a timestamped note to a task. The body is stored verbatim, newlines and markdown included, so long-form context lives here. The response echoes the body back as proof of that, or <code>{id, created, body_bytes}</code> under <code>include_body: false</code>. <code>tasqx_remove_annotation</code> on that <code>id</code> is the only way to take a note back.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-annotation.add"><code>annotation.add</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_annotate_task-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Note text, stored verbatim. Multi-line markdown is fine.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_annotate_task-include-body" data-param="include_body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">include_body</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><span class="pill opt">MCP only</span> Echo the stored body back. Default true (D72/D75): your proof the store kept it verbatim. Pass false for <code>body_bytes</code> in its place on a long note. This argument is read by the server and never forwarded: it describes the response envelope, which is the transport's own business and not something <code>annotation.add</code> has an opinion about.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_annotate_task-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release.&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_annotate_task&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-annotation.add"><code>annotation.add</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_add_tokens">tasqx_add_tokens</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span></div><p>Record token spend on a task after the fact, e.g. a count that arrived after completion (D167). Send the split counts, or <code>total_tokens</code> alone when only one number is known — never both. Stored as a self-report at confidence <code>medium</code>, as on <code>tasqx_complete_task</code>: nothing can check it, so it is never <code>high</code> (D50); only a session-confirmed transcript or OTLP telemetry earns that. Reuse <code>idempotency_key</code> on a retry.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-token.add"><code>token.add</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-cache-creation-tokens" data-param="cache_creation_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-cache-read-tokens" data-param="cache_read_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache. Kept in its own bucket and never blended with the others (D48).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-idempotency-key" data-param="idempotency_key"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">idempotency_key</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The same key twice on one task banks once.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-input-tokens" data-param="input_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-model" data-param="model"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work. Recorded, never interpreted.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-output-tokens" data-param="output_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-tool" data-param="tool"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The AI tool that spent them; defaults to the handshake&#39;s client.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_tokens-total-tokens" data-param="total_tokens"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, instead of the four.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;:12000,&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;:91000,&quot;confidence&quot;:&quot;medium&quot;,&quot;input_tokens&quot;:18400,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;opus&quot;,&quot;output_tokens&quot;:2600,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;self-report&quot;,&quot;tool&quot;:&quot;claude-code&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_tokens&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-token.add"><code>token.add</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_annotation"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_remove_annotation">tasqx_remove_annotation</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Permanently scrub one annotation&#39;s text by id. Unlike every other write here this is a HARD delete: the body is overwritten in the store and the original <code>annotation.add</code> event&#39;s body is redacted in the same transaction, so a secret is gone from <code>event.list</code> and <code>store.export</code> too (D113). A text-free tombstone stays for audit under <code>annotations_removed</code>. <code>tasqx undo</code> does NOT cover this. An unknown or removed id is <code>not_found</code>.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_annotation-annotation-id" data-param="annotation_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The annotation&#39;s id, as tasqx_annotate_task or tasqx_get_task reports.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_annotation-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;annotation_id&quot;:&quot;17dd6621-7db4-43b5-9f36-ddf89018081e&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_annotation&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_update_annotation"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_update_annotation">tasqx_update_annotation</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Correct one annotation&#39;s body in place, by id (D165): id, timestamp and position are kept, and search stops finding the old text. <code>tasqx undo</code> covers it. An omitted <code>expected_rev</code> pins the task&#39;s current <code>_rev</code>, as on <code>tasqx_modify_task</code>.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-annotation.update"><code>annotation.update</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_annotation-annotation-id" data-param="annotation_id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The annotation&#39;s id, as tasqx_annotate_task or tasqx_get_task reports.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_annotation-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The corrected text; replaces the old body whole.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_annotation-expected-rev" data-param="expected_rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">expected_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Guard on the task&#39;s <code>_rev</code>; supplied by the server when omitted.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_annotation-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;annotation_id&quot;:&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7401-a1e6-c040f1ddbe51&quot;,&quot;body&quot;:&quot;Ruling: the guide ships AFTER the 3.0 release.&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_update_annotation&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-annotation.update"><code>annotation.update</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_add_dependency"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_add_dependency">tasqx_add_dependency</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Make one task depend on another: <code>ref</code> is blocked until <code>depends_on</code> is done or cancelled, and a <code>ref</code> already closed is never blocked. Returns the resulting dependency list and blocked state. A cycle is refused as a conflict.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-dependency.add"><code>dependency.add</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_dependency-depends-on" data-param="depends_on"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task <code>ref</code> must wait for: short_id or UUID.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_dependency-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;depends_on&quot;:&quot;50&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;55&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_dependency&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-dependency.add"><code>dependency.add</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_dependency"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_remove_dependency">tasqx_remove_dependency</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Cut a dependency edge: <code>ref</code> stops waiting on <code>depends_on</code>. Returns the remaining dependency list and blocked state, so the answer says whether the task is actionable now or still waiting on something else.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-dependency.remove"><code>dependency.remove</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_dependency-depends-on" data-param="depends_on"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocker to stop waiting for: short_id or UUID.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_dependency-ref" data-param="ref"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">ref</code><span class="badge">integer or string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;depends_on&quot;:&quot;50&quot;,&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;51&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_dependency&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-dependency.remove"><code>dependency.remove</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_add_memory"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_add_memory">tasqx_add_memory</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span></div><p>Store a knowledge document in memory: patterns, documentation, decisions worth finding again. The body is stored verbatim (markdown fine) and becomes searchable through tasqx_search_memory.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-memory.add"><code>memory.add</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_memory-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Stored verbatim; multi-line markdown is fine.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_memory-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optional project scope. Omit to leave the doc unscoped; it is never defaulted onto a current project.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_memory-source" data-param="source"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where this came from: a path, URL, or ticket. One doc per source: one another doc holds is a <code>conflict</code> naming it (D174).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_memory-standing" data-param="standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">True marks a ruling that belongs in every session of its scope until retracted; default false (D156).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_add_memory-title" data-param="title"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc's title. Indexed with the body, so the words a future search will use belong in it.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;60 requests a minute per key, burst 120.&quot;,&quot;project&quot;:&quot;api&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;notes/limits.md&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;rate-limit-ceiling&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_add_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-memory.add"><code>memory.add</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_update_memory">tasqx_update_memory</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span></div><p>Correct a memory doc in place — title, body, source and/or project — by id. Prefer it over a second <code>tasqx_add_memory</code>: a correction written as a new doc leaves the stale one polluting search rankings, and <code>tasqx_remove_memory</code> is permanent. Optimistic concurrency as on <code>tasqx_modify_task</code>: an omitted <code>expected_rev</code> pins the current <code>rev</code>, so a concurrent edit is a <code>conflict</code> naming both (D75).</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-memory.update"><code>memory.update</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory-body" data-param="body"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New body, stored verbatim. Omit to leave unchanged.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory-expected-rev" data-param="expected_rev"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">expected_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Optimistic-concurrency guard. Supplied by the server from the doc&#39;s current <code>rev</code> when omitted; pass it to pin a rev you read earlier.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory-id" data-param="id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc UUID, as a search hit, <code>tasqx_add_memory</code> or <code>tasqx_list_memory</code> prints it.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory-project" data-param="project"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New project scope. Omit to leave unchanged.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory-source" data-param="source"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New source. Omit to leave unchanged. One another doc holds is a <code>conflict</code> naming it (D174).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory-standing" data-param="standing"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Set or clear the standing flag; omit to leave unchanged (D156).</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_update_memory-title" data-param="title"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">New title. Omit to leave unchanged.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;body&quot;:&quot;The handover happens Friday at 16:00, in the on-call channel.&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;1bce1a9b-5134-4ab7-8665-34cd79fe0c5f&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_update_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-memory.update"><code>memory.update</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_memory"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_remove_memory">tasqx_remove_memory</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill req">destructive</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Remove one knowledge document from memory by id. Use it to retract something that turned out wrong: a correction written as a second document leaves both in the store, with search ranking them together. The removal is permanent — <code>tasqx undo</code> does not cover memory docs, and the body is not recoverable from the event log.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-memory.remove"><code>memory.remove</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_remove_memory-id" data-param="id"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The document&#39;s id, as tasqx_search_memory reports it on a <code>doc</code> hit.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;091eb5ff-05d5-4cb2-ba2f-0afdc77f7935&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_remove_memory&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-memory.remove"><code>memory.remove</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ref" id="mcp-tasqx_create_project"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-mcp-tasqx_create_project">tasqx_create_project</h3><div class="pills"><span class="pill req">write scope</span><span class="pill opt">idempotent</span></div><p>Create a project. Returns its id and name. It does NOT become the default project — MCP exposes no <code>project.use</code> (D22) — so pass <code>project</code> explicitly on every <code>tasqx_add_task</code> that should land here.</p><p>Routes to <a href="#api-project.create"><code>project.create</code></a>, and hands back that method's result — the shape is documented there, once.</p><h4>Arguments</h4><dl class="params"><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_create_project-description" data-param="description"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">description</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the project is for. Shown by `project.list` and nowhere load-bearing.</dd></div><div class="param" id="mcp-tasqx_create_project-name" data-param="name"><dt class="param-h"><code class="pname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">required</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project's name. Dotted names (`work.tasqx`) are free-form: nothing nests, and a filter on `work` does not match `work.tasqx`.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="tabs"><div class="tabstrip"><button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="MCP">MCP</button><button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="JSON API">JSON API</button></div><div class="tabpanel active" data-tab="MCP"><div class="termbox"><div class="snip-h"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre class="term"><code>{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;jsonrpc&quot;:&quot;2.0&quot;,&quot;method&quot;:&quot;tools/call&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;arguments&quot;:{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Prototypes and spikes&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;research&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tasqx_create_project&quot;}}</code></pre></div><p>The answer is <code>content</code> text: the method's result as JSON, unless the description above says this tool sends less of it by default — a rendered view, a compact row, no <code>rank</code> — in which case an argument marked <em>MCP only</em>, or <code>fields</code>, asks for the rest. <code>isError</code> is <code>true</code> for a refusal, which is a value and not a transport failure.</p></div><div class="tabpanel" data-tab="JSON API"><p>The same call as an envelope — arguments are the method's params, one for one — is under <a href="#api-project.create"><code>project.create</code></a>, with a real request and the response it produced.</p></div></div></div></section><h3 id="h-what-an-agent-cannot-reach">What an agent cannot reach</h3><p>An agent cannot reach every method: seventeen of them are deliberately off the tool surface. Not exposing a tool is a decision here rather than silence — each one names its reason, and a method that ships with neither a tool nor a line in this table fails the build:</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-29-h0">Method</th><th id="tbl-29-h1">Why not</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-core.capabilities"><code>core.capabilities</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">the MCP handshake already answers this question: <code>initialize</code> reports the protocol          revision and scope, and <code>tools/list</code> reports the surface. A second, differently          shaped capability document is a second thing to keep in sync.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-event.list"><code>event.list</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">the audit log is unbounded and has no paging, so exposing it would repeat the          <code>task.get</code> mistake D63 fixed. It needs the same limit/offset treatment before it          can be a tool; no client has asked for it yet.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-event.revert"><code>event.revert</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">tasqx has an undo (D54) and an agent cannot reach it, which is the sharpest single          omission on this list. It stays off until the tool can show what it is about to          undo: <code>event.revert</code> acts on the last matching event, and its blast radius depends          on store state the calling agent has not read. A destructive one-shot whose effect          the caller cannot see is not a tool, it is a coin flip.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-graph.query"><code>graph.query</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">an agent already reaches the graph&#39;s ends: <code>tasqx_search_memory</code> returns the docs and annotations the inferred half would match, and <code>tasqx_get_task</code> returns a task&#39;s notes, checks and dependencies. What <code>graph.query</code> adds over those is a LAYOUT — nodes, edges and provenance to draw — and that is a desktop client&#39;s question (D160), not something a model gains by reading two hundred node objects into its context.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-link.add"><code>link.add</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">D160&#39;s explicit links are a curation surface: an agent proposing edges between docs, tasks and decisions is exactly the noise the graph&#39;s inferred half already covers without persisting anything. A link is durable and shows as fact, so it stays a human act until a promotion flow exists for an agent to ask for one.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-link.list"><code>link.list</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">nothing asks for it yet: an agent reaching the graph wants a node&#39;s neighbourhood with labels, which is <code>graph.query</code>&#39;s job, not a page of endpoint ids it would then have to resolve one by one.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-link.remove"><code>link.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">the corrective half of <code>link.add</code>, off for the same reason: an agent that cannot write an edge has nothing of its own to retract, and deleting a human&#39;s curated link unsupervised is a bigger foot-gun than the gap it closes (<code>token.remove</code>&#39;s reasoning).</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-memory.import"><code>memory.import</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">it takes a batch of documents read off a filesystem, and the filesystem the CLI          reads is not the one an MCP client is on. <code>memory.add</code> is the per-document tool          that does reach across the wire.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-memory.refresh"><code>memory.refresh</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">the sweep re-reads the files <code>memory.import</code> recorded on THIS machine (D180), and the filesystem an MCP client is on is not that one — <code>memory.import</code>&#39;s own reason, one method over. Keeping a server&#39;s own docs fresh is the server&#39;s job, reached by calling the engine, not an agent&#39;s to trigger across the wire.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-otlp.status"><code>otlp.status</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">an operator diagnostic for a machine-local, opt-in receiver (#18) — is telemetry reaching THIS daemon on THIS machine — not a fact about any task an agent is working. <code>tasqx config store</code> / a CLI verb is where a human checks it (#222).</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-project.archive"><code>project.archive</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">retiring a project is a decision about the human&#39;s workspace, not about the work.          An agent asked to tidy the project list is being asked to make that decision on          their behalf, and the CLI is where it belongs.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-project.use"><code>project.use</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">ruled out by D22: an agent has <code>project</code> on <code>task.add</code> and should name it, rather          than silently re-aiming the human&#39;s default for every later call, including the          human&#39;s own.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-reminder.fire"><code>reminder.fire</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">daemon-internal. Its <code>reminded</code> event is a dedupe key and a push surface, not a          thing a client asks for.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">an agent cannot snapshot what it just wrote, and that is a real gap — but the          payload is the whole store, which is exactly the size problem D63 and D66 spent          two rounds on. It needs a filter and a budget before it is a tool rather than a          way to blow a client&#39;s limit in one call.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-store.import"><code>store.import</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">it overwrites, in bulk, from a document nobody has reviewed. The confirmation model          (§7) defers to the host&#39;s gate, and a host gate on a call whose diff nobody can see          is not a safeguard.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-token.remove"><code>token.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">the corrective half of <code>token.add</code> (#210), kept off although its other half is <code>tasqx_add_tokens</code> (D167): an agent that reports a wrong count fixes it by reporting the right one, and a removal an agent could reach unsupervised on the ledger a lead reads for budget decisions is a bigger foot-gun than the gap it closes. A human runs <code>tasqx api token.remove</code> instead.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Method" headers="tbl-29-h0"><a href="#api-tokens.recompute"><code>tokens.recompute</code></a></td><td data-label="Why not" headers="tbl-29-h1">a maintenance pass over the whole store&#39;s attribution. It is an operator action with          a runtime proportional to history, not a step in anybody&#39;s task.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#api"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">JSON API</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-task"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Task</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-task"><h2>Task</h2><p class="lead">A task is one piece of work: a title, the dates and priority that score its urgency, the time tracked against it, and everything hung off it — notes, acceptance criteria, dependencies and token spend, each documented on its own page. No method deletes a task, and <code>event.revert</code> refuses to undo its <code>add</code>: a finished task is <code>done</code>, an abandoned one <code>cancelled</code>, and <code>task.reopen</code> brings either back.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-task-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-task-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s uuid, stable across exports and machines.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s short id — the small number every <code>ref</code> accepts and the CLI prints.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s title, verbatim.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>pending</code>, <code>backlog</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>cancelled</code> — or, on a stored row whose status text this build does not recognize, that text verbatim, with <code>status_unrecognized: true</code> beside it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">priority</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>H</code>, <code>M</code>, <code>L</code>, or null for none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project the task belongs to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">due</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it is due, as an instant, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">scheduled</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When work is planned to start, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>, out of the working set, as with <code>wait</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">wait</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Holds the task out of the working set until this instant, or null. While it is in the future a <code>pending</code> task reads as <code>backlog</code>; <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">estimate</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The estimate as an ISO 8601 duration (<code>PT4H</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">recurrence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The recurrence rule (<code>every 3 days</code>), or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">remind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The reminder spec — an offset from <code>due</code> or an absolute instant — or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The urgency score (D1): priority, due proximity and age, summed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tags</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every tag on the task, as plain strings.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the task was captured.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">completed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When <code>task.done</code> completed it, or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it, and <code>task.cancel</code> does not set it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">budget_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The size gauge over FRESH tokens (D139), or null for no threshold. It stops nothing.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The task&#39;s revision counter. The methods that change the task or its tags, notes, checks and dependencies bump it; <code>token.add</code>, <code>token.remove</code> and <code>reminder.fire</code> leave it alone. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status_unrecognized</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present, and true, only on a row whose <code>status</code> no writer of this build could have produced — a store an older import wrote unvalidated, or a hand-edited one. <code>store.import</code> now refuses such a status.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Time on the clock as an ISO duration, the interval still running included up to the moment of the read (D166). <code>active_since</code> marks where that one began.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_adjustment</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The net of every <code>task.adjust_tracked</code> correction already inside <code>tracked</code>, as a signed ISO duration (<code>-PT2H25M</code>); <code>PT0S</code> when there is none.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">active_since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the open interval started, or null when the timer is not running.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">active_since</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The open interval&#39;s anchor, omitted when no timer is running.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_seconds</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tracked time in raw seconds (D42). Omitted when it would be zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tracked_adjustment_seconds</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The signed net of the <code>task.adjust_tracked</code> corrections inside <code>tracked_seconds</code> (D166). Omitted when it would be zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">fresh_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh tokens spent on this task — input, output and cache creation, never cache reads (D139), plus any unsplit <code>total_tokens</code> in full (D167).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">over</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether <code>fresh_tokens</code> is past <code>budget_tokens</code>; null when no budget was set, because there is no verdict to give.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">spawned_from</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short id of the task whose completion spawned this one (a recurrence, D170); null on any other task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">spawned_from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The uuid of the task whose completion spawned this one (D170). Omitted on any other task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency_breakdown</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The terms <code>urgency</code> sums — present only when <code>explain: true</code> asked for them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency_breakdown.priority</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The priority term.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency_breakdown.due_proximity</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The due-date term.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency_breakdown.age</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The age term.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">urgency_breakdown.total</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The sum — the same number as the row&#39;s <code>urgency</code>, so nobody has to recompute the rounding.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;active_since&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;annotations&quot;</span>: [
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release, not after it. A migration note that lands a week late is a support ticket that already happened.&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-11T11:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;17dd6621-7db4-43b5-9f36-ddf89018081e&quot;</span>
    },
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Blocked until the rate limit lands: the guide has to state the real ceiling, and quoting a number that then changes is worse than waiting.&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-15T11:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ee4a9a3b-10de-465a-aab1-84eeb0e48236&quot;</span>
    },
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Scope: the 2.x → 3.0 rename table, the auth change, and a worked example per SDK. Not the reference — that generates itself.&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-04T11:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;fd496ca3-cd12-4457-8b43-5ef0668cab3c&quot;</span>
    }
  ],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;annotations_next_offset&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;annotations_offset&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;annotations_removed&quot;</span>: [],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;annotations_total&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">3</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;blocked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;blocks&quot;</span>: [],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;budget_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;checks&quot;</span>: [
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Every renamed symbol has a row in the table&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-04T11:30:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;evidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ebb86ee2-69ed-4938-b57c-c12a89e9414e&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-14T09:10:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;position&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;state&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;passed&quot;</span>
    },
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;One worked example per SDK (js, py, go)&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-04T11:30:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;evidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;6776fd34-ec65-4b9e-8ce6-a106f4f51c13&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-14T09:10:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;position&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">1</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;state&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;passed&quot;</span>
    },
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;The rate-limit ceiling is stated with its real number&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-04T11:30:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;evidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;7e37a508-7921-4cb2-bf0c-0a2944eb31e4&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-14T09:10:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;position&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;state&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;open&quot;</span>
    },
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Reviewed by whoever ships 3.0&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-04T11:30:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;evidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;e6a1096b-6f05-4e95-96f5-52452080f2ac&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-14T09:10:00Z&quot;</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;position&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">3</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;state&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;open&quot;</span>
    }
  ],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;completed&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;delivered_annotation&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;delivered_annotation_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;depends_on&quot;</span>: [
    <span class="j-n">50</span>
  ],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;due&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-21T00:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;estimate&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT5H&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;first_annotation&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release, not after it. A migration note that lands a week late is a support ticket that already happened.&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-11T11:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;17dd6621-7db4-43b5-9f36-ddf89018081e&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;fresh_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;over&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;priority&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;M&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;recurrence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;remind&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;scheduled&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;spawned_from&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tags&quot;</span>: [
    <span class="j-s">&quot;docs&quot;</span>
  ],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tokens&quot;</span>: [],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tracked_adjustment&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;PT0S&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;unmet_blockers&quot;</span>: [
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">50</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Rate-limit the /search endpoint&quot;</span>
    }
  ],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;urgency&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">12.2</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;wait&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-task-lifecycle">Lifecycle</h3><p>A task has five statuses. Three are open — <code>backlog</code>, <code>pending</code> and <code>active</code> — and two are closed: <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code>. Each arrow is labelled with the method that makes the move.</p><pre class="plain"><code>                          task.add
                              │
 ┌─ open ─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┐
 │                            v                             │
 │  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
 │  │ backlog  while a future wait or scheduled date     │  │
 │  │          holds it                                  │  │
 │  │ pending  otherwise — the clock and task.modify     │  │
 │  │          move a task between the two               │  │
 │  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
 │     │                  ^                          ^      │
 │     │ task.start       │ task.stop, or            │      │
 │     │ (pending only)   │ another task.start       │      │
 │     v                  │ without keep (D6)        │      │
 │  ┌──────────────────────────┐                     │      │
 │  │          active          │                     │      │
 │  └──────────────────────────┘                     │      │
 └────────────┬──────────────────────┬───────────────┼──────┘
              │ task.done from       │ task.cancel   │
              │ pending or active    │ from any      │
              │                      │ open status   │
              v                      v               │
         ┌─────────┐           ┌───────────┐         │
         │  done   │           │ cancelled │         │
         └─────────┘           └───────────┘         │
              │                      │               │
              └──────────────────────┴───────────────┘
                            task.reopen</code></pre><p><code>backlog</code> and <code>pending</code> are one question asked of the clock every time a task is read: a task is in <code>backlog</code> while its <code>wait</code> or <code>scheduled</code> instant is still in the future, and in <code>pending</code> otherwise. Only those two statuses are read against the clock: <code>active</code>, <code>done</code> and <code>cancelled</code> keep their status whatever the task's dates say. So every arrow into that box lands in whichever of the two the task's dates say — a task added, stopped or reopened with a future date is in <code>backlog</code>, and moves to <code>pending</code> only once neither its <code>wait</code> nor its <code>scheduled</code> is still in the future — each has passed or been cleared with <code>task.modify</code>. There is no separate waiting status. <code>task.start</code> and <code>task.done</code> refuse a backlog task. Starting a task without <code>keep</code> stops every task already running (D6), with one exception (D140): when the start names an <code>actor</code> and the most recently started running clock was started under a different named actor, the start is refused instead. A start that names no actor, as <code>tasqx start</code> sends none, auto-stops as usual; the MCP server fills in its connection's id when a call names none. When the newest event is a <code>task.stop</code>, <code>event.revert</code> takes it back, putting the task back to <code>active</code> if it is still <code>pending</code>. <code>task.modify</code> refuses a <code>status</code> other than <code>cancelled</code>.</p><p><strong>Blocked</strong> is not a status either: it is the <a href="#obj-dependency"><code>blocked</code></a> flag, true while an open task waits on a task that is neither done nor cancelled. <code>@working</code> is pending or active and not blocked, and <code>task.done</code> refuses a blocked task unless <code>force</code> records the override (D150).</p><section class="ref" id="obj-task-urgency"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-task-urgency">Urgency</h3><p><code>urgency</code> is one fixed formula (D1), the sum of three terms rounded to one decimal. The weights are not configurable.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-30-h0">Term</th><th id="tbl-30-h1">Score</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Term" headers="tbl-30-h0">priority</td><td data-label="Score" headers="tbl-30-h1"><code>H</code> 6.0 · <code>M</code> 3.9 · <code>L</code> 1.8 · <code>none</code> 0.0</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Term" headers="tbl-30-h0">due proximity</td><td data-label="Score" headers="tbl-30-h1">12 once the due date is reached or past; before that 12 × (1 − days left ÷ 14), never below 0 — a due date more than 14 days away adds nothing. No due date, 0.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Term" headers="tbl-30-h0">age</td><td data-label="Score" headers="tbl-30-h1">0.01 per day since <code>created</code>, capped at 1.0.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><code>tasqx why</code> prints the three terms for one task. The screen beside this is a task in the demo store: the terms, then their sum, then what still blocks it. <code>task.get</code> with <code>explain: true</code> answers the same terms as <a href="#obj-task-fields"><code>urgency_breakdown</code></a>.</p></div><div class="ref-code"><div class="snip"><div class="snip-h"><span class="dollar">$</span></div><pre class="cmd"><code>tasqx why 51</code></pre><pre class="term"><span style="color:#8a8a8a">#51</span>  <span style="font-weight:700">Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0</span>

  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">priority  </span> M           3.9
  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">deadline  </span> due Mon     8.0
  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">age       </span> 30 days     0.3
  <span style="color:#8a8a8a">urgency   </span>          <span style="font-weight:700">  12.2</span>
  <span style="color:#bf616a;font-weight:700">blocked by</span> #50 Rate-limit the /search endpoint — `next` skips this task
</pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-task-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-31-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-31-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-31-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.add"><code>task.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-add"><code>add</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_task"><code>tasqx_add_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a> · <a href="#cli-agenda"><code>agenda</code></a> · <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a> · <a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> · <a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-watch"><code>watch</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_tasks"><code>tasqx_list_tasks</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_task"><code>tasqx_get_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-brief"><code>brief</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.start"><code>task.start</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-start"><code>start</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_start_timer"><code>tasqx_start_timer</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.stop"><code>task.stop</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-stop"><code>stop</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_stop_timer"><code>tasqx_stop_timer</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.adjust_tracked"><code>task.adjust_tracked</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-adjust"><code>adjust</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_adjust_tracked"><code>tasqx_adjust_tracked</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_complete_task"><code>tasqx_complete_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.modify"><code>task.modify</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-modify"><code>modify</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_modify_task"><code>tasqx_modify_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.cancel"><code>task.cancel</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-cancel"><code>cancel</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_cancel_task"><code>tasqx_cancel_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-task.reopen"><code>task.reopen</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-reopen"><code>reopen</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_reopen_task"><code>tasqx_reopen_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-tag.add"><code>tag.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-tag"><code>tag</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_tag_task"><code>tasqx_tag_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-tag.remove"><code>tag.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-untag"><code>untag</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_untag_task"><code>tasqx_untag_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-31-h0"><a href="#api-reminder.fire"><code>reminder.fire</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-31-h1">—</td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-31-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#mcp"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">MCP</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-project"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Project</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-project"><h2>Project</h2><p class="lead">A project is a name tasks and knowledge docs are filed under. One project can be the store's default, where a task added without a project lands. Archiving hides a project and removes nothing.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-project-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-project-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s name — the value <code>project:</code> filters on and <code>task.add</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">name</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its name — what a task&#39;s <code>project</code> names.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">description</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project&#39;s description, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">description</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its description, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">archived</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the project is archived. Archived projects are omitted unless <code>include_archived</code> asked for them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">archived</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether it is archived.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">default</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether this is the project a bare <code>task.add</code> lands in.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was created.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a>, at <code>result/projects/0</code>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;archived&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Public REST API and its SDKs&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;309d6b79-965e-4a32-9ae4-45508201e2bd&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-project-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-32-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-32-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-32-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-32-h0"><a href="#api-project.create"><code>project.create</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-32-h1"><a href="#cli-init"><code>init</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-32-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_create_project"><code>tasqx_create_project</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-32-h0"><a href="#api-project.list"><code>project.list</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-32-h1"><a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> · <a href="#cli-projects"><code>projects</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-32-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_projects"><code>tasqx_list_projects</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-32-h0"><a href="#api-project.use"><code>project.use</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-32-h1"><a href="#cli-use"><code>use</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-32-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-32-h0"><a href="#api-project.archive"><code>project.archive</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-32-h1"><a href="#cli-archive"><code>archive</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-32-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-32-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-32-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-32-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-task"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Task</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-annotation"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Annotation</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-annotation"><h2>Annotation</h2><p class="lead">An annotation is a note on a task, stored verbatim. <code>annotation.update</code> corrects one in place, keeping its id, timestamp and position (D165), and <code>store.import</code> replaces an imported task's notes with the document's. <code>annotation.remove</code> scrubs a note's text and leaves a tombstone — its id and when it went — under <code>annotations_removed</code>; undoing the <code>annotation.add</code> that wrote a note deletes it outright, with no tombstone.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-annotation-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-annotation-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note&#39;s uuid — what <code>annotation.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note, stored verbatim (D41). <code>task.get</code> and <code>task.brief</code> given <code>max_body_bytes</code> return a prefix of a longer body and mark it with <code>body_truncated</code> and <code>body_bytes</code> (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the note was written.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_bytes</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The body&#39;s real size in bytes. Present only on a body this response cut (D148).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Present and true only on a body this response cut, so &quot;was this cut?&quot; stays a presence question.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_removed[].id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The scrubbed note&#39;s id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed.id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The scrubbed note&#39;s id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_removed[].removed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was scrubbed. Never the text — that is the point of the method.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">removed.removed</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was scrubbed. Never the text — that is the point of the method.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath">On a task</div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The notes on this task, oldest first within the page. Pages are counted back from the newest note, so <code>annotations_offset: 0</code> is the most recent page.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every note on the task — an export carries the whole history, unpaged.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">annotations_removed</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One tombstone per scrubbed note (D113) — id and instant, never the text. Excluded from <code>annotations</code> and its total.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note <code>task.done</code> pinned as the delivery note — the newest one at the instant of completion — or null. <code>task.reopen</code> clears it (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The note <code>task.done</code> pinned as the delivery note (D165). Present only on a task a completion pinned one on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">first_annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The oldest note, whatever page <code>annotations_limit</code>/<code>annotations_offset</code> asked for — the card&#39;s Description — or null when there is none (D165).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">delivered_annotation</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The pinned delivery note — on a closed task with no pin, the newest note — or null on an open task, or when the pinned note was removed (D165).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>, at <code>result/annotations/0</code>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Ruling: the guide ships WITH the 3.0 release, not after it. A migration note that lands a week late is a support ticket that already happened.&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-11T11:20:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;17dd6621-7db4-43b5-9f36-ddf89018081e&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-annotation-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-33-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-33-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-33-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-33-h0"><a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-33-h1"><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-33-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_task"><code>tasqx_get_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-33-h0"><a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-33-h1"><a href="#cli-brief"><code>brief</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-33-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-33-h0"><a href="#api-annotation.add"><code>annotation.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-33-h1"><a href="#cli-annotate"><code>annotate</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-33-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_annotate_task"><code>tasqx_annotate_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-33-h0"><a href="#api-annotation.remove"><code>annotation.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-33-h1"><a href="#cli-unannotate"><code>unannotate</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-33-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_annotation"><code>tasqx_remove_annotation</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-33-h0"><a href="#api-annotation.update"><code>annotation.update</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-33-h1"><a href="#cli-annotate"><code>annotate</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-33-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_update_annotation"><code>tasqx_update_annotation</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-33-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-33-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-33-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-project"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Project</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-check"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Check</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-check"><h2>Check</h2><p class="lead">A check is one acceptance criterion on a task (D138): a sentence tasqx stores and does not execute. It starts <code>open</code>, and <code>check.set</code> moves it to <code>passed</code>, <code>failed</code> or back to <code>open</code>, with the evidence that decided it.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-check-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-check-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion&#39;s uuid — what <code>check.set</code> and <code>check.remove</code> take.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The criterion itself, stored verbatim. tasqx never runs it; it is a claim, not a command.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">state</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>open</code>, <code>passed</code> or <code>failed</code>. A failure is a normal outcome, not an error.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">evidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The citation for the state, or null — some criteria are met by something nobody can quote.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">position</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it sits in the list, from zero.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the criterion was added.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When its state or evidence last changed.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath">On a task</div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">checks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The acceptance criteria on the task, in position order (D138).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>, at <code>result/checks/0</code>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Every renamed symbol has a row in the table&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-04T11:30:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;evidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;ebb86ee2-69ed-4938-b57c-c12a89e9414e&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-14T09:10:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;position&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;state&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;passed&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-check-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-34-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-34-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-34-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-34-h0"><a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-34-h1"><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-34-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_task"><code>tasqx_get_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-34-h0"><a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-34-h1"><a href="#cli-brief"><code>brief</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-34-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-34-h0"><a href="#api-check.add"><code>check.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-34-h1"><a href="#cli-check"><code>check</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-34-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_check"><code>tasqx_add_check</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-34-h0"><a href="#api-check.set"><code>check.set</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-34-h1"><a href="#cli-check"><code>check</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-34-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_set_check"><code>tasqx_set_check</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-34-h0"><a href="#api-check.remove"><code>check.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-34-h1"><a href="#cli-check"><code>check</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-34-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_check"><code>tasqx_remove_check</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-34-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-34-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-34-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-annotation"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Annotation</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-dependency"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Dependency</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-dependency"><h2>Dependency</h2><p class="lead">A dependency is an edge between two tasks: this task waits on that one. It has no id of its own: the API reads it off the tasks at both ends — <code>depends_on</code> on the task that waits, <code>blocks</code> on the one it waits on. A task is <code>blocked</code> while it is open and at least one task it waits on is neither <code>done</code> nor <code>cancelled</code>.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-dependency-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-dependency-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">depends_on</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this task waits on.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocks</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The short ids this task is holding back — the reverse edge of <code>depends_on</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether an unmet dependency is holding this task back.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unmet_blockers</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The open prerequisites, named — what <code>blocked: true</code> is blocked ON.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unmet_blockers[].short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s short id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked_by[].short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s short id.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">unmet_blockers[].title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s title, so a refusal can be read without a second call.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">blocked_by[].title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The blocking task&#39;s title, so a refusal can be read without a second call.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;blocked&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">true</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;blocks&quot;</span>: [],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;depends_on&quot;</span>: [
    <span class="j-n">50</span>
  ],
  <span class="j-k">&quot;unmet_blockers&quot;</span>: [
    {
      <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">50</span>,
      <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Rate-limit the /search endpoint&quot;</span>
    }
  ]
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-dependency-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-35-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-35-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-35-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-35-h0"><a href="#api-task.list"><code>task.list</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-35-h1"><a href="#cli-list"><code>list</code></a> · <a href="#cli-agenda"><code>agenda</code></a> · <a href="#cli-next"><code>next</code></a> · <a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> · <a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-watch"><code>watch</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-35-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_tasks"><code>tasqx_list_tasks</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-35-h0"><a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-35-h1"><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-35-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_task"><code>tasqx_get_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-35-h0"><a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-35-h1"><a href="#cli-brief"><code>brief</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-35-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-35-h0"><a href="#api-task.done"><code>task.done</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-35-h1"><a href="#cli-done"><code>done</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-35-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_complete_task"><code>tasqx_complete_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-35-h0"><a href="#api-dependency.add"><code>dependency.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-35-h1"><a href="#cli-dep"><code>dep</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-35-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_dependency"><code>tasqx_add_dependency</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-35-h0"><a href="#api-dependency.remove"><code>dependency.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-35-h1"><a href="#cli-undep"><code>undep</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-35-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_dependency"><code>tasqx_remove_dependency</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-35-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-35-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-35-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-check"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Check</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-memory"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Memory document</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-memory"><h2>Memory document</h2><p class="lead">A memory document is a piece of knowledge the store keeps beside the tasks: a title and a body, searchable together with the notes on tasks. It can be scoped to a project and marked standing (D156). Importing a doc with a <code>source</code> already stored replaces that doc in place; removing one is permanent.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-memory-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-memory-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it came from — the path <code>memory.import</code> keyed on, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where it came from, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">The doc&#39;s title.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">title</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Its title.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The whole body, stored and returned verbatim (D41).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was first stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it was stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it last changed — the column this list sorts by.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project it is scoped to, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">_rev</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The row&#39;s revision counter, bumped by every write. Send it back as <code>expected_rev</code> to make a change conditional.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether it is a standing ruling, meant for every session of its scope (D156). Stated on every doc, so a restore carries it.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">standing</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether it is a standing ruling (D156) — on every row, not only on a page filtered by <code>standing</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_path</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The absolute path of the file <code>memory.import</code> read this doc from, or null when no import set one (D180).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_mtime</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That file&#39;s modification time in unix seconds when it was read, or null (D180).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">origin_size</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That file&#39;s size in bytes when it was read, or null (D180).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_preview</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The opening of the body, or all of it when the body is short (<code>body_truncated</code> says which) — browsing pays for a preview, not a payload.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">body_truncated</code><span class="badge">boolean</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Whether the preview is shorter than the body.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;_rev&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;body&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;---\ndescription: How an SDK release is cut, tagged and announced\n---\nCut the release branch on Monday, tag after the canary has run for a day, and announce in the changelog feed once the packages are live.&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-05T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-10T09:15:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_mtime&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_path&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;origin_size&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;docs/release.md&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;standing&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;release-process&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-memory-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-36-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-36-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-36-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-brief"><code>brief</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.add"><code>memory.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_memory"><code>tasqx_add_memory</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.search"><code>memory.search</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_search_memory"><code>tasqx_search_memory</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.get"><code>memory.get</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_memory"><code>tasqx_get_memory</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.remove"><code>memory.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_remove_memory"><code>tasqx_remove_memory</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.import"><code>memory.import</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.refresh"><code>memory.refresh</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.list"><code>memory.list</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_list_memory"><code>tasqx_list_memory</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-memory.update"><code>memory.update</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-memory"><code>memory</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_update_memory"><code>tasqx_update_memory</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-36-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-36-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-36-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-dependency"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Dependency</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-link"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Link</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-link"><h2>Link</h2><p class="lead">A link is an explicit edge between two nodes of the knowledge graph (D160): a task, a memory document, an annotation or a project at either end, and a relation naming what it asserts. Links are written and removed, never edited, and a repeat of one that already exists answers with the link that is there rather than a second row. Unlike a dependency they may form cycles, and unlike an inferred graph edge they are durable: nothing mints one but a caller who asked for it. Removing a memory document removes its links with it; an annotation tombstone leaves them alone, because the node is still there.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-link-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-link-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The link&#39;s uuid — what <code>link.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link starts at, as <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code>: <code>task:</code>, <code>memory:</code>, <code>annotation:</code> or <code>project:</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">to</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node the link points at, spelled the same way.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the link asserts: <code>references</code>, <code>supersedes</code>, <code>implements_decision</code>, <code>derived_from</code> or <code>contradicts</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">metadata</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The caller&#39;s own object, stored verbatim and never interpreted, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created_at</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the link was written. Named <code>created_at</code> because <code>link.add</code> answers with a boolean <code>created</code> beside it.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-link.add"><code>link.add</code></a>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;created_at&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-17T09:12:04Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;from&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:019f7c0a-3d51-7c42-9a08-1f0c4e5b62d7&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f8b31-77a4-7f10-8c55-2d7e9a13b004&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;metadata&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;relation&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;implements_decision&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;to&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;memory:eb864f1e-e68a-4d96-af89-597bd0d2d52e&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> a new link mints a fresh v7 id whose low bits are random, and the response also carries the task&#39;s own uuid — the pinned clock fixes the timestamp half of each and nothing fixes the rest, so a captured answer would differ on every run.</p></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-link-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-37-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-37-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-37-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-37-h0"><a href="#api-link.add"><code>link.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-37-h1">—</td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-37-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-37-h0"><a href="#api-link.remove"><code>link.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-37-h1">—</td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-37-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-37-h0"><a href="#api-link.list"><code>link.list</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-37-h1">—</td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-37-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-37-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-37-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-37-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-memory"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Memory document</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-graph"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Graph</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-graph"><h2>Graph</h2><p class="lead">A graph projection is what <code>graph.query</code> hands back: the nodes around one root and the edges between them, bounded and deterministically ordered so the same call twice is the same picture. A node is a task, a memory document, an annotation or a project, wearing the id a link's endpoints use. An edge is either <em>structural</em> — read out of a table, and naming that table as its <code>source</code> — or <em>inferred</em>, computed for that one call from an FTS search on the root's title or from the tags two tasks share, carrying a <code>confidence</code> and stored nowhere. Nothing here is a row in the store: a projection is a view, and the durable edges it draws are <a href="#obj-link">links</a>.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-graph-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-graph-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node&#39;s stable id, <code>&lt;type&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;</code> — the same spelling a link&#39;s endpoints use, and what a follow-up <code>graph.query</code> takes as its <code>root</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">type</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which kind of node: <code>task</code>, <code>memory</code>, <code>annotation</code> or <code>project</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">label</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The one line to draw in the box: a task&#39;s title, a document&#39;s title, a note&#39;s first line (cut to 80 characters) or a project&#39;s name.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">summary</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The second line: <code>#&lt;short_id&gt; · &lt;status&gt; · &lt;priority&gt;</code> for a task, the source for a document, the owning task for a note, the description for a project. Null when a project has no description.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">project</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The project this node is filed under, or null — including on a project node, which is not filed under itself.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">status</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">A task&#39;s status, read the way every other surface reads it (a future <code>wait</code> shows <code>backlog</code>). Null on every other kind of node.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">modified</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the node last changed: <code>modified</code> for a task or a document, <code>created</code> for a note, which is never edited. Null for a project, which carries no such column — so the date window cannot exclude one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">short_id</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The small number a human types for a task. Null on every other kind of node.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">task</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node id of the task a note is written on. Null on every other kind of node.</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath">Edges</div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The edge&#39;s id, stable for the same edge across calls: <code>dep:</code>, <code>ann:</code>, <code>member:</code> or <code>link:</code> for a stored one, <code>search:</code> or <code>tag:</code> for a computed one.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">from</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node id the edge starts at. A <code>depends_on</code> edge always points from the task that waits to the one it waits on, whichever end the walk reached it from.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">to</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The node id the edge points at.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">relation</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What the edge asserts: <code>depends_on</code>, <code>has_annotation</code>, <code>belongs_to_project</code>, one of the five link relations, or <code>search_match</code>/<code>shared_tag</code> when <code>include_inferred</code> asked for them.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">kind</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d"><code>structural</code> for an edge read out of a table, <code>inferred</code> for one computed for this call and never stored.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">number</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How strong a computed edge is, 0 to 1 within this answer. Null on a structural edge: a stored fact has no confidence to report.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Where the edge came from: the table (<code>dependencies</code>, <code>annotations</code>, <code>tasks.project</code>, <code>docs.project</code>, <code>links</code>) or what computed it (<code>memory.search: &lt;words&gt;</code>, <code>tags: &lt;shared&gt;</code>).</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-graph.query"><code>graph.query</code></a>, at <code>result/nodes/0</code>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task:46773aad-c4aa-435a-abe1-fcde8ce09658&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;label&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;Write the migration guide for SDK 3.0&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;modified&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-08-16T10:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;project&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;api&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;short_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">51</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;status&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;pending&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;summary&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;#51 · pending · M&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;task&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;type&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;task&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-graph-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-38-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-38-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-38-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-38-h0"><a href="#api-graph.query"><code>graph.query</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-38-h1">—</td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-38-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-link"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Link</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-event"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Event</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-event"><h2>Event</h2><p class="lead">An event is one row of the audit log. Writes to tasks — their notes, checks, dependencies and measurements included — to projects and to memory documents append one. Events are not edited, with one narrow exception: <code>annotation.remove</code> redacts the body out of the <code>annotation.add</code> event that wrote the note, so a removed note's text does not survive in the log. <code>event.revert</code> rewrites nothing either: it undoes the newest event by appending its inverse, and refuses by name the ops it cannot reverse.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-event-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-event-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The event&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">entity</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What kind of thing it happened to: <code>task</code>, <code>project</code>, <code>doc</code> or <code>link</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">entity_id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">That thing&#39;s uuid.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">op</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">What happened: <code>add</code>, <code>done</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>tag.remove</code>, …</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">payload</code><span class="badge">object</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The op&#39;s own vocabulary. Null only for a row whose payload will not parse — a corrupt store.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">ts</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When it happened.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">actor</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Who did it, when the caller said, or null.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-event.list"><code>event.list</code></a>, at <code>result/events/0</code>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;actor&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;user&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;entity&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;project&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;entity_id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;73f778aa-f6fa-4db8-a56a-bd72fb710734&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;a66b0d38-9d95-447e-bd29-9753a7677796&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;op&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;create&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;payload&quot;</span>: {
    <span class="j-k">&quot;default&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">false</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;description&quot;</span>: <span class="j-b">null</span>,
    <span class="j-k">&quot;name&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;home&quot;</span>
  },
  <span class="j-k">&quot;ts&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-06-18T00:00:00Z&quot;</span>
}</code></pre></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-event-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-39-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-39-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-39-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-39-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-39-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-39-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-39-h0"><a href="#api-event.list"><code>event.list</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-39-h1"><a href="#cli-dashboard"><code>dashboard</code></a> · <a href="#cli-chart"><code>chart</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-39-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-39-h0"><a href="#api-event.revert"><code>event.revert</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-39-h1"><a href="#cli-undo"><code>undo</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-39-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-graph"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Graph</span></a><a class="next" href="#obj-measurement"><span class="pn-k">Next</span><span class="pn-l">Token measurement</span></a></div></section><section class="page" id="obj-measurement"><h2>Token measurement</h2><p class="lead">A token measurement is AI token spend banked against a task: four buckets kept apart (D48), the tool and model that spent them, and how checkable the figure is. A task's measurements are read under <code>tokens</code>.</p><section class="ref" id="obj-measurement-fields"><div class="ref-main"><h3 class="ref-h" id="h-obj-measurement-fields">Fields</h3><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">id</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The measurement&#39;s uuid — what <code>token.remove</code> takes.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tool</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Which tool spent the tokens (<code>claude-code</code>, <code>codex</code>, …).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">source</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How the figure was obtained: <code>self-report</code>, <code>log-parse</code> or <code>otel</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">model</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill opt">nullable</span></dt><dd class="param-d">The model that did the work, or null.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">input_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Fresh input tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">output_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Output tokens.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_read_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens read from cache — never blended with the others (D48).</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">cache_creation_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">Tokens spent writing the cache.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">confidence</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">How checkable the figure is: <code>high</code>, <code>medium</code> or <code>low</code>. A self-report may not claim <code>high</code>.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">created</code><span class="badge">string</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">When the measurement was banked.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">total_tokens</code><span class="badge">integer</span><span class="pill req">always</span></dt><dd class="param-d">One unsplit count, from a reporter that could not split it — 0 on a split measurement, and never folded into the four (D167).</dd></div></dl><div class="shapepath">On a task</div><dl class="params"><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill req">always</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a> · <a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every token measurement banked against this task.</dd></div><div class="param field"><dt class="param-h"><code class="fname">tokens</code><span class="badge">array</span><span class="pill opt">optional</span><span class="pdef">in <a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></span></dt><dd class="param-d">Every token measurement against this task. Omitted entirely for a task that has none.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ref-code"><p>From <a href="#api-token.add"><code>token.add</code></a>, at <code>result/measurement</code>.</p><div class="snip"><pre class="out json"><code>{
  <span class="j-k">&quot;cache_creation_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">12000</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;cache_read_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">91000</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;confidence&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;medium&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;created&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;2026-09-16T09:00:00Z&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;019f7c0a-3d51-7d22-b73c-9353de0a3360&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;input_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">18400</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;model&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;opus&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;output_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">2600</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;source&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;self-report&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;tool&quot;</span>: <span class="j-s">&quot;claude-code&quot;</span>,
  <span class="j-k">&quot;total_tokens&quot;</span>: <span class="j-n">0</span>
}</code></pre></div><div class="callout note"><span class="tag">Note</span><p><strong>Illustrative.</strong> the measurement&#39;s id is minted fresh, v7, half of it random.</p></div></div></section><h3 id="obj-measurement-ops">Operations</h3><p>Every method that acts on this object or answers with it, and the verb and tool that reach it.</p><div class="tw"><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th id="tbl-40-h0">JSON API</th><th id="tbl-40-h1">CLI</th><th id="tbl-40-h2">MCP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-40-h0"><a href="#api-task.get"><code>task.get</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-40-h1"><a href="#cli-pick"><code>pick</code></a> · <a href="#cli-show"><code>show</code></a> · <a href="#cli-why"><code>why</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-40-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_get_task"><code>tasqx_get_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-40-h0"><a href="#api-task.brief"><code>task.brief</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-40-h1"><a href="#cli-brief"><code>brief</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-40-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_brief_task"><code>tasqx_brief_task</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-40-h0"><a href="#api-token.add"><code>token.add</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-40-h1"><a href="#cli-tokens"><code>tokens</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-40-h2"><a href="#mcp-tasqx_add_tokens"><code>tasqx_add_tokens</code></a></td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-40-h0"><a href="#api-token.remove"><code>token.remove</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-40-h1">—</td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-40-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-40-h0"><a href="#api-tokens.recompute"><code>tokens.recompute</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-40-h1"><a href="#cli-tokens"><code>tokens</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-40-h2">—</td></tr><tr><td data-label="JSON API" headers="tbl-40-h0"><a href="#api-store.export"><code>store.export</code></a></td><td data-label="CLI" headers="tbl-40-h1"><a href="#cli-export"><code>export</code></a></td><td data-label="MCP" headers="tbl-40-h2">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="pagenav"><a class="prev" href="#obj-event"><span class="pn-k">Previous</span><span class="pn-l">Event</span></a></div></section></main></div><footer>tasqx 0.14.0 · every command and every block of output on this page was executed against this binary. One file, no external requests.</footer>
<script>
(function () {
  function list(sel, root) {
    return Array.prototype.slice.call((root || document).querySelectorAll(sel));
  }
  var pages = list('.page');
  if (!pages.length) { return; }
  var navEl = document.getElementById('nav');
  var tree = document.getElementById('navtree');
  var hits = document.getElementById('navhits');
  var queryBox = document.getElementById('navq');
  var navLinks = list('nav a[data-page]');
  var THEME_KEY = 'tasqx-docs-theme';
  var TAB_KEY = 'tasqx-docs-tab';

  // Only hide pages once we know we can show them again.
  document.documentElement.classList.add('js');

  function readStore(k) {
    try { return window.localStorage.getItem(k); } catch (e) { return null; }
  }
  function writeStore(k, v) {
    try { window.localStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch (e) { /* storage refused */ }
  }

  // ---- theme: light / dark / system ---------------------------------------
  var themeBtns = list('.themebtn');
  function applyTheme(mode) {
    var root = document.documentElement;
    if (mode === 'light' || mode === 'dark') {
      root.setAttribute('data-theme', mode);
    } else {
      root.removeAttribute('data-theme');
      mode = 'system';
    }
    themeBtns.forEach(function (b) {
      var on = b.getAttribute('data-theme-set') === mode;
      b.classList.toggle('active', on);
      b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
    });
  }
  applyTheme(readStore(THEME_KEY) || 'system');

  // ---- code tabs -----------------------------------------------------------
  function applyTab(box, label) {
    var panels = list('.tabpanel', box), found = null;
    panels.forEach(function (p) {
      if (p.getAttribute('data-tab') === label) { found = p; }
    });
    if (!found) { return false; }
    panels.forEach(function (p) { p.classList.toggle('active', p === found); });
    list('.tab', box).forEach(function (b) {
      b.classList.toggle('active', b.getAttribute('data-tab') === label);
    });
    return true;
  }
  var storedTab = readStore(TAB_KEY);
  if (storedTab) {
    list('.tabs').forEach(function (box) {
      var panels = list('.tabpanel', box), wanted = null;
      panels.forEach(function (p) {
        if (p.getAttribute('data-tab') === storedTab) { wanted = p; }
      });
      // A remembered label whose panel is a placeholder is not applied: the
      // reader would land on "coming soon" in every section at once.
      if (wanted && !wanted.querySelector('.soon')) { applyTab(box, storedTab); }
    });
  }

  // ---- one page at a time, driven by the hash ------------------------------
  function pageFor(id) {
    var direct = null;
    pages.forEach(function (p) { if (p.id === id) { direct = p; } });
    if (direct) { return { page: direct, target: null }; }
    var el = id ? document.getElementById(id) : null;
    var owner = el && el.closest ? el.closest('.page') : null;
    return { page: owner, target: owner ? el : null };
  }
  function show(id) {
    pages.forEach(function (p) { p.classList.toggle('active', p.id === id); });
    navLinks.forEach(function (a) {
      a.classList.toggle('active', a.getAttribute('data-page') === id);
    });
    if (navEl) { navEl.classList.remove('open'); }
  }
  function go(hash) {
    var hit = pageFor(hash);
    var page = hit.page || pages[0];
    show(page.id);
    // A heading or a parameter row inside a page that was hidden a moment ago:
    // reveal the page first, then scroll, or the browser measures nothing.
    if (hit.target) { hit.target.scrollIntoView(); } else { window.scrollTo(0, 0); }
  }

  // The browser sets the hash for us; we only react. Nav links, prev/next,
  // search hits and cross-references inside prose therefore all take one path.
  window.addEventListener('hashchange', function () { go(location.hash.slice(1)); });

  // ---- sidebar search ------------------------------------------------------
  // No index: the document is the index. Sidebar entries filter by label, and a
  // typed query also lists every matching heading and parameter across pages.
  var HIT_LIMIT = 14;
  function labelOfPage(page) {
    if (!page) { return ''; }
    var a = null;
    navLinks.forEach(function (x) {
      if (x.getAttribute('data-page') === page.id) { a = x; }
    });
    return a ? a.textContent : page.id;
  }
  function clearHits() {
    while (hits.firstChild) { hits.removeChild(hits.firstChild); }
  }
  function search() {
    var text = (queryBox.value || '').trim().toLowerCase();
    clearHits();
    if (!text) {
      hits.hidden = true;
      navLinks.forEach(function (a) { a.classList.remove('off'); });
      list('.navsec', tree).forEach(function (s) { s.classList.remove('off'); });
      return;
    }
    navLinks.forEach(function (a) {
      a.classList.toggle('off', a.textContent.toLowerCase().indexOf(text) < 0);
    });
    // A section with nothing left showing goes too — including the empty ones,
    // whose "coming soon" is an answer to nobody's query.
    list('.navsec', tree).forEach(function (s) {
      s.classList.toggle('off', !list('a[data-page]', s).some(function (a) {
        return !a.classList.contains('off');
      }));
    });
    var n = 0;
    list('.page h3, .page h4, .page [data-param]').forEach(function (el) {
      if (n >= HIT_LIMIT) { return; }
      var name = el.getAttribute('data-param') || el.textContent;
      if (name.toLowerCase().indexOf(text) < 0) { return; }
      var page = el.closest ? el.closest('.page') : null;
      var id = el.id || (page ? page.id : '');
      if (!id) { return; }
      n++;
      var a = document.createElement('a');
      a.className = 'hit';
      a.setAttribute('href', '#' + id);
      a.textContent = name;
      var where = document.createElement('span');
      where.className = 'hit-x';
      where.textContent = labelOfPage(page);
      a.appendChild(where);
      hits.appendChild(a);
    });
    if (!n) {
      var none = document.createElement('div');
      none.className = 'nohits';
      none.textContent = 'No matches';
      hits.appendChild(none);
    }
    hits.hidden = false;
  }
  if (queryBox && hits && tree) {
    queryBox.addEventListener('input', search);
    queryBox.addEventListener('search', search);
  }

  // ---- one click handler for the whole document ----------------------------
  document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var t = e.target;
    if (!t || !t.classList) { return; }

    if (t.classList.contains('themebtn')) {
      var mode = t.getAttribute('data-theme-set');
      applyTheme(mode);
      writeStore(THEME_KEY, mode);
      return;
    }
    if (t.classList.contains('tab')) {
      var box = t.closest ? t.closest('.tabs') : null;
      var label = t.getAttribute('data-tab');
      if (box && applyTab(box, label)) { writeStore(TAB_KEY, label); }
      return;
    }
    if (t.classList.contains('copy')) { copyFrom(t); return; }
    if (t.id === 'navtoggle') {
      e.stopPropagation();
      if (navEl) {
        var open = navEl.classList.toggle('open');
        t.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
      }
      return;
    }
    // Clicking the page you are already on fires no hashchange; close the
    // drawer anyway so the tap is not a no-op.
    var link = t.closest ? t.closest('a[href^="#"]') : null;
    if (link && navEl) { navEl.classList.remove('open'); }
  });

  // ---- copy buttons: clipboard where available, a textarea where not -------
  function copyFrom(btn) {
    var box = btn.closest ? btn.closest('.snip, .termbox') : null;
    if (!box) { return; }
    var node = box.querySelector('pre.cmd code') || box.querySelector('pre.term');
    if (!node) { return; }
    var text = node.textContent;
    function done() {
      btn.textContent = 'Copied';
      btn.classList.add('ok');
      setTimeout(function () {
        btn.textContent = 'Copy';
        btn.classList.remove('ok');
      }, 1200);
    }
    function fallback() {
      try {
        var ta = document.createElement('textarea');
        ta.value = text;
        ta.setAttribute('readonly', '');
        ta.style.position = 'fixed';
        ta.style.top = '-1000px';
        document.body.appendChild(ta);
        ta.select();
        document.execCommand('copy');
        document.body.removeChild(ta);
        done();
      } catch (err) { /* nothing left to try; the text is on screen */ }
    }
    if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(done, fallback);
    } else {
      fallback();
    }
  }

  go(location.hash.slice(1) || pages[0].id);
}());
</script>
</body>
</html>
